(6, 'Introduction to Computer Hardware Servicing', '<div>The foundation of Computer Hardware Servicing and its importance to the modern professional operations and general uses of computers.</div><p><br></p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p><strong>Learning Objectives:</strong></p><p>This lesson aims to:</p><ol style=\"list-style-type: decimal;\"><li>define Computer Hardware Servicing (CHS);</li><li>establish the importance of CHS; and</li><li>discuss components of CHS and recent trends.</li></ol>', 1, '', 1, 0, 'English', 0, '2026-03-08 22:30:57', '2026-06-29 07:54:45', '[{\"id\":1776121484117,\"file\":null,\"type\":\"topic\",\"order\":1,\"title\":\"Topic 1: What is Computer Hardware Servicing?\",\"caption\":\"\",\"content\":\"\",\"fileName\":null},{\"id\":1781590752877,\"file\":null,\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"order\":2,\"title\":\"\",\"caption\":\"\",\"content\":\"<div><div><div><div>Troubleshooting is a systematic process of identifying, analyzing, and resolving computer problems by observing symptoms, isolating causes, and applying solutions to</div><div><br></div></div></div><blockquote><div><div><div>restore normal operation.[1] It is essential in Computer Hardware Servicing because it allows technicians to efficiently diagnose and fix performance issues before they escalate into hardware damage, data loss, or system failure.[2] In this lesson, we will cover common hardware and software—their indicators, causes, and troubleshooting procedures—building on the CHS fundamentals you&#39;ve already learned in previous lessons.</div></div></div></blockquote></div>\",\"fileName\":null,\"tableData\":null,\"tableTitle\":\"\",\"contentLayout\":\"text\"},{\"id\":1776121484120,\"file\":null,\"type\":\"review-multiple-choice\",\"order\":3,\"title\":\"\",\"caption\":\"\",\"content\":\"\",\"fileName\":null,\"questions\":[{\"id\":1776121484119,\"type\":\"Easy\",\"skill\":\"Critical Thinking\",\"options\":[\"Repairing\",\"Maintenance\",\"Coding Games\",\"Installing computer hardware components\"],\"question\":\"From the choices below, which does not belong to the workflow of Computer Hardware Servicing?\",\"questionType\":\"Easy\",\"correctAnswer\":2}]},{\"id\":1776121484121,\"file\":null,\"type\":\"topic\",\"order\":4,\"title\":\"Topic 2: Importance of Computer Hardware Servicing\",\"caption\":\"\",\"content\":\"\",\"fileName\":null},{\"id\":1776121484122,\"file\":null,\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"order\":5,\"title\":\"\",\"caption\":\"\",\"content\":\"<div><p>    CHS encompasses basic troubleshooting skills, performing complex repairs, and understanding the types, functions, and specifications of various hardware components<b><sup>[3]</sup></b>. But why does having skills related to CHS relevant today? As discussed previously, computers had become crucial to every day activities and operations in various professional fields. Over time, its hardware components degrade or get damaged due to numerous reasons, all of which will be further discussed along your learning path. Professionals trained to perform CHS responsibilities address these concerns to ensure the optimal operation of the computers they are handling. The following points highlight the importance of CHS: </p><ul style=\\\"list-style-type: disc\\\"><li><ul style=\\\"list-style-type: none\\\"><li style=\\\"list-style-type: none\\\"><b>Performance</b>&nbsp;- Upgrading and tuning hardware components and systems make computer performance optimal, making the experience better for the users. Mitigating performance degrading issues, like overheating caused by dust buildup, is one of the major importance of CHS.<b><sup>[3][4]</sup></b></li><li style=\\\"list-style-type: none\\\"><b>Cost Efficiency</b>&nbsp;- Maintenance and regular checks help by being proactive with addressing minor issues, which can prevent further escalation to major issues that may require expensive resolutions.<b><sup>[4]</sup></b>&nbsp;&nbsp;</li><li style=\\\"list-style-type: none\\\"><b>Data Protection</b>&nbsp;- System downs and failures may lead to the loss of important data stored in computers. Identifying risks of such scenarios can minimize potential damages to data beforehand.<b><sup>[3][4]</sup></b></li><li style=\\\"list-style-type: none\\\"><b>Longevity</b>&nbsp;- Habitual actions to maintaining computer hardware components extends its lifespan, as expensive costs and frequent reconfiguration may be experienced if neglected.<b><sup>[3][4]</sup></b></li><li style=\\\"list-style-type: none\\\"><b>Safety</b>&nbsp;- Faulty components may trigger safety hazards, such as electrical fires due and overheating; Possessing CHS related skills helps identify possible risks and design correct course of action to prevent safety risks.<b><sup>[3]</sup></b></li></ul></li></ul></div>\",\"fileName\":null,\"tableData\":null,\"tableTitle\":\"\",\"contentLayout\":\"text\"},{\"id\":1776121484126,\"file\":null,\"type\":\"review-multiple-choice\",\"order\":6,\"title\":\"\",\"caption\":\"\",\"content\":\"\",\"fileName\":null,\"questions\":[{\"id\":1776121484123,\"type\":\"Easy\",\"skill\":\"Analytical Thinking\",\"options\":[\"Its performance improves\",\"Hardware components require duplicates\",\"It degrades and may have damages due to various factors\",\"Hardware components stops working completely at any moment\"],\"question\":\"What is expected from computer hardware components as time goes by?\",\"questionType\":\"Easy\",\"correctAnswer\":2},{\"id\":1776121484124,\"type\":\"Easy\",\"skill\":\"Memorization\",\"options\":[\"Cost Efficiency\",\"Longevity\",\"Data Protection\",\"Performance\"],\"question\":\"Which importance of CHS highlights the potential to minimize the need for expensive resolutions?\",\"questionType\":\"Easy\",\"correctAnswer\":0},{\"id\":1776121484125,\"type\":\"Easy\",\"skill\":\"Technical Comprehension\",\"options\":[\"Performance\",\"Longevity\",\"Cost Efficiency\",\"Safety\"],\"question\":\"Which of the following descriptions highlights the importance of CHS as it prevents computers and its parts to be replaced as long as possible?\",\"questionType\":\"Easy\",\"correctAnswer\":1}]},{\"id\":1776121484127,\"file\":null,\"type\":\"topic\",\"order\":7,\"title\":\"Topic 3: Trends Surrounding Computer Hardware Servicing\",\"caption\":\"\",\"content\":\"\",\"fileName\":null},{\"id\":1776121484142,\"file\":null,\"type\":\"video\",\"order\":8,\"title\":\"\",\"caption\":\"Lesson 1 Topic 3 Video\",\"content\":\"https://www.dropbox.com/scl/fi/3udi818zpelteunz5sdd3/Lesson-1-Topic-3.mp4?rlkey=3i0o5vb25iu1kk0hhgkie8qr8&st=bsbqs7th&dl=0\",\"fileName\":null},{\"id\":1776121484128,\"file\":null,\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"order\":9,\"title\":\"\",\"caption\":\"\",\"content\":\"<div><p>    Everyday, devices are getting designed to be more complex. To not be left behind, developing skills related to these advancements in technologies is necessary. It is important to recognize several trends that are influencing the field of computer hardware servicing so that knowledge about sustaining further advancements of technology can keep up.</p><ol style=\\\"list-style-type: decimal\\\"><ol style=\\\"list-style-type: decimal\\\"><li><b>Artificial Intelligence (AI) </b>- Computer systems are now being made for automation using various technologies under the umbrella of AI.<b><sup>[5]</sup></b> Not only does CHS help with AI from the perspective of maintaining efficient hardware performance, the technology itself also offers aid in CHS-related tasks, such as automating diagnostic checks or predictive maintenance, alerting technicians to potential issues before they become critical, and general digital tools that make tasks easier and faster.<b><sup>[3]</sup></b> Alongside these progress in technology, the need for skilled technicians to maintain AI-driven systems is much more prevalent. </li><li><b>The Internet of Things (IoT)</b> - More often than not, most devices of this age have capability of interconnection through a network, such as smart home devices, mobile devices, and wearables.<b><sup>[3]</sup></b> To put it simply, physical objects, typically found within our homes, are now functional due to being embedded with sensors, software, and other technologies, with the intent of interconnection and data exchange to other devices connected to the internet. CHS may expand to cater to these devices, and further understanding of computer networks will be needed. </li></ol><li><b>Remote Servicing</b> - A tangent to CHS trends involving networking and internet would be the ability for remote servicing. Online platforms allow the conveyance of support, maintenance, and consulting services, allowing technicians to troubleshoot while not present on-site.<b><sup>[3][7]</sup></b> This is particularly useful for businesses that depend on minimizing downtime. </li><li><b>Virtual Reality (VR) and Augmented Reality (AR) </b>- CHS may encounter new and intricate systems with the rise of technologies that utilize VR and AR. VR devices use technology to create a simulated environment to perceive as reality while AR devices involve the use of technology that enhances an experience by overlaying digital information on the real world<b><sup>[8]</sup></b>, both of which often integrate hardware components and software configurations.<b><sup>[3]</sup></b></li><li><b>Sustainability Concerns - </b>Environmental awareness is not a new topic anymore, and certain workflows adapt to responsible consumption and sustainable practices. In CHS, several implementations, such as recycling old components, utilizing energy-efficient hardware, and minimizing e-waste, are observed as an integral part of the work and training.<b><sup>[3][4]</sup></b> Further lessons, specially tackling assembly, repair, and maintenance of computer and its components incorporates sustainable practices that one must observe while training.<br></li></ol></div>\",\"fileName\":null,\"tableData\":null,\"tableTitle\":\"\",\"contentLayout\":\"text\"},{\"id\":1776121484131,\"file\":null,\"type\":\"review-multiple-choice\",\"order\":10,\"title\":\"\",\"caption\":\"\",\"content\":\"\",\"fileName\":null,\"questions\":[{\"id\":1776121484129,\"type\":\"Easy\",\"skill\":\"Memorization\",\"options\":[\"Remote Servicing\",\"Virtual Reality (VR) and Augmented Reality (AR)\",\"Internet of Things (IoT)\",\"Artificial Intelligence (AI)\"],\"question\":\"Which trend of CHS pertains to the ability to provide diagnosis, advice, and troubleshooting while not present on-site?\",\"questionType\":\"Easy\",\"correctAnswer\":0},{\"id\":1776121484130,\"type\":\"Easy\",\"skill\":\"Technical Comprehension\",\"options\":[\"Sustainability Concerns\",\"Remote Servicing\",\"Virtual Reality (VR) and Augmented Reality (AR)\",\"Artificial Intelligence (AI)\"],\"question\":\"Which trend of CHS introduces computer systems that are able to operate without human presence?\",\"questionType\":\"Easy\",\"correctAnswer\":3}]},{\"id\":1776121484132,\"file\":null,\"type\":\"topic\",\"order\":11,\"title\":\"Topic 4: Components of Computer Hardware Servicing\",\"caption\":\"\",\"content\":\"\",\"fileName\":null},{\"id\":1776121484133,\"file\":null,\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"order\":12,\"title\":\"\",\"caption\":\"\",\"content\":\"<div><p>    You are just about another step to start with your Computer Hardware Servicing Training! While you are breaking down and absorbing what you’ve learned so far about CHS, we will also give you an overview of the components of your training in ModuLearn. We will tackle <b>basic Computer Hardware Operations</b>, <b>assembly and disassembly</b>, <b>troubleshooting and maintenance of </b>computer hardware.</p><p>    <b>Computer hardware </b>the physical parts of a computer that you can see and touch are referred to as computer hardware. These components work together to process input and deliver output based on user instructions.</p><p>Computer hardware has <b>four main basic operations</b> namely: input, processing, storage and output.</p><b>Inputting Data - </b>Inputting data is a computer&#39;s first basic operation. The process of giving data or information to a computer is known as input operations. A keyboard, mouse, microphone, camera, and other input devices can all be used to enter data into a computer. The process of feeding information into a computer, where it is processed and transformed into a format that it can understand, is known as data input.<br><b>Processing Data </b>- After the data is inputted, the computer processes the data. In order to get the outcome you want, data processing involves adjusting and converting the incoming data. The manipulation of input data by a computer to generate meaningful information is referred to as processing operations. The central processing unit (CPU), the computer&#39;s brain and will be discussed later, is responsible for carrying out these functions.<br><b>Storing Data </b>- Storing data is the process of storing processed data on a hard drive, solid-state drive, or flash drive. Even when the computer is shut down, the data is kept on the storage device so it can be used later. Storing information and data in memory or on secondary storage devices such as cloud storage (saving files and data on the internet instead of a hard drive.), hard disks, flash drives, CDs, and DVDs is also possible.<br><b>Output/Outputting Data</b> - Output operations refer to the presentation of processed data in a useful form. Outputting data is the process of presenting the processed data to the user in a readable form. Output devices such as a monitor, printer, or speaker are used to display or play the processed data. <p>    <b>Computer assembly</b> is the process of fitting all the internal parts needed for the computer system to enable it to work. There is a proper sequence of attachment of each and every component into the computer system. To provide you with an insight, assembling a computer typically follows the following sequence:</p><ol style=\\\"list-style-type: decimal\\\"><li>Open the case.</li><li>Install the power supply.</li><li>Attach the components to the motherboard.</li><li>Install the motherboard.</li><li>Install internal drives.</li><li>Connect all internal cables.</li><li>Install motherboard power connections</li><li>Connect external cables to the computer.</li><li>Boot the computer for the first time.  <br><br><br></li></ol></div>\",\"fileName\":null,\"tableData\":null,\"tableTitle\":\"\",\"contentLayout\":\"text\"},{\"id\":1776121484134,\"file\":null,\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"order\":13,\"title\":\"\",\"caption\":\"\",\"content\":\"<p><strong>Computer disassembly</strong>, on the other hand, is the process of breaking down a device into separate parts. Disassembly of any device is required to determine a problem, to replace a part, or take the parts and use them in another device. Just like in computer assembly, there is a standard process of computer disassembly like listed in the following:</p><ol style=\\\"list-style-type: decimal;\\\"><li>Unplugging.</li><li>Open the case.</li><li>Disconnect all the connectors.</li><li>Remove the fan.</li><li>Remove the power supply.</li><li>Removing HDD and optical drive.</li><li>Removing RAM (random access memory) modules.</li><li>Remove expansion cards.</li><li>Remove the motherboard.</li><li>Reassembling of components.</li></ol>\",\"fileName\":null,\"tableData\":null,\"tableTitle\":\"\",\"contentLayout\":\"text\"},{\"id\":1776121484135,\"file\":null,\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"order\":14,\"title\":\"\",\"caption\":\"\",\"content\":\"<div><div><p><b>Troubleshooting </b>involves identifying, diagnosing, and fixing issues related to the physical components of a computer. Knowing how to troubleshoot these components can save you time, money, and a lot of frustration.</p><p>In this training, we will follow the following troubleshooting steps as a foundation to developing proper troubleshooting and diagnosis:</p><ol style=\\\"list-style-type: decimal\\\"><li><b>Identify the problem</b> - Begin by understanding the symptoms. Is the computer completely dead, or is it just a specific component that’s malfunctioning?</li><li><b>Gather information </b>- Research the symptoms. Use forums, manufacturer websites, and tech support resources. Sometimes, a quick search can lead you to a solution.</li><li><b>Test hypothesis</b> - Based on your research, start testing potential solutions. For example, if the computer won’t turn on, test the power supply first.</li><li><b>Implement solutions</b> - Once you identify the probable cause, implement the solution. Like replacing faulty components, updating drivers, or cleaning out dust.</li><li><b>Verify fix</b> - After implementing a fix, verify that the problem is resolved. For example, restart the computer and check if it operates normally.</li></ol></div><div><p>    <b>Troubleshooting </b>involves identifying, diagnosing, and fixing issues related to the physical components of a computer. Knowing how to troubleshoot these components can save you time, money, and a lot of frustration.</p><p>In this training, we will follow the following troubleshooting steps as a foundation to developing proper troubleshooting and diagnosis:</p><ol style=\\\"list-style-type: decimal\\\"><li><b>Identify the problem</b> - Begin by understanding the symptoms. Is the computer completely dead, or is it just a specific component that’s malfunctioning?</li><li><b>Gather information </b>- Research the symptoms. Use forums, manufacturer websites, and tech support resources. Sometimes, a quick search can lead you to a solution.</li><li><b>Test hypothesis</b> - Based on your research, start testing potential solutions. For example, if the computer won’t turn on, test the power supply first.</li><li><b>Implement solutions</b> - Once you identify the probable cause, implement the solution. Like replacing faulty components, updating drivers, or cleaning out dust.</li><li><b>Verify fix</b> - After implementing a fix, verify that the problem is resolved. For example, restart the computer and check if it operates normally.<br></li></ol></div></div>\",\"fileName\":null,\"tableData\":null,\"tableTitle\":\"\",\"contentLayout\":\"text\"},{\"id\":1776121484136,\"file\":null,\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"order\":15,\"title\":\"\",\"caption\":\"\",\"content\":\"<div><div><p>    All of the tasks necessary to keep your computer operating effectively and consistently are included in computer maintenance. It covers both software and hardware maintenance procedures that help protect your device from potential threats, enhance performance, and prevent system problems. Your computer&#39;s lifespan can be increased by many years and its best performance can be maintained with routine maintenance.</p><p>Preventing problems before they exist is just as important as correcting them when they do occur. Consider it similar to car maintenance: routine tune-ups and oil changes avoid serious malfunctions and expensive repairs. Computer maintenance helps it to have the following:</p><ol style=\\\"list-style-type: decimal\\\"><li><b>Extended device lifespan</b> - proper maintenance can add years to your computer’s life</li><li><b>Improved system performance -</b> regular cleanup keeps your PC running faster</li><li><b>Enhanced data security</b> - updated software protects against threats</li><li><b>Reduced repair costs </b>- preventing problems is cheaper than fixing them</li><li><b>Better user experience</b> - a well-maintained computer is more reliable and responsive</li></ol></div></div>\",\"fileName\":null,\"tableData\":null,\"tableTitle\":\"\",\"contentLayout\":\"text\"},{\"id\":1776121484137,\"file\":null,\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"order\":16,\"title\":\"\",\"caption\":\"\",\"content\":\"<div><div><p>    <b>You are now at the end of lesson 1. Good job on finishing the first lesson. Next step is the final assessment for the whole lesson. You can take it any time. If you wish to review or re-read the lesson, feel free to do so! Just remember, you cannot retake the final assessment, and you cannot pause while answering. An honest take is our priority, and we discourage you to take any kinds of cheating.</b></p></div><div><p>    <b>You are now at the end of lesson 1. Good job on finishing the first lesson. Next step is the final assessment for the whole lesson. You can take it any time. If you wish to review or re-read the lesson, feel free to do so! Just remember, you cannot retake the final assessment, and you cannot pause while answering. An honest take is our priority, and we discourage you to take any kinds of cheating.</b></p></div></div>\",\"fileName\":null,\"tableData\":null,\"tableTitle\":\"\",\"contentLayout\":\"text\"},{\"id\":1776121484141,\"file\":null,\"type\":\"review-multiple-choice\",\"order\":17,\"title\":\"\",\"caption\":\"\",\"content\":\"\",\"fileName\":null,\"questions\":[{\"id\":1776121484138,\"type\":\"Easy\",\"skill\":\"Analytical Thinking\",\"options\":[\"Inputting Data\",\"Input Operations\",\"Outputting Data\",\"Output Operations\"],\"question\":\"What basic computer hardware operation is the procedure for providing the user with the processed data in a clear format?\",\"questionType\":\"Easy\",\"correctAnswer\":3},{\"id\":1776121484139,\"type\":\"Easy\",\"skill\":\"Problem Solving\",\"options\":[\"time and expensive costs\",\"effort and expensive costs\",\"knowledge and effort\",\"time and knowledge\"],\"question\":\"Knowing how troubleshooting and maintenance of computers saves you ____?\",\"questionType\":\"Easy\",\"correctAnswer\":0},{\"id\":1776121484140,\"type\":\"Easy\",\"skill\":\"Critical Thinking\",\"options\":[\"slow download speed\",\"slow computer response\",\"threats\",\"computer getting dirty\"],\"question\":\"By maintaining data security, your computer gets protected from?\",\"questionType\":\"Easy\",\"correctAnswer\":2}]},{\"id\":\"references-1782690885715\",\"type\":\"references\",\"order\":18,\"title\":\"\",\"caption\":\"\",\"content\":\"https://medium.com/@zargull/the-importance-of-computers-in-the-modern-world-cf80eb3ecf0c\\nhttps://ticktocktech.com/blog/2022/08/28/what-is-computer-hardware-servicing-and-how-is-it-done-in-2022/\\nhttps://umatechnology.org/what-is-computer-hardware-servicing/\\nhttps://mefmobile.org/what-is-computer-hardware-servicing/\\nhttps://www.coursera.org/articles/what-is-artificial-intelligence?msockid=133d0c738b796b820b6e1a398a6d6a23\\nhttps://www.oracle.com/asean/internet-of-things/\\nhttps://www.teamviewer.com/apac/insights/remote-servicing-in-modern-business-operations/\\nhttps://www.geeksforgeeks.org/python/virtual-reality-vs-augmented-reality-whats-the-difference/\\nhttps://ticktocktech.com/blog/2022/08/28/what-is-computer-hardware-servicing-and-how-is-it-done-in-2022/#google_vignette\\nhttps://www.geeksforgeeks.org/computer-science-fundamentals/computer-hardware/\\nhttps://rpatoolstutorial.com/basic-operations-of-computer/\\nhttps://ncert.nic.in/vocational/pdf/keit104.pdf\\nhttps://www.techallabout.com/computer-hardware-troubleshooting-a-comprehensive-guide/\\nhttps://www.hp.com/us-en/shop/tech-takes/pc-maintenance-and-repair-tips?pStoreID=techsoup%27%5B0%5D&msockid=377c7f12845d6e621d65697d85d56f25\"}]', '[{\"id\":1776121484119,\"type\":\"Easy\",\"skill\":\"Critical Thinking\",\"options\":[\"Repairing\",\"Maintenance\",\"Coding Games\",\"Installing computer hardware components\"],\"question\":\"From the choices below, which does not belong to the workflow of Computer Hardware Servicing?\",\"questionType\":\"Easy\",\"correctAnswer\":2},{\"id\":1776121484123,\"type\":\"Easy\",\"skill\":\"Analytical Thinking\",\"options\":[\"Its performance improves\",\"Hardware components require duplicates\",\"It degrades and may have damages due to various factors\",\"Hardware components stops working completely at any moment\"],\"question\":\"What is expected from computer hardware components as time goes by?\",\"questionType\":\"Easy\",\"correctAnswer\":2},{\"id\":1776121484124,\"type\":\"Easy\",\"skill\":\"Memorization\",\"options\":[\"Cost Efficiency\",\"Longevity\",\"Data Protection\",\"Performance\"],\"question\":\"Which importance of CHS highlights the potential to minimize the need for expensive resolutions?\",\"questionType\":\"Easy\",\"correctAnswer\":0},{\"id\":1776121484125,\"type\":\"Easy\",\"skill\":\"Technical Comprehension\",\"options\":[\"Performance\",\"Longevity\",\"Cost Efficiency\",\"Safety\"],\"question\":\"Which of the following descriptions highlights the importance of CHS as it prevents computers and its parts to be replaced as long as possible?\",\"questionType\":\"Easy\",\"correctAnswer\":1},{\"id\":1776121484129,\"type\":\"Easy\",\"skill\":\"Memorization\",\"options\":[\"Remote Servicing\",\"Virtual Reality (VR) and Augmented Reality (AR)\",\"Internet of Things (IoT)\",\"Artificial Intelligence (AI)\"],\"question\":\"Which trend of CHS pertains to the ability to provide diagnosis, advice, and troubleshooting while not present on-site?\",\"questionType\":\"Easy\",\"correctAnswer\":0}]', '[{\"id\":1776121484168,\"type\":\"Easy\",\"skill\":\"Critical Thinking\",\"options\":[\"Repairing\",\"Maintenance\",\"Coding Games\",\"Installing computer hardware components\"],\"question\":\"From the choices below, which does not belong to the workflow of Computer Hardware Servicing?\",\"questionType\":\"Easy\",\"correctAnswer\":2},{\"id\":1776121484169,\"type\":\"Easy\",\"skill\":\"Analytical Thinking\",\"options\":[\"Its performance improves\",\"Hardware components require duplicates\",\"It degrades and may have damages due to various factors\",\"Hardware components stops working completely at any moment\"],\"question\":\"What is expected from computer hardware components as time goes by?\",\"questionType\":\"Easy\",\"correctAnswer\":2},{\"id\":1776121484170,\"type\":\"Easy\",\"skill\":\"Memorization\",\"options\":[\"Cost Efficiency\",\"Longevity\",\"Data Protection\",\"Performance\"],\"question\":\"Which importance of CHS highlights the potential to minimize the need for expensive resolutions?\",\"questionType\":\"Easy\",\"correctAnswer\":0},{\"id\":1776121484171,\"type\":\"Easy\",\"skill\":\"Technical Comprehension\",\"options\":[\"Performance\",\"Longevity\",\"Cost Efficiency\",\"Safety\"],\"question\":\"Which of the following descriptions highlights the importance of CHS as it prevents computers and its parts to be replaced as long as possible?\",\"questionType\":\"Easy\",\"correctAnswer\":1},{\"id\":1776121484172,\"type\":\"Easy\",\"skill\":\"Memorization\",\"options\":[\"Remote Servicing\",\"Virtual Reality (VR) and Augmented Reality (AR)\",\"Internet of Things (IoT)\",\"Artificial Intelligence (AI)\"],\"question\":\"Which trend of CHS pertains to the ability to provide diagnosis, advice, and troubleshooting while not present on-site?\",\"questionType\":\"Easy\",\"correctAnswer\":0},{\"id\":1776121484173,\"type\":\"Easy\",\"skill\":\"Technical Comprehension\",\"options\":[\"Sustainability Concerns\",\"Remote Servicing\",\"Virtual Reality (VR) and Augmented Reality (AR)\",\"Artificial Intelligence (AI)\"],\"question\":\"Which trend of CHS introduces computer systems that are able to operate without human presence?\",\"questionType\":\"Easy\",\"correctAnswer\":3},{\"id\":1776121484174,\"type\":\"Easy\",\"skill\":\"Analytical Thinking\",\"options\":[\"Inputting Data\",\"Input Operations\",\"Outputting Data\",\"Output Operations\"],\"question\":\"What basic computer hardware operation is the procedure for providing the user with the processed data in a clear format?\",\"questionType\":\"Easy\",\"correctAnswer\":3},{\"id\":1776121484175,\"type\":\"Easy\",\"skill\":\"Problem Solving\",\"options\":[\"time and expensive costs\",\"effort and expensive costs\",\"knowledge and effort\",\"time and knowledge\"],\"question\":\"Knowing how troubleshooting and maintenance of computers saves you ____?\",\"questionType\":\"Easy\",\"correctAnswer\":0},{\"id\":1776121484176,\"type\":\"Easy\",\"skill\":\"Critical Thinking\",\"options\":[\"slow download speed\",\"slow computer response\",\"threats\",\"computer getting dirty\"],\"question\":\"By maintaining data security, your computer gets protected from?\",\"questionType\":\"Easy\",\"correctAnswer\":2},{\"id\":1776121484177,\"type\":\"Easy\",\"skill\":\"Problem Solving\",\"options\":[\"Unplugging\",\"Reassemble of components\",\"Disconnect all the connectors\",\"Attach the components to the motherboard\"],\"question\":\"If computer assembly is the process of fitting all the internal parts needed, and computer disassembly is the process of breaking down a device into separate parts, which step indicates computer assembly?\",\"questionType\":\"Easy\",\"correctAnswer\":3}]', '[{\"id\":1776121484178,\"type\":\"Situational\",\"skill\":\"Analytical Thinking\",\"options\":[\"The process of creating software for computers\",\"The procedural workflow of installing, repairing, and maintaining hardware components\",\"The management of computer networks only\",\"The designing of new computer systems\"],\"question\":\"Question: A technician is assigned to install new RAM, repair a damaged hard drive, and regularly maintain computers in an office. Which description best represents the work being performed?\",\"questionType\":\"Situational\",\"correctAnswer\":1},{\"id\":1776121484179,\"type\":\"Situational\",\"skill\":\"Memorization\",\"options\":[\"Routine diagnosis and maintenance\",\"Immediate hardware replacement\",\"Installing new software\",\"Complete system disassembly\"],\"question\":\"Question: A user reports that their computer is running slower than usual. Which TWO CHS procedures would be MOST appropriate as initial steps?\",\"questionType\":\"Situational\",\"correctAnswer\":0},{\"id\":1776121484180,\"type\":\"Situational\",\"skill\":\"Problem Solving\",\"options\":[\"Attempt the repair anyway without tools\",\"Only perform maintenance and routine diagnosis, consulting an expert for internal issues\",\"Refuse to help completely\",\"Purchase all professional tools immediately\"],\"question\":\"Question: You\'ve been asked to help maintain computers in a small office, but you lack proper tools for internal hardware checks. According to the lesson, what should you do?\",\"questionType\":\"Situational\",\"correctAnswer\":1},{\"id\":1776121484181,\"type\":\"Situational\",\"skill\":\"Technical Comprehension\",\"options\":[\"Performance\",\"Cost Efficiency\",\"Data Protection\",\"Longevity\"],\"question\":\"Question: A company\'s server unexpectedly shuts down, and important client data becomes inaccessible. Which importance of CHS was MOST likely neglected?\",\"questionType\":\"Situational\",\"correctAnswer\":2},{\"id\":1776121484182,\"type\":\"Situational\",\"skill\":\"Problem Solving\",\"options\":[\"Safety and Performance\",\"Cost Efficiency and Data Protection\",\"Longevity and Safety\",\"Performance and Longevity\"],\"question\":\"Question: A computer technician notices a burning smell coming from a desktop computer and identifies a faulty power supply. Which TWO importances of CHS are being addressed by replacing this component?\",\"questionType\":\"Situational\",\"correctAnswer\":0},{\"id\":1776121484183,\"type\":\"Situational\",\"skill\":\"Technical Comprehension\",\"options\":[\"Artificial Intelligence – because devices make automated decisions\",\"Internet of Things – because physical objects are interconnected through networks\",\"Remote Servicing – because devices can be controlled remotely\",\"Augmented Reality – because devices enhance user experience\"],\"question\":\"Question: A technician is working with smart home devices that communicate with each other through a network. The devices include sensors, embedded software, and exchange data over the internet. Which trend does this PRIMARILY represent?\",\"questionType\":\"Situational\",\"correctAnswer\":1},{\"id\":1776121484184,\"type\":\"Situational\",\"skill\":\"Memorization\",\"options\":[\"Artificial Intelligence\",\"Sustainability Concerns\",\"Internet of Things\",\"Remote Servicing\"],\"question\":\"Question: A CHS training program emphasizes recycling old components, using energy-efficient hardware, and minimizing e-waste. Which trend is being implemented?\",\"questionType\":\"Situational\",\"correctAnswer\":1},{\"id\":1776121484185,\"type\":\"Situational\",\"skill\":\"Technical Comprehension\",\"options\":[\"Inputting Data\",\"Processing Data\",\"Storing Data\",\"Outputting Data\"],\"question\":\"Question: When a computer performs calculations, executes program instructions, and processes commands from software, which hardware operation is taking place?\",\"questionType\":\"Situational\",\"correctAnswer\":1},{\"id\":1776121484186,\"type\":\"Situational\",\"skill\":\"Problem Solving\",\"options\":[\"Implement solutions\",\"Identify the problem\",\"Test hypothesis\",\"Gather information\"],\"question\":\"Question: A technician begins troubleshooting by collecting system symptoms, user reports, and device behavior before forming possible solutions. Which troubleshooting step is being performed?\",\"questionType\":\"Situational\",\"correctAnswer\":3},{\"id\":1776121484187,\"type\":\"Situational\",\"skill\":\"Analytical Thinking\",\"options\":[\"Clicking a mouse to open a folder\",\"Taking a photo with a webcam, editing it, saving it to a flash drive, and printing it\",\"Listening to music stored on a hard drive\",\"Typing text into a word processor without saving\"],\"question\":\"Question: Which of the following scenarios demonstrates ALL FOUR basic computer hardware operations?\",\"questionType\":\"Situational\",\"correctAnswer\":1},{\"id\":1776121484188,\"type\":\"Situational\",\"skill\":\"Critical Thinking\",\"options\":[\"Motherboard\",\"Power supply\",\"Internal drives\",\"RAM modules\"],\"question\":\"Question: While assembling a desktop computer, a technician prepares the case and begins installing internal components. According to the correct assembly sequence, which component should be installed first?\",\"questionType\":\"Situational\",\"correctAnswer\":1},{\"id\":1776121484189,\"type\":\"Situational\",\"skill\":\"Critical Thinking\",\"options\":[\"Regular maintenance, upgrading components when needed, and recycling old parts\",\"Replacing all computers every year with new energy-efficient models\",\"Only repairing systems after complete failure\",\"Using only remote servicing tools\"],\"question\":\"Question: A small business owner asks you to help extend the life of their office computers while keeping costs low and reducing environmental impact. Which CHS approach BEST satisfies these goals?\",\"questionType\":\"Situational\",\"correctAnswer\":0},{\"id\":1776121484190,\"type\":\"Situational\",\"skill\":\"Critical Thinking\",\"options\":[\"Continue with the assembly and install the power supply last\",\"Force the power supply into place around the motherboard\",\"Remove the motherboard and install the power supply in the correct sequence\",\"Leave the power supply out and use an external power source\"],\"question\":\"Question: During computer assembly, you\'ve installed the motherboard but forgot to install the power supply first. What is the BEST course of action?\",\"questionType\":\"Situational\",\"correctAnswer\":2},{\"id\":1776121484191,\"type\":\"Situational\",\"skill\":\"Memorization\",\"options\":[\"Artificial Intelligence (AI)\",\"Remote Servicing\",\"Sustainability Concerns\",\"Internet of Things (IoT)\"],\"question\":\"Question: A technician was asked to fix a device that seems to have a sensor, which the customer uses to connect other devices within their home through the internet. Which trend of CHS is being shown? Artificial Intelligence (AI) Remote Servicing Sustainability Concerns Internet of Things (IoT)\",\"questionType\":\"Situational\",\"correctAnswer\":3},{\"id\":1776121484192,\"type\":\"Situational\",\"skill\":\"Analytical Thinking\",\"options\":[\"maintaining computer hardware and performing routine diagnosis\",\"using tools to solder resistors to an electric circuit board of an appliance\",\"creating a code to make a game character to jump through a development software\",\"creating schematics for network architecture of a company\"],\"question\":\"Question: Claire found out that cleaning her friend’s computer system unit monthly helps lessen the frequency of which her friend would need to bring their computer to a technician to be fixed. Which procedure of CHS is being shown? maintaining computer hardware and performing routine diagnosis using tools to solder resistors to an electric circuit board of an appliance creating a code to make a game character to jump through a development software creating schematics for network architecture of a company\",\"questionType\":\"Situational\",\"correctAnswer\":2},{\"id\":1776121484208,\"type\":\"Situational\",\"skill\":\"Critical Thinking\",\"options\":[\"Repairing\",\"Maintenance\",\"Coding Games\",\"Installing computer hardware components\"],\"question\":\"Question: A senior student in the Computer Hardware Servicing (CHS) program is asked to help prepare activities for a laboratory session that focuses strictly on hardware servicing skills. The instructor reminds the student that the activities should involve tasks directly related to diagnosing, maintaining, or assembling computer components. Which of the following activities would be least appropriate to include in the laboratory session?\",\"questionType\":\"Situational\",\"correctAnswer\":2},{\"id\":1776121484209,\"type\":\"Situational\",\"skill\":\"Analytical Thinking\",\"options\":[\"Its performance improves\",\"Hardware components require duplicates\",\"It degrades and may have damages due to various factors\",\"Hardware components stops working completely at any moment\"],\"question\":\"Question: After several years of use, a technician notices that a computer’s components are not performing as efficiently as before due to dust buildup, heat exposure, and wear. What normally happens to hardware components over time?\",\"questionType\":\"Situational\",\"correctAnswer\":2},{\"id\":1776121484210,\"type\":\"Situational\",\"skill\":\"Memorization\",\"options\":[\"Cost Efficiency\",\"Longevity\",\"Data Protection\",\"Performance\"],\"question\":\"Question: A company regularly performs preventive maintenance on its computers so that small hardware problems can be fixed before they become major failures requiring costly replacements. Which importance of CHS does this situation demonstrate?\",\"questionType\":\"Situational\",\"correctAnswer\":0},{\"id\":1776121484211,\"type\":\"Situational\",\"skill\":\"Technical Comprehension\",\"options\":[\"Performance\",\"Longevity\",\"Cost Efficiency\",\"Safety\"],\"question\":\"Question: A technician regularly cleans internal components, checks cooling systems, and ensures that hardware parts function properly so the computers can be used for many more years without replacement. Which importance of CHS is being demonstrated?\",\"questionType\":\"Situational\",\"correctAnswer\":1},{\"id\":1776121484212,\"type\":\"Situational\",\"skill\":\"Memorization\",\"options\":[\"Remote Servicing\",\"Virtual Reality (VR) and Augmented Reality (AR)\",\"Internet of Things (IoT)\",\"Artificial Intelligence (AI)\"],\"question\":\"Question: A technician helps a user fix a computer problem by connecting through the internet, checking system settings, and guiding the user through troubleshooting steps without physically visiting the location. Which CHS trend does this represent?\",\"questionType\":\"Situational\",\"correctAnswer\":0},{\"id\":1776121484213,\"type\":\"Situational\",\"skill\":\"Technical Comprehension\",\"options\":[\"Sustainability Concerns\",\"Remote Servicing\",\"Virtual Reality (VR) and Augmented Reality (AR)\",\"Artificial Intelligence (AI)\"],\"question\":\"Question: A computer system automatically analyzes hardware conditions, predicts failures, and performs certain adjustments without requiring direct human intervention. Which CHS trend does this example represent?\",\"questionType\":\"Situational\",\"correctAnswer\":3},{\"id\":1776121484214,\"type\":\"Situational\",\"skill\":\"Analytical Thinking\",\"options\":[\"Inputting Data\",\"Input Operations\",\"Outputting Data\",\"Output Operations\"],\"question\":\"Question: After processing a user’s request, the computer displays the results on a monitor so the user can read and understand the information. Which hardware operation is being performed?\",\"questionType\":\"Situational\",\"correctAnswer\":3},{\"id\":1776121484215,\"type\":\"Situational\",\"skill\":\"Problem Solving\",\"options\":[\"time and expensive costs\",\"effort and expensive costs\",\"knowledge and effort\",\"time and knowledge\"],\"question\":\"Question: A user learns basic troubleshooting and maintenance skills so they can solve minor computer issues without calling a technician each time a problem occurs. What benefit does this provide?\",\"questionType\":\"Situational\",\"correctAnswer\":0},{\"id\":1776121484216,\"type\":\"Situational\",\"skill\":\"Critical Thinking\",\"options\":[\"slow download speed\",\"slow computer response\",\"threats\",\"computer getting dirty\"],\"question\":\"Question: A technician installs security updates, uses strong passwords, and ensures antivirus protection so that harmful activities cannot compromise the system or its stored information. What does maintaining data security primarily protect the computer from?\",\"questionType\":\"Situational\",\"correctAnswer\":2},{\"id\":1776121484217,\"type\":\"Situational\",\"skill\":\"Problem Solving\",\"options\":[\"Unplugging\",\"Reassemble of components\",\"Disconnect all the connectors\",\"Attach the components to the motherboard\"],\"question\":\"Question: During the building of a desktop computer, a technician carefully places and secures different hardware components into their proper locations on the motherboard so the system can function properly. Which step represents computer assembly?\",\"questionType\":\"Situational\",\"correctAnswer\":3},{\"id\":1776121484193,\"type\":\"Easy\",\"skill\":\"Analytical Thinking\",\"options\":[\"The process of creating software for computers\",\"The procedural workflow of installing, repairing, and maintaining hardware components\",\"The management of computer networks only\",\"The designing of new computer systems\"],\"question\":\"Computer Hardware Servicing (CHS) is best defined as?\",\"questionType\":\"Easy\",\"correctAnswer\":1},{\"id\":1776121484194,\"type\":\"Easy\",\"skill\":\"Memorization\",\"options\":[\"Routine diagnosis and maintenance\",\"Immediate hardware replacement\",\"Installing new software\",\"Complete system disassembly\"],\"question\":\"Which TWO activities are considered appropriate initial procedures in Computer Hardware Servicing when diagnosing a slow computer?\",\"questionType\":\"Easy\",\"correctAnswer\":0},{\"id\":1776121484195,\"type\":\"Easy\",\"skill\":\"Problem Solving\",\"options\":[\"Attempt the repair anyway without tools\",\"Only perform maintenance and routine diagnosis, consulting an expert for internal issues\",\"Refuse to help completely\",\"Purchase all professional tools immediately\"],\"question\":\"What is the most appropriate action if a technician lacks proper tools for internal hardware checks?\",\"questionType\":\"Easy\",\"correctAnswer\":1},{\"id\":1776121484196,\"type\":\"Easy\",\"skill\":\"Technical Comprehension\",\"options\":[\"Performance\",\"Cost Efficiency\",\"Data Protection\",\"Longevity\"],\"question\":\"Which importance of Computer Hardware Servicing focuses on protecting files and digital information from loss?\",\"questionType\":\"Easy\",\"correctAnswer\":2},{\"id\":1776121484197,\"type\":\"Easy\",\"skill\":\"Problem Solving\",\"options\":[\"Safety and Performance\",\"Cost Efficiency and Data Protection\",\"Longevity and Safety\",\"Performance and Longevity\"],\"question\":\"Replacing faulty components that overheat or emit burning smells helps address which two important goals of CHS?\",\"questionType\":\"Easy\",\"correctAnswer\":0},{\"id\":1776121484198,\"type\":\"Easy\",\"skill\":\"Technical Comprehension\",\"options\":[\"Artificial Intelligence – because devices make automated decisions\",\"Internet of Things – because physical objects are interconnected through networks\",\"Remote Servicing – because devices can be controlled remotely\",\"Augmented Reality – because devices enhance user experience\"],\"question\":\"Which technological trend refers to devices connected through the internet that communicate and exchange data with each other?\",\"questionType\":\"Easy\",\"correctAnswer\":1},{\"id\":1776121484199,\"type\":\"Easy\",\"skill\":\"Memorization\",\"options\":[\"Artificial Intelligence\",\"Sustainability Concerns\",\"Internet of Things\",\"Remote Servicing\"],\"question\":\"Which CHS trend focuses on reducing electronic waste and promoting environmentally responsible practices?\",\"questionType\":\"Easy\",\"correctAnswer\":1},{\"id\":1776121484200,\"type\":\"Easy\",\"skill\":\"Technical Comprehension\",\"options\":[\"Inputting Data\",\"Processing Data\",\"Storing Data\",\"Outputting Data\"],\"question\":\"The Central Processing Unit (CPU) is responsible for which basic computer hardware operation?\",\"questionType\":\"Easy\",\"correctAnswer\":1},{\"id\":1776121484201,\"type\":\"Easy\",\"skill\":\"Problem Solving\",\"options\":[\"Implement solutions\",\"Identify the problem\",\"Test hypothesis\",\"Gather information\"],\"question\":\"What is the FIRST step in the hardware troubleshooting process?\",\"questionType\":\"Easy\",\"correctAnswer\":3},{\"id\":1776121484202,\"type\":\"Easy\",\"skill\":\"Analytical Thinking\",\"options\":[\"Clicking a mouse to open a folder\",\"Taking a photo with a webcam, editing it, saving it to a flash drive, and printing it\",\"Listening to music stored on a hard drive\",\"Typing text into a word processor without saving\"],\"question\":\"Which activity demonstrates all four basic computer hardware operations (input, processing, storage, output)?\",\"questionType\":\"Easy\",\"correctAnswer\":1},{\"id\":1776121484203,\"type\":\"Easy\",\"skill\":\"Critical Thinking\",\"options\":[\"Motherboard\",\"Power supply\",\"Internal drives\",\"RAM modules\"],\"question\":\"According to the proper sequence for computer assembly, which component should be installed FIRST after opening the case?\",\"questionType\":\"Easy\",\"correctAnswer\":1},{\"id\":1776121484204,\"type\":\"Easy\",\"skill\":\"Critical Thinking\",\"options\":[\"Regular maintenance, upgrading components when needed, and recycling old parts\",\"Replacing all computers every year with new energy-efficient models\",\"Only repairing systems after complete failure\",\"Using only remote servicing tools\"],\"question\":\"Which CHS practice helps extend computer lifespan while minimizing cost and environmental impact?\",\"questionType\":\"Easy\",\"correctAnswer\":0},{\"id\":1776121484205,\"type\":\"Easy\",\"skill\":\"Critical Thinking\",\"options\":[\"Continue with the assembly and install the power supply last\",\"Force the power supply into place around the motherboard\",\"Remove the motherboard and install the power supply in the correct sequence\",\"Leave the power supply out and use an external power source\"],\"question\":\"What should a technician do if they installed components in the wrong order during computer assembly?\",\"questionType\":\"Easy\",\"correctAnswer\":2},{\"id\":1776121484206,\"type\":\"Easy\",\"skill\":\"Memorization\",\"options\":[\"Artificial Intelligence (AI)\",\"Remote Servicing\",\"Sustainability Concerns\",\"Internet of Things (IoT)\"],\"question\":\"It is a trend in CHS where devices typically found within homes are now functional due to being embedded with sensors, software, and other technologies, with the intent of interconnection and data exchange to other devices connected to the internet.\",\"questionType\":\"Easy\",\"correctAnswer\":3},{\"id\":1776121484207,\"type\":\"Easy\",\"skill\":\"Analytical Thinking\",\"options\":[\"maintaining computer hardware and performing routine diagnosis\",\"using tools to solder resistors to an electric circuit board of an appliance\",\"creating a code to make a game character to jump through a development software\",\"creating schematics for network architecture of a company\"],\"question\":\"Among the situations below, which is the appropriate description about what CHS is all about?\",\"questionType\":\"Easy\",\"correctAnswer\":2}]', '{\"hours\":2,\"minutes\":30}', 'Easy', NULL, '[{\"id\":\"introduction\",\"type\":\"introduction\",\"label\":\"Introduction\",\"order\":1},{\"id\":\"diagnostic\",\"type\":\"diagnostic\",\"label\":\"Diagnostic\",\"order\":2},{\"id\":\"lesson\",\"type\":\"lesson\",\"label\":\"Lesson\",\"order\":3},{\"id\":\"final\",\"type\":\"final\",\"label\":\"Final Assessment\",\"order\":4}]');
INSERT INTO `module` (`ModuleID`, `ModuleTitle`, `Description`, `LessonOrder`, `Tesda_Reference`, `Is_Unlocked`, `Is_Completed`, `LessonLanguage`, `Is_Deleted`, `created_at`, `updated_at`, `sections`, `diagnosticQuestions`, `reviewQuestions`, `finalQuestions`, `LessonTime`, `Difficulty`, `finalInstruction`, `roadmapStages`) VALUES
(7, 'Occupational Health and Safety Practices', '<div>A practice that involves a systematic approach to protecting workers by identifying and controlling hazards, implementing preventive measures, and providing training. An effective OHS reduces workplace injuries, illnesses, and operational disruptions.</div><p><br></p><p><br></p><p><strong>Learning Objectives:</strong></p><p>This lesson aims to:</p><ol style=\"list-style-type: decimal;\"><li>define Occupational Health and Safety (OHS);</li><li>identify common workplace hazards; and</li><li>demonstrate safe practices to minimize or prevent workplace hazards.</li></ol>', 2, '', 1, 0, 'English', 0, '2026-03-09 22:04:11', '2026-06-29 07:54:55', '[{\"id\":1776122922462,\"file\":null,\"type\":\"topic\",\"order\":1,\"title\":\"Topic 1: Common Workplace Hazards\",\"caption\":\"\",\"content\":\"\",\"fileName\":null},{\"id\":1777220246972,\"file\":null,\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"order\":2,\"title\":\"\",\"caption\":\"\",\"content\":\"<p>Computer servicing may look safe on the surface, but hidden hazards can injure, damage equipment, or disrupt workflow if not understood. This topic will help you identify common risks, practice safe troubleshooting habits, and maintain a secure, hazard-free environment.</p>\\n<p>Understanding workplace hazards in computer servicing means learning to identify, assess, and prevent the risks that technicians may face while repairing, assembling, or maintaining computer systems and related equipment. Even though computer servicing may look like a low-risk job, it involves several hidden hazards that can lead to accidents, injuries or equipment damage if not properly managed.</p>\\n<p>Here are the 4 hazards to be discussed in this lesson:</p>\\n<p>Electric Hazard - Electrical shocks, burns, or arc flashes from live circuits, frayed power cords, or ungrounded outlets during computer servicing; always unplug devices, use insulated tools, and verify power is off with a multimeter before handling components.[73][74]</p>\\n<p>Physical Hazard - Cuts from sharp edges on cases or fans, impacts from dropping heavy components like monitors or PSUs, trips over cables, or strains from awkward handling; secure workspaces, wear cut-resistant gloves, and use trolleys for transport.[73][75]</p>\\n<p>Ergonomic Hazard - Repetitive strain injuries (RSI) from prolonged typing, mouse use, or awkward postures while assembling parts, leading to carpal tunnel or back pain; adjust workstations to elbow height, take micro-breaks, and use anti-fatigue mats.[73][76]</p>\\n<p>Chemical Hazard - Toxic fumes or skin irritation from solder flux, cleaning solvents (e.g., isopropyl alcohol), battery leaks, or thermal paste; ensure ventilation, wear nitrile gloves and respirators, and use spill kits for containment.[73][74]</p>\",\"fileName\":null,\"tableTitle\":\"\",\"contentLayout\":\"text\"},{\"id\":1776122922630,\"file\":null,\"type\":\"video\",\"order\":3,\"title\":\"\",\"caption\":\"Lesson 2 Topic 1 Video\",\"content\":\"https://www.dropbox.com/scl/fi/k6xe1dbu0spvw6uv54d9k/Lesson-2-Topic-1.mp4?rlkey=otk72a7ujsb19blh4i59xu9zw&st=520yiyvs&dl=0\",\"fileName\":null},{\"id\":1776122922469,\"file\":null,\"type\":\"review-multiple-choice\",\"order\":4,\"title\":\"\",\"caption\":\"\",\"content\":\"\",\"fileName\":null,\"questions\":[{\"id\":1776122922466,\"type\":\"Easy\",\"skill\":\"Memorization\",\"options\":[\"Using an anti-static wrist strap\",\"Working with damaged or exposed wires\",\"Organizing files on the desktop\",\"Cleaning the computer screen with a microfiber cloth\"],\"question\":\"Which of the following is an example of an electric hazard in computer servicing?\",\"questionType\":\"Easy\",\"correctAnswer\":1},{\"id\":1776122922467,\"type\":\"Easy\",\"skill\":\"Memorization\",\"options\":[\"Pull the cord from the wire to save time\",\"Touch equipment with wet hands\",\"Inspect cables before using computers\",\"Open the power supply unit to check for issues\"],\"question\":\"What is a safe practice when dealing with electrical equipment?\",\"questionType\":\"Easy\",\"correctAnswer\":2},{\"id\":1776122922468,\"type\":\"Easy\",\"skill\":\"Problem Solving\",\"options\":[\"Open it to examine the inside\",\"Continue using it until it stops working\",\"Report it and stop using the device\",\"Tap it lightly to make the noise disappear\"],\"question\":\"What should be done when a power supply shows signs of malfunction such as unusual noise?\",\"questionType\":\"Easy\",\"correctAnswer\":2}]},{\"id\":1776122922470,\"file\":null,\"type\":\"topic\",\"order\":5,\"title\":\"Topic 2: Electric Hazards\",\"caption\":\"\",\"content\":\"\",\"fileName\":null},{\"id\":1777220246973,\"file\":null,\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"order\":6,\"title\":\"\",\"caption\":\"\",\"content\":\"<p>In this field, a lot of devices are being used—computers, routers, printers, monitors—everything is powered by electricity. That means, in any situation where electricity can harm a person or damage equipment, there’s always a risk if we’re not careful.</p>\\n<p>Damaged or Exposed Wires</p>\\n<p>Overloading Power Outlets</p>\\n<p>Wet Areas Near Equipment</p>\\n<p>Faulty Power Supplies or Old Equipment</p>\\n<p>Poor Cable Management</p>\\n<p>Ungrounded Outlets</p>\\n<p>Safe Practices Against Electric Hazards:</p>\",\"fileName\":null,\"tableTitle\":\"\",\"contentLayout\":\"text\"},{\"id\":1777220246974,\"file\":null,\"type\":\"image\",\"order\":7,\"title\":\"Electric Hazards\",\"images\":[{\"url\":\"/uploads/lessons/001_damaged_or_exposed_wires.webp\",\"file\":null,\"caption\":\"Damaged or Exposed Wires\",\"fileName\":null},{\"url\":\"/uploads/lessons/002_overloading_power_outlets.webp\",\"file\":null,\"caption\":\"Overloading Power Outlets\",\"fileName\":null},{\"url\":\"/uploads/lessons/003_wet_areas_near_equipment.webp\",\"file\":null,\"caption\":\"Wet Areas Near Equipment\",\"fileName\":null},{\"url\":\"/uploads/lessons/004_faulty_power_supplies_or_old_equipment.webp\",\"file\":null,\"caption\":\"Faulty Power Supplies or Old Equipment\",\"fileName\":null},{\"url\":\"/uploads/lessons/005_poor_cable_management.webp\",\"file\":null,\"caption\":\"Poor Cable Management\",\"fileName\":null},{\"url\":\"/uploads/lessons/006_ungrounded_outlets.webp\",\"file\":null,\"caption\":\"Ungrounded Outlets\",\"fileName\":null}],\"layout\":\"grid-3\",\"caption\":\"\",\"content\":\"/uploads/lessons/001_damaged_or_exposed_wires.webp\",\"fileName\":null},{\"id\":1776122922486,\"file\":null,\"type\":\"video\",\"order\":8,\"title\":\"\",\"caption\":\"\",\"content\":\"https://www.youtube.com/shorts/EGhmCir-Bdk\",\"fileName\":null},{\"id\":1776122922490,\"file\":null,\"type\":\"review-multiple-choice\",\"order\":9,\"title\":\"\",\"caption\":\"\",\"content\":\"\",\"fileName\":null,\"questions\":[{\"id\":1776122922487,\"type\":\"Easy\",\"skill\":\"Memorization\",\"options\":[\"Hazards caused by electricity\",\"Situations that can physically harm a person through posture, movement, or surroundings\",\"Threats from computer viruses\",\"Hazards involving chemical substances\"],\"question\":\"What are physical hazards in the workplace?\",\"questionType\":\"Easy\",\"correctAnswer\":1},{\"id\":1776122922488,\"type\":\"Easy\",\"skill\":\"Memorization\",\"options\":[\"Underground outlets\",\"Damaged power supply\",\"Poor workstation setup\",\"Overload extension cords\"],\"question\":\"Which of the following is an example of physical hazard?\",\"questionType\":\"Easy\",\"correctAnswer\":2},{\"id\":1776122922489,\"type\":\"Easy\",\"skill\":\"Memorization\",\"options\":[\"Faster internet speed\",\"Better airflow\",\"Tripping accidents and equipment damage\",\"Less need for cable management\"],\"question\":\"What can cluttered cables and wires cause?\",\"questionType\":\"Easy\",\"correctAnswer\":2}]},{\"id\":1776122922491,\"file\":null,\"type\":\"topic\",\"order\":10,\"title\":\"Topic 3: Physical Hazards\",\"caption\":\"\",\"content\":\"\",\"fileName\":null},{\"id\":1777220246975,\"file\":null,\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"order\":11,\"title\":\"\",\"caption\":\"\",\"content\":\"<p>Physical hazards are anything in the environment that can physically harm a person. Unlike electrical hazards, these don’t involve electricity. Instead, they involve your body—your posture, movement, and surroundings. These are situations that can cause injuries like slips, falls, cuts, muscle pain, or even long-term health problems if we are not careful.</p>\\n<p>Most physical hazards come from:</p>\\n<p>Poor workstation setup</p>\\n<p>Misplaced equipment</p>\\n<p>Unsafe lifting techniques</p>\\n<p>Cluttered areas</p>\\n<p>Inadequate lighting or ventilation</p>\\n<p>These sources of physical hazards tend to appear as a result in workplace through the following:</p>\",\"fileName\":null,\"tableTitle\":\"\",\"contentLayout\":\"text\"},{\"id\":1777220246976,\"file\":null,\"type\":\"image\",\"order\":12,\"title\":\"Physical Hazards\",\"images\":[{\"url\":\"/uploads/lessons/007_poor_workstation_setup.webp\",\"file\":null,\"caption\":\"Poor workstation setup\",\"fileName\":null},{\"url\":\"/uploads/lessons/008_misplaced_equipment.webp\",\"file\":null,\"caption\":\"Misplaced equipment\",\"fileName\":null},{\"url\":\"/uploads/lessons/009_unsafe_lifting_techniques.webp\",\"file\":null,\"caption\":\"Unsafe lifting techniques\",\"fileName\":null},{\"url\":\"/uploads/lessons/010_cluttered_areas_crop.webp\",\"file\":null,\"caption\":\"Cluttered areas\",\"fileName\":null},{\"url\":\"/uploads/lessons/011_inadequate_lighting_or_ventilation.webp\",\"file\":null,\"caption\":\"Inadequate lighting or ventilation\",\"fileName\":null}],\"layout\":\"grid-3\",\"caption\":\"\",\"content\":\"/uploads/lessons/007_poor_workstation_setup.webp\",\"fileName\":null},{\"id\":1776122922510,\"file\":null,\"type\":\"review-multiple-choice\",\"order\":13,\"title\":\"\",\"caption\":\"\",\"content\":\"\",\"fileName\":null,\"questions\":[{\"id\":1776122922507,\"type\":\"Easy\",\"skill\":\"Technical Comprehension\",\"options\":[\"They cause injuries instantly\",\"They only affect computer hardware\",\"They cause injuries slowly over time due to repetitive tasks\",\"They immediately damage equipment\"],\"question\":\"Why are ergonomic hazards dangerous?\",\"questionType\":\"Easy\",\"correctAnswer\":2},{\"id\":1776122922508,\"type\":\"Easy\",\"skill\":\"Memorization\",\"options\":[\"Wet floors\",\"A monitor placed too high or too low\",\"Exposed wires\",\"Overloaded sockets\"],\"question\":\"Which of the following is an example of an ergonomic hazard?\",\"questionType\":\"Easy\",\"correctAnswer\":1},{\"id\":1776122922509,\"type\":\"Easy\",\"skill\":\"Memorization\",\"options\":[\"Undergrounded outlets\",\"Solvents and cleaning sprays\",\"Cluttered cables\",\"Improper lifting of heavy objects\"],\"question\":\"Which of the following is an example of a chemical hazard?\",\"questionType\":\"Easy\",\"correctAnswer\":1}]},{\"id\":1776122922511,\"file\":null,\"type\":\"topic\",\"order\":14,\"title\":\"Topic 4. Ergonomic Hazards\",\"caption\":\"\",\"content\":\"\",\"fileName\":null},{\"id\":1777220246977,\"file\":null,\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"order\":15,\"title\":\"\",\"caption\":\"\",\"content\":\"<p>We are now going to talk about something that affects everyone who uses computers—whether in school, at home, or in the workplace: ergonomics. You might not think about it, but the way you sit, type, use the mouse, or position your monitor can affect your health over time.</p>\\n<p>In computer servicing or ICT, people often sit for long hours doing repetitive tasks. This can lead to pain, discomfort, and long-term injuries if the workstations aren\'t designed correctly.</p>\\n<p>Ergonomic hazards are risks in the workplace that can hurt your muscles, joints, tendons, or posture. These hazards come from the way the work is set up–your chair, your table, the height of your monitor, even how far you reach for the mouse.</p>\\n<p>Unlike accidents that happen suddenly, ergonomic hazards cause injuries slowly over time.</p>\\n<p>For example:</p>\\n<p>Sitting in a slouched position for hours</p>\\n<p>Reaching too far for the keyboard</p>\\n<p>Working without taking breaks</p>\",\"fileName\":null,\"tableTitle\":\"\",\"contentLayout\":\"text\"},{\"id\":1776122922520,\"file\":null,\"type\":\"review-multiple-choice\",\"order\":16,\"title\":\"\",\"caption\":\"\",\"content\":\"\",\"fileName\":null,\"questions\":[{\"id\":1776122922517,\"type\":\"Easy\",\"skill\":\"Technical Comprehension\",\"options\":[\"They spill easily\",\"They produce toxic fumes when heated\",\"They smell bad\",\"They damage computer keyboards\"],\"question\":\"Why is solder and flux considered hazardous?\",\"questionType\":\"Easy\",\"correctAnswer\":1},{\"id\":1776122922518,\"type\":\"Easy\",\"skill\":\"Memorization\",\"options\":[\"Torx Screwdriver\",\"Wire Stripper\",\"Wire Cutter\",\"Crimping Tool\"],\"question\":\"It is a hand tool designed to precisely remove the insulation from the ends of electrical wires without damaging the conductor inside.\",\"questionType\":\"Easy\",\"correctAnswer\":1},{\"id\":1776122922519,\"type\":\"Easy\",\"skill\":\"Memorization\",\"options\":[\"Phillips Screwdriver\",\"Wire Stripper\",\"Wire Cutter\",\"Crimping Tool\"],\"question\":\"Question: A technician is attaching an RJ-45 connector to a network cable. The wire has already been stripped, and the connector must now be firmly attached by compressing the metal pins onto the wires. Which tool should be used?\",\"questionType\":\"Easy\",\"correctAnswer\":3}]},{\"id\":1776122922521,\"file\":null,\"type\":\"topic\",\"order\":17,\"title\":\"Topic 5. Chemical Hazards\",\"caption\":\"\",\"content\":\"\",\"fileName\":null},{\"id\":1777220246978,\"file\":null,\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"order\":18,\"title\":\"\",\"caption\":\"\",\"content\":\"<p>In our workplace, chemical hazards come from maintenance/cleaning supplies like solvents and sprays, compressed gases like dusters, and components like solder, potentially causing skin/respiratory issues from inhalation or contact, requiring personal protective equipment (PPE) like gloves and masks, good ventilation proper storage, and training on handling risks from chemicals like cleaning agents, aerosols, and potentially even heavy metals in components.</p>\\n<p>Common Chemical Hazards</p>\\n<p>Cleaning &amp; Maintenance: Solvents, contact cleaners, keyboard cleaners, sprays, and wipes used for equipment upkeep can release harmful vapors or skin irritation.</p>\\n<p>Compressed Gas Dusters: Used to remove dust, these can cause frostbite if held too close or sprayed on skin and release irritant propellants.</p>\\n<p>Solder &amp; Flux: Used for hardware repair, these contain chemicals that can produce toxic fumes.</p>\\n<p>Adhesives &amp; Sealants: Glues like superglue or epoxy used in repairs can bond skin and release irritating fumes.</p>\\n<p>Old Components: Older electronics might contain hazardous materials like asbestos or heavy metals.</p>\\n<p>Health Effects</p>\",\"fileName\":null,\"tableTitle\":\"\",\"contentLayout\":\"text\"},{\"id\":1776122922532,\"file\":null,\"type\":\"review-multiple-choice\",\"order\":19,\"title\":\"\",\"caption\":\"\",\"content\":\"\",\"fileName\":null,\"questions\":[{\"id\":1776122922529,\"type\":\"Easy\",\"skill\":\"Memorization\",\"options\":[\"Anti-Static Wrist Strap\",\"LAN Tester\",\"Loopback Adapter\",\"Multimeter\"],\"question\":\"This tool is used to test circuit integrity and a component’s electricity quality.\",\"questionType\":\"Easy\",\"correctAnswer\":3},{\"id\":1776122922530,\"type\":\"Easy\",\"skill\":\"Memorization\",\"options\":[\"Anti-Static Wrist Strap\",\"Lint-Free Cloth\",\"Anti-Static Mat\",\"Cable Ties\"],\"question\":\"This tool is used to put on hardware to prevent static electricity building up.\",\"questionType\":\"Easy\",\"correctAnswer\":0},{\"id\":1776122922531,\"type\":\"Easy\",\"skill\":\"Memorization\",\"options\":[\"Tools are grouped by type\",\"Handles are color-coded\",\"Presence of cracks, rust, or frayed cords\",\"Tools are stored in padded cases\"],\"question\":\"Question: While preparing tools for a servicing task, a technician notices that one tool has rust on its metal surface and the power cord is frayed. What does this indicate about the condition of the tool?\",\"questionType\":\"Easy\",\"correctAnswer\":2}]},{\"id\":1776122922533,\"file\":null,\"type\":\"topic\",\"order\":20,\"title\":\"Topic 6. Different Tools Used in Computer Hardware Servicing\",\"caption\":\"\",\"content\":\"\",\"fileName\":null},{\"id\":1777220246979,\"file\":null,\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"order\":21,\"title\":\"\",\"caption\":\"\",\"content\":\"<p>Proper Use of Tools</p>\\n<p>i. Procedures for Using Hand Tools Correctly</p>\\n<p>Phillips head screwdriver is a tool used to loosen or tighten cross-head screws. To properly use the tool, select the right size bit for the screw head to avoid stripping. Apply firm, straight downward pressure while turning clockwise to tighten or counterclockwise to loosen; never over-torque to prevent cam-out, or when the screwdriver bit—a detachable tip or toolhead used to drive screws—comes out of the screw head while turning it.[31]</p>\\n<p>Flat Head Screwdriver</p>\\n<p>Flat head screwdriver is a tool used to loosen or tighten slotted screw-a single straight slot on the head. To properly use the tool, match the blade width to the screw slot exactly. Insert fully straight into the slot, then turn slowly with steady pressure to avoid slipping, which can damage the screw or surrounding case.[31]</p>\\n<p>Torx Screwdriver</p>\\n<p>Torx screwdriver is a tool used to loosen or tighten screws that have a star-like depression on the top. To properly use the tool, align the T-bit precisely with the star-shaped recess. Rotate smoothly with even force, as Torx resists stripping better but requires full seating to avoid rounding the drive.[31]</p>\\n<p>Hex Driver</p>\",\"fileName\":null,\"tableTitle\":\"\",\"contentLayout\":\"text\"},{\"id\":1777220246980,\"file\":null,\"type\":\"image\",\"order\":22,\"title\":\"Phillips head screwdriver\",\"images\":[{\"url\":\"/uploads/lessons/012_flathead_crop.webp\",\"file\":null,\"caption\":\"Phillips head screwdriver\",\"fileName\":null}],\"layout\":\"text-left\",\"caption\":\"\",\"content\":\"/uploads/lessons/012_flathead_crop.webp\",\"fileName\":null,\"sideTexts\":[\"<p><strong>Phillips head screwdriver</strong></p><p>Phillips head screwdriver is a tool used to loosen or tighten cross-head…</p>\"],\"layerImages\":[[{\"url\":\"/uploads/lessons/012_flathead_crop.webp\",\"file\":null,\"caption\":\"Phillips head screwdriver\",\"fileName\":null}]]},{\"id\":1777220246981,\"file\":null,\"type\":\"image\",\"order\":23,\"title\":\"Flat head screwdriver\",\"images\":[{\"url\":\"/uploads/lessons/014_flat_head_screwdriver_is_a_tool_used_to_.webp\",\"file\":null,\"caption\":\"Flat head screwdriver\",\"fileName\":null}],\"layout\":\"text-left\",\"caption\":\"\",\"content\":\"/uploads/lessons/014_flat_head_screwdriver_is_a_tool_used_to_.webp\",\"fileName\":null,\"sideTexts\":[\"<p><strong>Flat head screwdriver</strong></p><p>Flat head screwdriver is a tool used to loosen or tighten slotted screw-a…</p>\"],\"layerImages\":[[{\"url\":\"/uploads/lessons/014_flat_head_screwdriver_is_a_tool_used_to_.webp\",\"file\":null,\"caption\":\"Flat head screwdriver\",\"fileName\":null}]]},{\"id\":1777220246982,\"file\":null,\"type\":\"image\",\"order\":24,\"title\":\"Torx screwdriver\",\"images\":[{\"url\":\"/uploads/lessons/017_torx_screwdriver_is_a_tool_used_to_loose.webp\",\"file\":null,\"caption\":\"Torx screwdriver\",\"fileName\":null}],\"layout\":\"text-left\",\"caption\":\"\",\"content\":\"/uploads/lessons/017_torx_screwdriver_is_a_tool_used_to_loose.webp\",\"fileName\":null,\"sideTexts\":[\"<p><strong>Torx screwdriver</strong></p><p>Torx screwdriver is a tool used to loosen or tighten screws that have a…</p>\"],\"layerImages\":[[{\"url\":\"/uploads/lessons/017_torx_screwdriver_is_a_tool_used_to_loose.webp\",\"file\":null,\"caption\":\"Torx screwdriver\",\"fileName\":null}]]},{\"id\":1777220246983,\"file\":null,\"type\":\"image\",\"order\":25,\"title\":\"Hex Driver\",\"images\":[{\"url\":\"/uploads/lessons/018_hex_driver.webp\",\"file\":null,\"caption\":\"Hex Driver\",\"fileName\":null}],\"layout\":\"text-left\",\"caption\":\"\",\"content\":\"/uploads/lessons/018_hex_driver.webp\",\"fileName\":null,\"sideTexts\":[\"<p><strong>Hex Driver</strong></p>\"],\"layerImages\":[[{\"url\":\"/uploads/lessons/018_hex_driver.webp\",\"file\":null,\"caption\":\"Hex Driver\",\"fileName\":null}]]},{\"id\":1777220246984,\"file\":null,\"type\":\"image\",\"order\":26,\"title\":\"Needle nose pliers\",\"images\":[{\"url\":\"/uploads/lessons/020_needle_nose_pliers_is_a_tool_used_to_hol.webp\",\"file\":null,\"caption\":\"Needle nose pliers\",\"fileName\":null}],\"layout\":\"text-left\",\"caption\":\"\",\"content\":\"/uploads/lessons/020_needle_nose_pliers_is_a_tool_used_to_hol.webp\",\"fileName\":null,\"sideTexts\":[\"<p><strong>Needle nose pliers</strong></p><p>Needle nose pliers is a tool used to hold small parts. To properly use the…</p>\"],\"layerImages\":[[{\"url\":\"/uploads/lessons/020_needle_nose_pliers_is_a_tool_used_to_hol.webp\",\"file\":null,\"caption\":\"Needle nose pliers\",\"fileName\":null}]]},{\"id\":1777220246985,\"file\":null,\"type\":\"image\",\"order\":27,\"title\":\"Wire cutter\",\"images\":[{\"url\":\"/uploads/lessons/021_wire_cutter_is_a_tool_used_to_strip_and_.webp\",\"file\":null,\"caption\":\"Wire cutter\",\"fileName\":null}],\"layout\":\"text-left\",\"caption\":\"\",\"content\":\"/uploads/lessons/021_wire_cutter_is_a_tool_used_to_strip_and_.webp\",\"fileName\":null,\"sideTexts\":[\"<p><strong>Wire cutter</strong></p><p>Wire cutter is a tool used to strip and cut wires. To properly use the tool,…</p>\"],\"layerImages\":[[{\"url\":\"/uploads/lessons/021_wire_cutter_is_a_tool_used_to_strip_and_.webp\",\"file\":null,\"caption\":\"Wire cutter\",\"fileName\":null}]]},{\"id\":1777220246986,\"file\":null,\"type\":\"image\",\"order\":28,\"title\":\"Wire Stripper\",\"images\":[{\"url\":\"/uploads/lessons/022_to_properly_use_the_tool_select_the_notc.webp\",\"file\":null,\"caption\":\"Wire Stripper\",\"fileName\":null}],\"layout\":\"text-left\",\"caption\":\"\",\"content\":\"/uploads/lessons/022_to_properly_use_the_tool_select_the_notc.webp\",\"fileName\":null,\"sideTexts\":[\"<p><strong>Wire Stripper</strong></p><p>To properly use the tool, select the notch matching the wire gauge (e.g., 22–24…</p>\"],\"layerImages\":[[{\"url\":\"/uploads/lessons/022_to_properly_use_the_tool_select_the_notc.webp\",\"file\":null,\"caption\":\"Wire Stripper\",\"fileName\":null}]]},{\"id\":1777220246987,\"file\":null,\"type\":\"image\",\"order\":29,\"title\":\"Flashlight\",\"images\":[{\"url\":\"/uploads/lessons/023_flashlight_is_a_tool_used_to_light_up_ar.webp\",\"file\":null,\"caption\":\"Flashlight\",\"fileName\":null}],\"layout\":\"text-left\",\"caption\":\"\",\"content\":\"/uploads/lessons/023_flashlight_is_a_tool_used_to_light_up_ar.webp\",\"fileName\":null,\"sideTexts\":[\"<p><strong>Flashlight</strong></p><p>Flashlight is a tool used to light up areas that you cannot see well. To…</p>\"],\"layerImages\":[[{\"url\":\"/uploads/lessons/023_flashlight_is_a_tool_used_to_light_up_ar.webp\",\"file\":null,\"caption\":\"Flashlight\",\"fileName\":null}]]},{\"id\":1777220246988,\"file\":null,\"type\":\"image\",\"order\":30,\"title\":\"Part retriever\",\"images\":[{\"url\":\"/uploads/lessons/024_part_retriever_is_a_tool_used_to_retriev.webp\",\"file\":null,\"caption\":\"Part retriever\",\"fileName\":null}],\"layout\":\"text-left\",\"caption\":\"\",\"content\":\"/uploads/lessons/024_part_retriever_is_a_tool_used_to_retriev.webp\",\"fileName\":null,\"sideTexts\":[\"<p><strong>Part retriever</strong></p><p>Part retriever is a tool used to retrieve parts from a location that is too…</p>\"],\"layerImages\":[[{\"url\":\"/uploads/lessons/024_part_retriever_is_a_tool_used_to_retriev.webp\",\"file\":null,\"caption\":\"Part retriever\",\"fileName\":null}]]},{\"id\":1777220246989,\"file\":null,\"type\":\"image\",\"order\":31,\"title\":\"Tweezers\",\"images\":[{\"url\":\"/uploads/lessons/025_tweezers_is_a_tool_used_to_manipulate_sm.webp\",\"file\":null,\"caption\":\"Tweezers\",\"fileName\":null}],\"layout\":\"text-left\",\"caption\":\"\",\"content\":\"/uploads/lessons/025_tweezers_is_a_tool_used_to_manipulate_sm.webp\",\"fileName\":null,\"sideTexts\":[\"<p><strong>Tweezers</strong></p><p>Tweezers is a tool used to manipulate small parts. To properly use the tool,…</p>\"],\"layerImages\":[[{\"url\":\"/uploads/lessons/025_tweezers_is_a_tool_used_to_manipulate_sm.webp\",\"file\":null,\"caption\":\"Tweezers\",\"fileName\":null}]]},{\"id\":1777220246990,\"file\":null,\"type\":\"image\",\"order\":32,\"title\":\"Crimping Tool\",\"images\":[{\"url\":\"/uploads/lessons/026_crimping_tool.webp\",\"file\":null,\"caption\":\"Crimping Tool\",\"fileName\":null}],\"layout\":\"text-left\",\"caption\":\"\",\"content\":\"/uploads/lessons/026_crimping_tool.webp\",\"fileName\":null,\"sideTexts\":[\"<p><strong>Crimping Tool</strong></p>\"],\"layerImages\":[[{\"url\":\"/uploads/lessons/026_crimping_tool.webp\",\"file\":null,\"caption\":\"Crimping Tool\",\"fileName\":null}]]},{\"id\":1777220246991,\"file\":null,\"type\":\"image\",\"order\":33,\"title\":\"RJ45\",\"images\":[{\"url\":\"/uploads/lessons/027_rj45.webp\",\"file\":null,\"caption\":\"RJ45\",\"fileName\":null}],\"layout\":\"text-left\",\"caption\":\"\",\"content\":\"/uploads/lessons/027_rj45.webp\",\"fileName\":null,\"sideTexts\":[\"<p><strong>RJ45</strong></p>\"],\"layerImages\":[[{\"url\":\"/uploads/lessons/027_rj45.webp\",\"file\":null,\"caption\":\"RJ45\",\"fileName\":null}]]},{\"id\":1777220246992,\"file\":null,\"type\":\"image\",\"order\":34,\"title\":\"Loopback adapter\",\"images\":[{\"url\":\"/uploads/lessons/028_loopback_adapter_is_a_tool_used_to_test_.webp\",\"file\":null,\"caption\":\"Loopback adapter\",\"fileName\":null}],\"layout\":\"text-left\",\"caption\":\"\",\"content\":\"/uploads/lessons/028_loopback_adapter_is_a_tool_used_to_test_.webp\",\"fileName\":null,\"sideTexts\":[\"<p><strong>Loopback adapter</strong></p><p>Loopback adapter is a tool used to test the functionality of computer ports. To…</p>\"],\"layerImages\":[[{\"url\":\"/uploads/lessons/028_loopback_adapter_is_a_tool_used_to_test_.webp\",\"file\":null,\"caption\":\"Loopback adapter\",\"fileName\":null}]]},{\"id\":1777220246993,\"file\":null,\"type\":\"image\",\"order\":35,\"title\":\"Multimeter\",\"images\":[{\"url\":\"/uploads/lessons/029_multimeter.webp\",\"file\":null,\"caption\":\"Multimeter\",\"fileName\":null}],\"layout\":\"text-left\",\"caption\":\"\",\"content\":\"/uploads/lessons/029_multimeter.webp\",\"fileName\":null,\"sideTexts\":[\"<p><strong>Multimeter</strong></p>\"],\"layerImages\":[[{\"url\":\"/uploads/lessons/029_multimeter.webp\",\"file\":null,\"caption\":\"Multimeter\",\"fileName\":null}]]},{\"id\":1777220246994,\"file\":null,\"type\":\"image\",\"order\":36,\"title\":\"LAN Tester\",\"images\":[{\"url\":\"/uploads/lessons/030_lan_tester.webp\",\"file\":null,\"caption\":\"LAN Tester\",\"fileName\":null}],\"layout\":\"text-left\",\"caption\":\"\",\"content\":\"/uploads/lessons/030_lan_tester.webp\",\"fileName\":null,\"sideTexts\":[\"<p><strong>LAN Tester</strong></p>\"],\"layerImages\":[[{\"url\":\"/uploads/lessons/030_lan_tester.webp\",\"file\":null,\"caption\":\"LAN Tester\",\"fileName\":null}]]},{\"id\":1777220246995,\"file\":null,\"type\":\"image\",\"order\":37,\"title\":\"Lint-Free Cloth\",\"images\":[{\"url\":\"/uploads/lessons/031_lint_free_cloth.webp\",\"file\":null,\"caption\":\"Lint-Free Cloth\",\"fileName\":null}],\"layout\":\"text-left\",\"caption\":\"\",\"content\":\"/uploads/lessons/031_lint_free_cloth.webp\",\"fileName\":null,\"sideTexts\":[\"<p><strong>Lint-Free Cloth</strong></p>\"],\"layerImages\":[[{\"url\":\"/uploads/lessons/031_lint_free_cloth.webp\",\"file\":null,\"caption\":\"Lint-Free Cloth\",\"fileName\":null}]]},{\"id\":1777220246996,\"file\":null,\"type\":\"image\",\"order\":38,\"title\":\"Compressed Air\",\"images\":[{\"url\":\"/uploads/lessons/032_compressed_air.webp\",\"file\":null,\"caption\":\"Compressed Air\",\"fileName\":null}],\"layout\":\"text-left\",\"caption\":\"\",\"content\":\"/uploads/lessons/032_compressed_air.webp\",\"fileName\":null,\"sideTexts\":[\"<p><strong>Compressed Air</strong></p>\"],\"layerImages\":[[{\"url\":\"/uploads/lessons/032_compressed_air.webp\",\"file\":null,\"caption\":\"Compressed Air\",\"fileName\":null}]]},{\"id\":1777220246997,\"file\":null,\"type\":\"image\",\"order\":39,\"title\":\"Anti-Static Mat\",\"images\":[{\"url\":\"/uploads/lessons/034_anti_static_mat.webp\",\"file\":null,\"caption\":\"Anti-Static Mat\",\"fileName\":null}],\"layout\":\"text-left\",\"caption\":\"\",\"content\":\"/uploads/lessons/034_anti_static_mat.webp\",\"fileName\":null,\"sideTexts\":[\"<p><strong>Anti-Static Mat</strong></p>\"],\"layerImages\":[[{\"url\":\"/uploads/lessons/034_anti_static_mat.webp\",\"file\":null,\"caption\":\"Anti-Static Mat\",\"fileName\":null}]]},{\"id\":1777220246998,\"file\":null,\"type\":\"image\",\"order\":40,\"title\":\"Anti-Static Wrist Strap\",\"images\":[{\"url\":\"/uploads/lessons/035_anti_static_wrist_strap.webp\",\"file\":null,\"caption\":\"Anti-Static Wrist Strap\",\"fileName\":null}],\"layout\":\"text-left\",\"caption\":\"\",\"content\":\"/uploads/lessons/035_anti_static_wrist_strap.webp\",\"fileName\":null,\"sideTexts\":[\"<p><strong>Anti-Static Wrist Strap</strong></p>\"],\"layerImages\":[[{\"url\":\"/uploads/lessons/035_anti_static_wrist_strap.webp\",\"file\":null,\"caption\":\"Anti-Static Wrist Strap\",\"fileName\":null}]]},{\"id\":1776122922604,\"file\":null,\"type\":\"review-multiple-choice\",\"order\":41,\"title\":\"\",\"caption\":\"\",\"content\":\"\",\"fileName\":null,\"questions\":[{\"id\":1776122922603,\"type\":\"Easy\",\"skill\":\"Memorization\",\"options\":[\"Hanging all tools on magnetic strips\",\"Keeping compressed air cans near heat sources\",\"Storing sharp tools in sheaths or closed drawers and placing heavier items low\",\"Grouping all tools together in one container\"],\"question\":\"Which storage practice is recommended to ensure safety and prevent injuries when storing computer servicing tools?\",\"questionType\":\"Easy\",\"correctAnswer\":2}]},{\"id\":1776122922605,\"file\":null,\"type\":\"topic\",\"order\":42,\"title\":\"Topic 7: Reporting and Documenting Accidents or Hazards\",\"caption\":\"\",\"content\":\"\",\"fileName\":null},{\"id\":1777220246999,\"file\":null,\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"order\":43,\"title\":\"\",\"caption\":\"\",\"content\":\"<p>A hazard is a potential source of harm or dangerous condition that could lead to injury, damage, or illness but has not yet caused it—essentially a risk waiting to be realized. In contrast, an accident is an unplanned event where that hazard actually results in harm, injury, property damage, or loss.</p>\\n<p>For example, worn jaws on needle nose pliers represent a hazard because they could slip and pinch a finger, while the actual finger cut from that slip during wire bending is the accident; frayed multimeter leads pose a shock hazard, but the electric jolt from touching a live circuit turns it into an accident.</p>\\n<p>Similarly, a compressed air can lying on its side is a hazard for propellant leaks and chemical splashes, whereas the resulting skin burn from the tipped can is the accident, and an ungrounded ESD mat creates a static buildup hazard that becomes an accident when it fries a motherboard during a CPU swap.</p>\\n<p>The key takeaway is to identify hazards like dull wire stripper blades through inspections to prevent accidents such as nicked wires causing shorts; in Philippine DOLE terms, report both via WAIR forms—hazards preventively and accidents reactively.[60][63]</p>\\n<p>According to the lesson, what best distinguishes a hazard from an accident?</p>\\n<p>A hazard is a potential source of harm, while an accident is the actual harmful event</p>\\n<p>A hazard is intentional, while an accident is planned</p>\\n<p>A hazard causes damage, while an accident does not</p>\",\"fileName\":null,\"tableTitle\":\"\",\"contentLayout\":\"text\"},{\"id\":1777220247000,\"file\":null,\"type\":\"image\",\"order\":44,\"title\":\"Reporting and Documenting Accidents or Hazards\",\"images\":[{\"url\":\"/uploads/lessons/036_reporting_accidents_or_hazards_in_the_wo.webp\",\"file\":null,\"caption\":\"Reporting accidents or hazards in the workplace is essential\",\"fileName\":null},{\"url\":\"/uploads/lessons/037_ii_legal_and_organizational_compliance.webp\",\"file\":null,\"caption\":\"ii\",\"fileName\":null},{\"url\":\"/uploads/lessons/038_osha_301_forms.webp\",\"file\":null,\"caption\":\"OSHA 301 FORMS\",\"fileName\":null}],\"layout\":\"grid-3\",\"caption\":\"\",\"content\":\"/uploads/lessons/036_reporting_accidents_or_hazards_in_the_wo.webp\",\"fileName\":null},{\"id\":1776122922629,\"file\":null,\"type\":\"review-multiple-choice\",\"order\":45,\"title\":\"\",\"caption\":\"\",\"content\":\"\",\"fileName\":null,\"questions\":[{\"id\":1776122922626,\"type\":\"Easy\",\"skill\":\"Memorization\",\"options\":[\"A hazard is a potential source of harm, while an accident is the actual harmful event\",\"A hazard is intentional, while an accident is planned\",\"A hazard causes damage, while an accident does not\",\"A hazard only applies to tools, while accidents apply to people\"],\"question\":\"According to the lesson, what best distinguishes a hazard from an accident?\",\"questionType\":\"Easy\",\"correctAnswer\":0},{\"id\":1776122922627,\"type\":\"Easy\",\"skill\":\"Memorization\",\"options\":[\"It reduces paperwork requirements\",\"It allows immediate corrective actions to prevent recurrence\",\"It replaces the need for tool inspections\",\"It eliminates the use of diagnostic tools\"],\"question\":\"Why is timely reporting of accidents and hazards important for worker safety?\",\"questionType\":\"Easy\",\"correctAnswer\":1},{\"id\":1776122922628,\"type\":\"Easy\",\"skill\":\"Memorization\",\"options\":[\"It allows responders to prepare the correct first aid and medical supplies quickly\",\"It ensures tools are replaced annually\",\"It delays response until management approval\",\"It removes the need for first aid kits\"],\"question\":\"How does detailed reporting help during an emergency response?\",\"questionType\":\"Easy\",\"correctAnswer\":0}]}]', '[{\"id\":1776122922466,\"type\":\"Easy\",\"skill\":\"Memorization\",\"options\":[\"Using an anti-static wrist strap\",\"Working with damaged or exposed wires\",\"Organizing files on the desktop\",\"Cleaning the computer screen with a microfiber cloth\"],\"question\":\"Which of the following is an example of an electric hazard in computer servicing?\",\"questionType\":\"Easy\",\"correctAnswer\":1},{\"id\":1776122922467,\"type\":\"Easy\",\"skill\":\"Memorization\",\"options\":[\"Pull the cord from the wire to save time\",\"Touch equipment with wet hands\",\"Inspect cables before using computers\",\"Open the power supply unit to check for issues\"],\"question\":\"What is a safe practice when dealing with electrical equipment?\",\"questionType\":\"Easy\",\"correctAnswer\":2},{\"id\":1776122922468,\"type\":\"Easy\",\"skill\":\"Problem Solving\",\"options\":[\"Open it to examine the inside\",\"Continue using it until it stops working\",\"Report it and stop using the device\",\"Tap it lightly to make the noise disappear\"],\"question\":\"What should be done when a power supply shows signs of malfunction such as unusual noise?\",\"questionType\":\"Easy\",\"correctAnswer\":2},{\"id\":1776122922487,\"type\":\"Easy\",\"skill\":\"Memorization\",\"options\":[\"Hazards caused by electricity\",\"Situations that can physically harm a person through posture, movement, or surroundings\",\"Threats from computer viruses\",\"Hazards involving chemical substances\"],\"question\":\"What are physical hazards in the workplace?\",\"questionType\":\"Easy\",\"correctAnswer\":1},{\"id\":1776122922488,\"type\":\"Easy\",\"skill\":\"Memorization\",\"options\":[\"Underground outlets\",\"Damaged power supply\",\"Poor workstation setup\",\"Overload extension cords\"],\"question\":\"Which of the following is an example of physical hazard?\",\"questionType\":\"Easy\",\"correctAnswer\":2}]', '[{\"id\":1776122922760,\"type\":\"Easy\",\"skill\":\"Memorization\",\"options\":[\"Using an anti-static wrist strap\",\"Working with damaged or exposed wires\",\"Organizing files on the desktop\",\"Cleaning the computer screen with a microfiber cloth\"],\"question\":\"Which of the following is an example of an electric hazard in computer servicing?\",\"questionType\":\"Easy\",\"correctAnswer\":1},{\"id\":1776122922761,\"type\":\"Easy\",\"skill\":\"Memorization\",\"options\":[\"Pull the cord from the wire to save time\",\"Touch equipment with wet hands\",\"Inspect cables before using computers\",\"Open the power supply unit to check for issues\"],\"question\":\"What is a safe practice when dealing with electrical equipment?\",\"questionType\":\"Easy\",\"correctAnswer\":2},{\"id\":1776122922762,\"type\":\"Easy\",\"skill\":\"Problem Solving\",\"options\":[\"Open it to examine the inside\",\"Continue using it until it stops working\",\"Report it and stop using the device\",\"Tap it lightly to make the noise disappear\"],\"question\":\"What should be done when a power supply shows signs of malfunction such as unusual noise?\",\"questionType\":\"Easy\",\"correctAnswer\":2},{\"id\":1776122922763,\"type\":\"Easy\",\"skill\":\"Memorization\",\"options\":[\"Hazards caused by electricity\",\"Situations that can physically harm a person through posture, movement, or surroundings\",\"Threats from computer viruses\",\"Hazards involving chemical substances\"],\"question\":\"What are physical hazards in the workplace?\",\"questionType\":\"Easy\",\"correctAnswer\":1},{\"id\":1776122922764,\"type\":\"Easy\",\"skill\":\"Memorization\",\"options\":[\"Underground outlets\",\"Damaged power supply\",\"Poor workstation setup\",\"Overload extension cords\"],\"question\":\"Which of the following is an example of physical hazard?\",\"questionType\":\"Easy\",\"correctAnswer\":2},{\"id\":1776122922765,\"type\":\"Easy\",\"skill\":\"Memorization\",\"options\":[\"Faster internet speed\",\"Better airflow\",\"Tripping accidents and equipment damage\",\"Less need for cable management\"],\"question\":\"What can cluttered cables and wires cause?\",\"questionType\":\"Easy\",\"correctAnswer\":2},{\"id\":1776122922766,\"type\":\"Easy\",\"skill\":\"Technical Comprehension\",\"options\":[\"They cause injuries instantly\",\"They only affect computer hardware\",\"They cause injuries slowly over time due to repetitive tasks\",\"They immediately damage equipment\"],\"question\":\"Why are ergonomic hazards dangerous?\",\"questionType\":\"Easy\",\"correctAnswer\":2},{\"id\":1776122922767,\"type\":\"Easy\",\"skill\":\"Memorization\",\"options\":[\"Wet floors\",\"A monitor placed too high or too low\",\"Exposed wires\",\"Overloaded sockets\"],\"question\":\"Which of the following is an example of an ergonomic hazard?\",\"questionType\":\"Easy\",\"correctAnswer\":1},{\"id\":1776122922768,\"type\":\"Easy\",\"skill\":\"Memorization\",\"options\":[\"Undergrounded outlets\",\"Solvents and cleaning sprays\",\"Cluttered cables\",\"Improper lifting of heavy objects\"],\"question\":\"Which of the following is an example of a chemical hazard?\",\"questionType\":\"Easy\",\"correctAnswer\":1},{\"id\":1776122922769,\"type\":\"Easy\",\"skill\":\"Technical Comprehension\",\"options\":[\"They spill easily\",\"They produce toxic fumes when heated\",\"They smell bad\",\"They damage computer keyboards\"],\"question\":\"Why is solder and flux considered hazardous?\",\"questionType\":\"Easy\",\"correctAnswer\":1},{\"id\":1776122922770,\"type\":\"Easy\",\"skill\":\"Memorization\",\"options\":[\"Torx Screwdriver\",\"Wire Stripper\",\"Wire Cutter\",\"Crimping Tool\"],\"question\":\"It is a hand tool designed to precisely remove the insulation from the ends of electrical wires without damaging the conductor inside.\",\"questionType\":\"Easy\",\"correctAnswer\":1},{\"id\":1776122922771,\"type\":\"Easy\",\"skill\":\"Memorization\",\"options\":[\"Phillips Screwdriver\",\"Wire Stripper\",\"Wire Cutter\",\"Crimping Tool\"],\"question\":\"Question: A technician is attaching an RJ-45 connector to a network cable. The wire has already been stripped, and the connector must now be firmly attached by compressing the metal pins onto the wires. Which tool should be used?\",\"questionType\":\"Easy\",\"correctAnswer\":3},{\"id\":1776122922772,\"type\":\"Easy\",\"skill\":\"Memorization\",\"options\":[\"Anti-Static Wrist Strap\",\"LAN Tester\",\"Loopback Adapter\",\"Multimeter\"],\"question\":\"This tool is used to test circuit integrity and a component’s electricity quality.\",\"questionType\":\"Easy\",\"correctAnswer\":3},{\"id\":1776122922773,\"type\":\"Easy\",\"skill\":\"Memorization\",\"options\":[\"Anti-Static Wrist Strap\",\"Lint-Free Cloth\",\"Anti-Static Mat\",\"Cable Ties\"],\"question\":\"This tool is used to put on hardware to prevent static electricity building up.\",\"questionType\":\"Easy\",\"correctAnswer\":0},{\"id\":1776122922774,\"type\":\"Easy\",\"skill\":\"Memorization\",\"options\":[\"Tools are grouped by type\",\"Handles are color-coded\",\"Presence of cracks, rust, or frayed cords\",\"Tools are stored in padded cases\"],\"question\":\"Question: While preparing tools for a servicing task, a technician notices that one tool has rust on its metal surface and the power cord is frayed. What does this indicate about the condition of the tool?\",\"questionType\":\"Easy\",\"correctAnswer\":2},{\"id\":1776122922775,\"type\":\"Easy\",\"skill\":\"Memorization\",\"options\":[\"Hanging all tools on magnetic strips\",\"Keeping compressed air cans near heat sources\",\"Storing sharp tools in sheaths or closed drawers and placing heavier items low\",\"Grouping all tools together in one container\"],\"question\":\"Which storage practice is recommended to ensure safety and prevent injuries when storing computer servicing tools?\",\"questionType\":\"Easy\",\"correctAnswer\":2},{\"id\":1776122922776,\"type\":\"Easy\",\"skill\":\"Memorization\",\"options\":[\"A hazard is a potential source of harm, while an accident is the actual harmful event\",\"A hazard is intentional, while an accident is planned\",\"A hazard causes damage, while an accident does not\",\"A hazard only applies to tools, while accidents apply to people\"],\"question\":\"According to the lesson, what best distinguishes a hazard from an accident?\",\"questionType\":\"Easy\",\"correctAnswer\":0},{\"id\":1776122922777,\"type\":\"Easy\",\"skill\":\"Memorization\",\"options\":[\"It reduces paperwork requirements\",\"It allows immediate corrective actions to prevent recurrence\",\"It replaces the need for tool inspections\",\"It eliminates the use of diagnostic tools\"],\"question\":\"Why is timely reporting of accidents and hazards important for worker safety?\",\"questionType\":\"Easy\",\"correctAnswer\":1},{\"id\":1776122922778,\"type\":\"Easy\",\"skill\":\"Memorization\",\"options\":[\"It allows responders to prepare the correct first aid and medical supplies quickly\",\"It ensures tools are replaced annually\",\"It delays response until management approval\",\"It removes the need for first aid kits\"],\"question\":\"How does detailed reporting help during an emergency response?\",\"questionType\":\"Easy\",\"correctAnswer\":0},{\"id\":1776122922779,\"type\":\"Easy\",\"skill\":\"Memorization\",\"options\":[\"₱20,000 to ₱100,000 per violation plus possible business suspension\",\"₱20,000 to ₱1,000,000 per violation plus possible business suspension\",\"₱10,000 to ₱200,000 per violation\",\"₱75,000 to ₱300,000 per violation plus possible business suspension\"],\"question\":\"Question: A company fails to report a workplace accident to the Department of Labor and Employment using the required reporting form. According to the Occupational Safety and Health Standards, what penalty may the company face for this violation?\",\"questionType\":\"Easy\",\"correctAnswer\":1}]', '[{\"id\":1776122922780,\"type\":\"Situational\",\"skill\":\"Critical Thinking\",\"options\":[\"Using an anti-static wrist strap\",\"Working with damaged or exposed wires\",\"Organizing files on the desktop\",\"Cleaning the computer screen with a microfiber cloth\"],\"question\":\"Question: While repairing a computer, a technician notices that the power cable insulation is broken and the internal wires are exposed. Which situation represents an electrical hazard?\",\"questionType\":\"Situational\",\"correctAnswer\":1},{\"id\":1776122922781,\"type\":\"Situational\",\"skill\":\"Technical Comprehension\",\"options\":[\"Pulling the cord from the wire when unplugging\",\"Touching equipment with wet hands\",\"Inspecting cables before using computers\",\"Opening the power supply unit while it is connected\"],\"question\":\"Question: Before turning on several computers in a laboratory, a technician carefully checks each power cable for visible damage. What safety practice is being applied?\",\"questionType\":\"Situational\",\"correctAnswer\":2},{\"id\":1776122922782,\"type\":\"Situational\",\"skill\":\"Critical Thinking\",\"options\":[\"Opening the device immediately while it is powered on\",\"Continuing to use the computer until it stops working\",\"Stopping use and reporting the issue immediately\",\"Tapping the component to stop the sound\"],\"question\":\"Question: While using a desktop computer, a technician hears unusual buzzing noises from the power supply. What is the safest action to take?\",\"questionType\":\"Situational\",\"correctAnswer\":2},{\"id\":1776122922783,\"type\":\"Situational\",\"skill\":\"Memorization\",\"options\":[\"Hazards caused by computer viruses\",\"Situations that may physically harm a person due to surroundings or posture\",\"Problems related to software malfunction\",\"Hazards involving chemical substances only\"],\"question\":\"Question: A technician frequently bumps into poorly arranged equipment and loose cables while moving around the workstation. What type of hazard is present?\",\"questionType\":\"Situational\",\"correctAnswer\":1},{\"id\":1776122922784,\"type\":\"Situational\",\"skill\":\"Analytical Thinking\",\"options\":[\"Underground power outlets\",\"Damaged computer monitor\",\"Poor workstation setup\",\"Overloaded power strips\"],\"question\":\"Question: After months of working in a poorly arranged workstation with improper chair height and desk alignment, an office worker experiences constant back pain. Which hazard caused this problem?\",\"questionType\":\"Situational\",\"correctAnswer\":2},{\"id\":1776122922785,\"type\":\"Situational\",\"skill\":\"Problem Solving\",\"options\":[\"Faster internet connection\",\"Better cable organization\",\"Tripping accidents and equipment damage\",\"Improved electrical flow\"],\"question\":\"Question: In a computer laboratory, several cables run across the floor without proper management. Students frequently step on them when walking. What risk does this situation create?\",\"questionType\":\"Situational\",\"correctAnswer\":2},{\"id\":1776122922786,\"type\":\"Situational\",\"skill\":\"Analytical Thinking\",\"options\":[\"They cause injuries instantly\",\"They only affect computer hardware\",\"They cause injuries gradually due to repetitive tasks\",\"They make computers malfunction\"],\"question\":\"Question: A programmer types continuously for many hours each day without wrist support or breaks. After several months, wrist pain begins to develop. Why are ergonomic hazards dangerous?\",\"questionType\":\"Situational\",\"correctAnswer\":2},{\"id\":1776122922787,\"type\":\"Situational\",\"skill\":\"Memorization\",\"options\":[\"Wet floor near workstation\",\"A monitor placed too high or too low\",\"Exposed electrical wires\",\"Overloaded electrical sockets\"],\"question\":\"Question: A technician constantly tilts their head upward to see a monitor mounted far above eye level. What hazard does this represent?\",\"questionType\":\"Situational\",\"correctAnswer\":1},{\"id\":1776122922788,\"type\":\"Situational\",\"skill\":\"Memorization\",\"options\":[\"Ungrounded outlets\",\"Solvents and cleaning sprays\",\"Loose network cables\",\"Heavy computer equipment\"],\"question\":\"Question: While cleaning computer components, a technician uses strong chemical sprays in a poorly ventilated room. Which hazard is present?\",\"questionType\":\"Situational\",\"correctAnswer\":1},{\"id\":1776122922789,\"type\":\"Situational\",\"skill\":\"Technical Comprehension\",\"options\":[\"They spill easily\",\"They produce harmful fumes when heated\",\"They damage keyboards\",\"They weaken cables\"],\"question\":\"Question: During motherboard repair, a technician heats solder frequently without ventilation. Why can this be harmful?\",\"questionType\":\"Situational\",\"correctAnswer\":1},{\"id\":1776122922790,\"type\":\"Situational\",\"skill\":\"Problem Solving\",\"options\":[\"Torx screwdriver\",\"Wire stripper\",\"Wire cutter\",\"Crimping tool\"],\"question\":\"Question: A technician needs to expose the copper conductor of a cable without cutting the wire. Which tool should be used?\",\"questionType\":\"Situational\",\"correctAnswer\":1},{\"id\":1776122922791,\"type\":\"Situational\",\"skill\":\"Technical Comprehension\",\"options\":[\"Screwdriver\",\"Crimping tool\",\"Wire stripper\",\"Multimeter\"],\"question\":\"Question: A technician is assembling a network cable and needs to secure the RJ45 connector to the cable. Which tool is required?\",\"questionType\":\"Situational\",\"correctAnswer\":1},{\"id\":1776122922792,\"type\":\"Situational\",\"skill\":\"Analytical Thinking\",\"options\":[\"Prevent electric shock from power outlets\",\"Prevent static electricity from damaging components\",\"Improve computer performance\",\"Clean electronic parts\"],\"question\":\"Question: Before touching the internal components of a computer, a technician connects a wrist strap to the chassis. What is the purpose of this action?\",\"questionType\":\"Situational\",\"correctAnswer\":1},{\"id\":1776122922793,\"type\":\"Situational\",\"skill\":\"Problem Solving\",\"options\":[\"Protect computer hardware\",\"Reduce electrical hazards\",\"Prevent injuries such as back strain\",\"Improve workspace organization\"],\"question\":\"Question: A technician lifts a heavy server incorrectly and later experiences back pain. Why should proper lifting techniques be practiced?\",\"questionType\":\"Situational\",\"correctAnswer\":2},{\"id\":1776122922794,\"type\":\"Situational\",\"skill\":\"Critical Thinking\",\"options\":[\"Improve room ventilation\",\"Prevent cable clutter\",\"Respond quickly to electrical fires\",\"Increase equipment lifespan Reserve Questions : Use only if needed, not required\"],\"question\":\"Question: A technician keeps a fire extinguisher near a workstation where many electronic devices are operating. Why is this important? Reserve Questions : Use only if needed, not required\",\"questionType\":\"Situational\",\"correctAnswer\":2},{\"id\":1776122922820,\"type\":\"Situational\",\"skill\":\"Memorization\",\"options\":[\"Using an anti-static wrist strap\",\"Working with damaged or exposed wires\",\"Organizing files on the desktop\",\"Cleaning the computer screen with a microfiber cloth\"],\"question\":\"Question: While inspecting a workstation, a student observes several conditions. Which situation presents an electrical hazard that must be addressed immediately?\",\"questionType\":\"Situational\",\"correctAnswer\":1},{\"id\":1776122922821,\"type\":\"Situational\",\"skill\":\"Memorization\",\"options\":[\"Pull the cord from the wire to save time\",\"Touch equipment with wet hands\",\"Inspect cables before using computers\",\"Open the power supply unit to check for issues\"],\"question\":\"Before starting a repair, a trainee performs safety checks on a computer setup. Which action reflects proper safety practice?\",\"questionType\":\"Situational\",\"correctAnswer\":2},{\"id\":1776122922822,\"type\":\"Situational\",\"skill\":\"Problem Solving\",\"options\":[\"Open it to examine the inside\",\"Continue using it until it stops working\",\"Report it and stop using the device\",\"Tap it lightly to make the noise disappear\"],\"question\":\"Question: A technician notices a power supply making unusual noises during operation. What is the most appropriate action to ensure safety?\",\"questionType\":\"Situational\",\"correctAnswer\":2},{\"id\":1776122922823,\"type\":\"Situational\",\"skill\":\"Memorization\",\"options\":[\"Hazards caused by electricity\",\"Situations that can physically harm a person through posture, movement, or surroundings\",\"Threats from computer viruses\",\"Hazards involving chemical substances\"],\"question\":\"Question: In a computer laboratory, a student is asked to identify hazards related to movement, posture, and the physical setup of the workspace. What type of hazard is being described?\",\"questionType\":\"Situational\",\"correctAnswer\":1},{\"id\":1776122922824,\"type\":\"Situational\",\"skill\":\"Memorization\",\"options\":[\"Underground outlets\",\"Damaged power supply\",\"Poor workstation setup\",\"Overload extension cords\"],\"question\":\"Question: A student complains of back pain after working long hours in a poorly arranged workstation. Which condition is most likely causing this issue?\",\"questionType\":\"Situational\",\"correctAnswer\":2},{\"id\":1776122922825,\"type\":\"Situational\",\"skill\":\"Memorization\",\"options\":[\"Faster internet speed\",\"Better airflow\",\"Tripping accidents and equipment damage\",\"Less need for cable management\"],\"question\":\"Question: While moving around the lab, a technician trips over several loose cables scattered on the floor. What risk is most associated with this situation?\",\"questionType\":\"Situational\",\"correctAnswer\":2},{\"id\":1776122922826,\"type\":\"Situational\",\"skill\":\"Technical Comprehension\",\"options\":[\"They cause injuries instantly\",\"They only affect computer hardware\",\"They cause injuries slowly over time due to repetitive tasks\",\"They immediately damage equipment\"],\"question\":\"Question: A technician experiences wrist pain after repeatedly performing the same task over long periods without proper posture. Why is this type of hazard dangerous?\",\"questionType\":\"Situational\",\"correctAnswer\":2},{\"id\":1776122922827,\"type\":\"Situational\",\"skill\":\"Memorization\",\"options\":[\"Wet floors\",\"A monitor placed too high or too low\",\"Exposed wires\",\"Overloaded sockets\"],\"question\":\"Question: A student adjusts their workstation and notices discomfort due to improper screen positioning. Which condition represents an ergonomic hazard?\",\"questionType\":\"Situational\",\"correctAnswer\":1},{\"id\":1776122922828,\"type\":\"Situational\",\"skill\":\"Memorization\",\"options\":[\"Undergrounded outlets\",\"Solvents and cleaning sprays\",\"Cluttered cables\",\"Improper lifting of heavy objects\"],\"question\":\"Question: While cleaning computer components, a technician is exposed to substances that may release harmful fumes. Which of the following represents this type of hazard?\",\"questionType\":\"Situational\",\"correctAnswer\":1},{\"id\":1776122922829,\"type\":\"Situational\",\"skill\":\"Technical Comprehension\",\"options\":[\"They spill easily\",\"They produce toxic fumes when heated\",\"They smell bad\",\"They damage computer keyboards\"],\"question\":\"Question: During a repair task involving soldering, a student is advised to work in a well-ventilated area. Why is this precaution necessary?\",\"questionType\":\"Situational\",\"correctAnswer\":1},{\"id\":1776122922830,\"type\":\"Situational\",\"skill\":\"Memorization\",\"options\":[\"Torx Screwdriver\",\"Wire Stripper\",\"Wire Cutter\",\"Crimping Tool\"],\"question\":\"Question: A technician needs to prepare an electrical wire before connecting it to a terminal. The insulation must be removed carefully without damaging the metal conductor inside the wire. Which tool should the technician use?\",\"questionType\":\"Situational\",\"correctAnswer\":1},{\"id\":1776122922831,\"type\":\"Situational\",\"skill\":\"Memorization\",\"options\":[\"Phillips Screwdriver\",\"Wire Stripper\",\"Wire Cutter\",\"Crimping Tool\"],\"question\":\"Question: A technician is attaching an RJ-45 connector to a network cable. The wire has already been stripped, and the connector must now be firmly attached by compressing the metal pins onto the wires. Which tool should be used?\",\"questionType\":\"Situational\",\"correctAnswer\":3},{\"id\":1776122922832,\"type\":\"Situational\",\"skill\":\"Memorization\",\"options\":[\"Anti-Static Wrist Strap\",\"LAN Tester\",\"Loopback Adapter\",\"Multimeter\"],\"question\":\"Question: A technician suspects that a power supply unit is not delivering the correct voltage. To verify the electrical output and check the circuit condition, which tool should be used?\",\"questionType\":\"Situational\",\"correctAnswer\":3},{\"id\":1776122922833,\"type\":\"Situational\",\"skill\":\"Memorization\",\"options\":[\"Anti-Static Wrist Strap\",\"Lint-Free Cloth\",\"Anti-Static Mat\",\"Cable Ties\"],\"question\":\"Question: Before installing sensitive internal components such as RAM and processors, a technician wears a device connected to the computer chassis to prevent electrostatic discharge from damaging the hardware. Which tool is being used?\",\"questionType\":\"Situational\",\"correctAnswer\":0},{\"id\":1776122922834,\"type\":\"Situational\",\"skill\":\"Memorization\",\"options\":[\"Tools are grouped by type\",\"Handles are color-coded\",\"Presence of cracks, rust, or frayed cords\",\"Tools are stored in padded cases\"],\"question\":\"Question: While preparing tools for a servicing task, a technician notices that one tool has rust on its metal surface and the power cord is frayed. What does this indicate about the condition of the tool?\",\"questionType\":\"Situational\",\"correctAnswer\":2},{\"id\":1776122922800,\"type\":\"Easy\",\"skill\":\"Critical Thinking\",\"options\":[\"Using an anti-static wrist strap\",\"Working with damaged or exposed wires\",\"Organizing files on the desktop\",\"Cleaning the computer screen with a microfiber cloth\"],\"question\":\"What is an example of an electrical hazard in computer servicing?\",\"questionType\":\"Easy\",\"correctAnswer\":1},{\"id\":1776122922801,\"type\":\"Easy\",\"skill\":\"Technical Comprehension\",\"options\":[\"Pulling the cord from the wire when unplugging\",\"Touching equipment with wet hands\",\"Inspecting cables before using computers\",\"Opening the power supply unit while it is connected\"],\"question\":\"What is a safe practice when dealing with electrical equipment?\",\"questionType\":\"Easy\",\"correctAnswer\":2},{\"id\":1776122922802,\"type\":\"Easy\",\"skill\":\"Critical Thinking\",\"options\":[\"Opening the device immediately while it is powered on\",\"Continuing to use the computer until it stops working\",\"Stopping use and reporting the issue immediately\",\"Tapping the component to stop the sound\"],\"question\":\"What should be done when a computer component shows signs of malfunction?\",\"questionType\":\"Easy\",\"correctAnswer\":2},{\"id\":1776122922803,\"type\":\"Easy\",\"skill\":\"Memorization\",\"options\":[\"Hazards caused by computer viruses\",\"Situations that may physically harm a person due to surroundings or posture\",\"Problems related to software malfunction\",\"Hazards involving chemical substances only\"],\"question\":\"What are physical hazards in the workplace?\",\"questionType\":\"Easy\",\"correctAnswer\":1},{\"id\":1776122922804,\"type\":\"Easy\",\"skill\":\"Analytical Thinking\",\"options\":[\"Underground power outlets\",\"Damaged computer monitor\",\"Poor workstation setup\",\"Overloaded power strips\"],\"question\":\"Which of the following is an example of a physical hazard in a computer workstation?\",\"questionType\":\"Easy\",\"correctAnswer\":2},{\"id\":1776122922805,\"type\":\"Easy\",\"skill\":\"Problem Solving\",\"options\":[\"Faster internet connection\",\"Better cable organization\",\"Tripping accidents and equipment damage\",\"Improved electrical flow\"],\"question\":\"What can cluttered cables and wires cause in a computer workstation?\",\"questionType\":\"Easy\",\"correctAnswer\":2},{\"id\":1776122922806,\"type\":\"Easy\",\"skill\":\"Analytical Thinking\",\"options\":[\"They cause injuries instantly\",\"They only affect computer hardware\",\"They cause injuries gradually due to repetitive tasks\",\"They make computers malfunction\"],\"question\":\"Why are ergonomic hazards dangerous?\",\"questionType\":\"Easy\",\"correctAnswer\":2},{\"id\":1776122922807,\"type\":\"Easy\",\"skill\":\"Memorization\",\"options\":[\"Wet floor near workstation\",\"A monitor placed too high or too low\",\"Exposed electrical wires\",\"Overloaded electrical sockets\"],\"question\":\"Which of the following is an example of an ergonomic hazard?\",\"questionType\":\"Easy\",\"correctAnswer\":1},{\"id\":1776122922808,\"type\":\"Easy\",\"skill\":\"Memorization\",\"options\":[\"Ungrounded outlets\",\"Solvents and cleaning sprays\",\"Loose network cables\",\"Heavy computer equipment\"],\"question\":\"Which of the following is an example of a chemical hazard?\",\"questionType\":\"Easy\",\"correctAnswer\":1},{\"id\":1776122922809,\"type\":\"Easy\",\"skill\":\"Technical Comprehension\",\"options\":[\"They spill easily\",\"They produce harmful fumes when heated\",\"They damage keyboards\",\"They weaken cables\"],\"question\":\"Why are solder and flux considered hazardous materials?\",\"questionType\":\"Easy\",\"correctAnswer\":1},{\"id\":1776122922810,\"type\":\"Easy\",\"skill\":\"Problem Solving\",\"options\":[\"Torx screwdriver\",\"Wire stripper\",\"Wire cutter\",\"Crimping tool\"],\"question\":\"Which tool is used to remove insulation from electrical wires?\",\"questionType\":\"Easy\",\"correctAnswer\":1},{\"id\":1776122922811,\"type\":\"Easy\",\"skill\":\"Technical Comprehension\",\"options\":[\"Screwdriver\",\"Crimping tool\",\"Wire stripper\",\"Multimeter\"],\"question\":\"Which tool is used to attach connectors to wires by compressing them?\",\"questionType\":\"Easy\",\"correctAnswer\":1},{\"id\":1776122922812,\"type\":\"Easy\",\"skill\":\"Analytical Thinking\",\"options\":[\"Prevent electric shock from power outlets\",\"Prevent static electricity from damaging components\",\"Improve computer performance\",\"Clean electronic parts\"],\"question\":\"Why is an anti-static wrist strap used when servicing computers?\",\"questionType\":\"Easy\",\"correctAnswer\":1},{\"id\":1776122922813,\"type\":\"Easy\",\"skill\":\"Problem Solving\",\"options\":[\"Protect computer hardware\",\"Reduce electrical hazards\",\"Prevent injuries such as back strain\",\"Improve workspace organization\"],\"question\":\"Why is proper lifting technique important when handling computer equipment?\",\"questionType\":\"Easy\",\"correctAnswer\":2},{\"id\":1776122922814,\"type\":\"Easy\",\"skill\":\"Critical Thinking\",\"options\":[\"Improve room ventilation\",\"Prevent cable clutter\",\"Respond quickly to electrical fires\",\"Increase equipment lifespan Reserve Questions : Use only if needed, not required\"],\"question\":\"What is an important safety measure when working with electronic equipment?\",\"questionType\":\"Easy\",\"correctAnswer\":2}]', '{\"hours\":1,\"minutes\":30}', 'Easy', NULL, '[{\"id\":\"introduction\",\"type\":\"introduction\",\"label\":\"Introduction\",\"order\":1},{\"id\":\"diagnostic\",\"type\":\"diagnostic\",\"label\":\"Diagnostic\",\"order\":2},{\"id\":\"lesson\",\"type\":\"lesson\",\"label\":\"Lesson\",\"order\":3},{\"id\":\"final\",\"type\":\"final\",\"label\":\"Final Assessment\",\"order\":4}]');
INSERT INTO `module` (`ModuleID`, `ModuleTitle`, `Description`, `LessonOrder`, `Tesda_Reference`, `Is_Unlocked`, `Is_Completed`, `LessonLanguage`, `Is_Deleted`, `created_at`, `updated_at`, `sections`, `diagnosticQuestions`, `reviewQuestions`, `finalQuestions`, `LessonTime`, `Difficulty`, `finalInstruction`, `roadmapStages`) VALUES
(8, 'Computer and Its Parts', '<div>This lesson introduces learners to the fundamental components that make up a computer system. It explains the purpose and function of each part– both hardware and software–and how they work together to process information.</div><p><br></p><p><br></p><p><strong>Learning Objectives:</strong></p><p>This lesson aims to:</p><p>1. identify and describe the hardware and software of a computer;</p><p>\t\t2. apply basic troubleshooting for common problems encountered; and</p><p>\t\t3. demonstrate proper maintenance and best practices.</p>', 3, '', 0, 0, 'English', 0, '2026-03-10 05:26:12', '2026-06-29 07:55:03', '[{\"id\":1776123188180,\"file\":null,\"type\":\"topic\",\"order\":1,\"title\":\"Topic 1: The Hardware Components of a Computer\",\"caption\":\"\",\"content\":\"\",\"fileName\":null},{\"id\":1777220247001,\"file\":null,\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"order\":2,\"title\":\"\",\"caption\":\"\",\"content\":\"<p>Learning the basics of computers may seem complicated on the inside, but every device—from the smallest smartphone to the largest desktop—relies on the same essential building blocks. These building blocks are called hardware components, the physical parts of a computer that you can see and touch.[1][2]</p>\\n<p>Computer hardware is everything from the central processing unit (CPU) to random access memory (RAM), storage devices (like hard disk drives and solid-state drives), motherboards, power supplies, and input/output devices (such as keyboards, mice, and printers). Each component has a specific function and plays an integral role in the overall performance of the computer.[1][2]</p>\\n<p>Source: https://scot-comp.co.uk/</p>\\n<p>A computer is an electronic device that accepts data, performs operations, displays results, and stores the data or results as needed. It is a combination of hardware and software resources that integrate and provide various functionalities to the user. Hardware is the physical components of a computer, such as a processor, memory devices, monitor, keyboard, etc., while software is a set of programs or instructions that are required by the hardware resources to function properly.[1]</p>\\n<p>In this lesson, you will learn about the different parts and components that make up a desktop computer unit. It is important for us to know the basic parts of the computer hardware, so that you can establish your understanding and keep up for the following lessons in ModuLearn. Along with it, you will learn their functions and parts as well. To further prepare your learning drive, here is an overview of what we will be discussing along the lesson:</p>\\n<p>Central processing unit (CPU) - known as the ‘brain’ of the computer because it executes instructions and carries out commands.[image-33]</p>\\n<p>Motherboard - provides the structure for all other components and connects them, while also providing a way to distribute power, deliver information and connect to devices such as a printer or mouse.[image-34]</p>\\n<p>Random Access Memory (RAM) - is where data lives temporarily while it’s being actively used by programs, such as when a user launches a computer application.[image-35]</p>\",\"fileName\":null,\"tableTitle\":\"\",\"contentLayout\":\"text\"},{\"id\":1777220247002,\"file\":null,\"type\":\"image\",\"order\":3,\"title\":\"The Hardware Components of a Computer\",\"images\":[{\"url\":\"/uploads/lessons/051_computer_hardware_is_everything_from_the.webp\",\"file\":null,\"caption\":\"Computer hardware is everything from the central processing\",\"fileName\":null},{\"url\":\"/uploads/lessons/052_in_this_lesson_you_will_learn_about_the_.webp\",\"file\":null,\"caption\":\"In this lesson\",\"fileName\":null},{\"url\":\"/uploads/lessons/053_central_processing_unit_cpu_known_as_the.webp\",\"file\":null,\"caption\":\"Central processing unit (CPU)\",\"fileName\":null},{\"url\":\"/uploads/lessons/056_storage_devices_an_essential_hardware_th_approx.webp\",\"file\":null,\"caption\":\"Storage Devices\",\"fileName\":null},{\"url\":\"/uploads/lessons/057_graphics_processing_unit_gpu_a_specializ_approx.webp\",\"file\":null,\"caption\":\"Graphics Processing Unit (GPU)\",\"fileName\":null},{\"url\":\"/uploads/lessons/059_cooling_system_a_computer_s_system_to_de_approx.webp\",\"file\":null,\"caption\":\"Cooling System\",\"fileName\":null},{\"url\":\"/uploads/lessons/062_hard_drive_a_data_storage_device_used_to_approx.webp\",\"file\":null,\"caption\":\"Hard drive\",\"fileName\":null},{\"url\":\"/uploads/lessons/063_monitor_an_electronic_device_that_displa_approx.webp\",\"file\":null,\"caption\":\"Monitor\",\"fileName\":null}],\"layout\":\"grid-3\",\"caption\":\"\",\"content\":\"/uploads/lessons/051_computer_hardware_is_everything_from_the.webp\",\"fileName\":null},{\"id\":1776123188209,\"file\":null,\"type\":\"review-multiple-choice\",\"order\":4,\"title\":\"\",\"caption\":\"\",\"content\":\"\",\"fileName\":null,\"questions\":[{\"id\":1776123188207,\"type\":\"Easy\",\"skill\":\"Memorization\",\"options\":[\"RAM\",\"CPU\",\"Motherboard\",\"Hard Drive\"],\"question\":\"Which part of the computer is known as the ‘brain’ of the system?\",\"questionType\":\"Easy\",\"correctAnswer\":1},{\"id\":1776123188208,\"type\":\"Easy\",\"skill\":\"Technical Comprehension\",\"options\":[\"Stores data permanently\",\"Stores temporary data while the computer is running\",\"Processes instructions\",\"Cools the CPU\"],\"question\":\"What is the main function of RAM?\",\"questionType\":\"Easy\",\"correctAnswer\":1}]},{\"id\":1776123188210,\"file\":null,\"type\":\"topic\",\"order\":5,\"title\":\"Topic 2: Central Processing Unit (CPU)\",\"caption\":\"\",\"content\":\"\",\"fileName\":null},{\"id\":1777220247003,\"file\":null,\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"order\":6,\"title\":\"\",\"caption\":\"\",\"content\":\"<p>Do you know that a computer cannot function without a CPU, even if it has a monitor, keyboard, and a mouse? Just like the human brain, the CPU controls all the activities of the computer. Without it, the system cannot think, calculate, or respond.</p>\\n<p>In computer hardware servicing, knowing how the CPU works is essential for installation, troubleshooting, upgrading, and maintenance.        This is the main processing component of a computer. It executes instructions from programs and controls all hardware operations.[3]</p>\\n<p>Arithmetic/Logic Unit</p>\\n<p>This part of the CPU is responsible for doing calculations and making decisions based on comparisons. Its math functionality is based on four types of operations (addition, subtraction, multiplication and division). Logical operations typically involve some type of comparison (checking whether something is greater than, less than, or equal to something else) that is tied to a particular computer action.[3][4] In simple terms, the ALU is the “calculator and decision maker” of the CPU.</p>\\n<p>Control Unit (CU)</p>\\n<p>The Control Unit acts like a manager or traffic controller inside the CPU. The control unit of the CPU houses circuitry (electronic pathways that allow electricity to move and control components) that guides the computer system through a system of electrical pulses (tiny bursts of electrical signals used to send instructions) and notifies it to execute high-level computer instructions (commands given by programs or software).[3][4] Simply put, the CU tells all the other parts of the computer what to do and when to do it.</p>\\n<p>Memory Unit</p>\\n<p>The Memory Unit is responsible for handling data and instructions while the CPU is working. It handles several key functions related to memory usage, from managing the data flow (movement of information) that occurs between RAM and the CPU to overseeing the important work of the cache memory (a small, very fast memory used to store frequently used data). Memory units contain all types of data and instructions needed for data processing (handling and organizing information) and offer memory-protection safeguards (features that prevent programs from interfering with each other’s data).[3][4] In simple terms, the Memory Unit keeps important data ready so the CPU can use it quickly and safely.</p>\",\"fileName\":null,\"tableTitle\":\"\",\"contentLayout\":\"text\"},{\"id\":1776123188311,\"file\":null,\"type\":\"video\",\"order\":7,\"title\":\"\",\"caption\":\"Lesson 3 CPU Video\",\"content\":\"https://www.dropbox.com/scl/fi/8rmvptztbdqs9g6a689we/Lesson-3-Topic-1-CPU.mp4?rlkey=ujw4423z4xfgh6lv7zwfbpmd1&st=m45e58vs&dl=0\",\"fileName\":null},{\"id\":1776123188214,\"file\":null,\"type\":\"review-multiple-choice\",\"order\":8,\"title\":\"\",\"caption\":\"\",\"content\":\"\",\"fileName\":null,\"questions\":[{\"id\":1776123188212,\"type\":\"Easy\",\"skill\":\"Technical Comprehension\",\"options\":[\"Control Unit\",\"Memory Unit\",\"Arithmetic/Logic Unit\",\"Register\"],\"question\":\"Which part of the CPU is responsible for arithmetic and logical operations?\",\"questionType\":\"Easy\",\"correctAnswer\":2},{\"id\":1776123188213,\"type\":\"Easy\",\"skill\":\"Technical Comprehension\",\"options\":[\"Cache\",\"Register\",\"Bus\",\"Clock\"],\"question\":\"What CPU component stores data that needs to be accessed immediately?\",\"questionType\":\"Easy\",\"correctAnswer\":1}]},{\"id\":1776123188215,\"file\":null,\"type\":\"topic\",\"order\":9,\"title\":\"Topic 3: Motherboard\",\"caption\":\"\",\"content\":\"\",\"fileName\":null},{\"id\":1777220247004,\"file\":null,\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"order\":10,\"title\":\"\",\"caption\":\"\",\"content\":\"<p>If the CPU is the brain, the motherboard is the body’s nervous system. Without it, the computer’s parts cannot communicate or function together. It is also called the mainboard or system board, it is the main circuit board of a computer. It connects, controls, and allows communication among all major hardware components such as the CPU, RAM, storage devices, and peripherals.[5]</p>\\n<p>A motherboard is easily identified, as it is the largest board inside a computer’s casing. In tower computer’s, it stands vertically on the tower’s left or right side. While motherboards come in a variety of types and sizes– each designed to be placed in a different kind of computer and to work with different types of processors and memory– they all have the same basic components. The base of any motherboard is made of a hard sheet of nonconductive material, usually plastic.[6]</p>\\n<p>When you turn your computer on, the power supply transfers electricity to the motherboard to be used by the computer. Data is transported between the chipset components via data buses and travels between the southbridge and northbridge sections.</p>\\n<p>The data connections to the CPU, RAM, or PCIe are made through the northbridge component. The operations performed by the RAM are first “interpreted” by the CPU as being output after the RAM begins to deliver inputs to the CPU. After being written to the PCIe, the data is either copied or moved to the expansion card, based on the kind of card you have.</p>\\n<p>The data connection to the basic input/output system (BIOS), the universal serial bus (USB), the serial advanced technology attachment (SATA), and the PCI bus are managed by the southbridge component. Your computer can start up because of signals sent to the BIOS, and the data sent to the SATA “awakens” your optical, hard disc, and solid-state drives. The video card, network card, and sound card receive power from the information stored on the SATA.</p>\\n<p>The remaining components interact via an electrical signal, which serves as a hub for them. These data buses pass via a microchip’s northbridge or southbridge elements, which then branch off to other components like the CPU, RAM, PCI, and PCIe, amongst other elements.</p>\\n<p>The information sent over buses will be encoded using a programming language (1 and 0). When a signal is sent to a motherboard from one of its components, the motherboard will process it and translate it into a language the other component can comprehend. On most of today’s computing systems, all of this will occur in a split second, and there is almost no delay between the input and the output.[5]</p>\\n<p>Connectivity - refers to the motherboard’s ability to link all major computer components so they can communicate and work together. It connects the CPU (the computer’s main processor), RAM (temporary working memory), storage devices like SSDs/HDDs (where files are permanently stored), the GPU (graphics processor), and peripherals (devices like keyboard and mouse). The motherboard acts as the central hub where all these parts exchange information.</p>\",\"fileName\":null,\"tableTitle\":\"\",\"contentLayout\":\"text\"},{\"id\":1776123188309,\"file\":null,\"type\":\"video\",\"order\":11,\"title\":\"\",\"caption\":\"Lesson 3 Motherboard Video\",\"content\":\"https://www.dropbox.com/scl/fi/8199jhk8dcan8c460jxcv/Lesson-3-Topic-1-Motherboard.mp4?rlkey=osshw5z07qcpykhtt40cayohg&st=4vgafh3c&dl=0\",\"fileName\":null},{\"id\":1776123188218,\"file\":null,\"type\":\"review-multiple-choice\",\"order\":12,\"title\":\"\",\"caption\":\"\",\"content\":\"\",\"fileName\":null,\"questions\":[{\"id\":1776123188217,\"type\":\"Easy\",\"skill\":\"Memorization\",\"options\":[\"RAM\",\"BIOS/UEFI\",\"PCIe slot\",\"Power supply\"],\"question\":\"Which motherboard component stores startup instructions that allow the computer to boot?\",\"questionType\":\"Easy\",\"correctAnswer\":1}]},{\"id\":1776123188219,\"file\":null,\"type\":\"topic\",\"order\":13,\"title\":\"Topic 4: RAM\",\"caption\":\"\",\"content\":\"\",\"fileName\":null},{\"id\":1777220247005,\"file\":null,\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"order\":14,\"title\":\"\",\"caption\":\"\",\"content\":\"<p>Every time you open an app, browse the web, or run a program, the Random Access Memory (RAM) is working behind the scenes to keep everything fast and smooth.</p>\\n<p>Think of RAM as your computer’s short-term brain—the more brain power it has, the better it can think, remember, and multitask!</p>\\n<p>Random Access Memory (RAM) is one of the most important components in Computer Hardware Servicing (CHS) because it directly affects a computer’s speed and overall performance. RAM serves as the computer’s temporary working memory, where data and programs that are currently in use are stored, so the processor can access them quickly. When a computer is powered on, the operating system and active applications are loaded into RAM, allowing tasks such as opening files, browsing the internet, and running software to be performed smoothly. However, once the computer is shut down, all data stored in RAM is erased, which is why it is referred to as volatile memory.[7]</p>\\n<p>In practical terms, RAM can be compared to a study desk: the larger the desk, the more books and materials can be opened at the same time without clutter. Similarly, a computer with higher RAM capacity can run multiple applications simultaneously with less lag or freezing. RAM works much faster than storage devices such as hard disk drives (HDDs) or solid-state drives (SSDs), which are used for long-term data storage. While storage keeps files permanently, RAM focuses on speed and efficiency, ensuring that the CPU can quickly retrieve the information it needs to perform tasks.[7]</p>\\n<p>Dynamic Random Access Memory (DRAM) - is typically used for a computer’s main memory. It needs continuous power to retain stored data. DRAM is cheaper than Static Random Access Memory (SRAM), has a higher density, but it produces more heat, consumes more power and is not as fast as SRAM. Each DRAM cell stores a positive or negative charge held in an electrical capacitor. This data must be constantly refreshed with an electronic charge every few milliseconds to compensate for leaks from the capacitor. A transistor serves as a gate, determining whether a capacitor’s value can be read or written.</p>\\n<p>Double Data Rate (DDR) - The first generation, released around 2000, offering twice the bandwidth of SDRAM by transferring data on both clock edges, operating at ~2.5V.</p>\\n<p>DDR2 (2nd Generation) - Faster bus speeds than DDR1, lower voltage (1.8V), and a 4n prefetch buffer, released around 2003.</p>\\n<p>DDR3 (3rd Generation) - Focused on power efficiency with lower voltage (1.5V/1.35V), higher clock speeds (800-2133 MHz), and a larger 8n prefetch buffer, released around 2007.</p>\",\"fileName\":null,\"tableTitle\":\"\",\"contentLayout\":\"text\"},{\"id\":1776123188307,\"file\":null,\"type\":\"video\",\"order\":15,\"title\":\"\",\"caption\":\"Lesson 3 RAM Video\",\"content\":\"https://www.dropbox.com/scl/fi/xi1pkxtei70e1m3groiqw/Lesson-3-Topic-1-RAM.mp4?rlkey=628yw9mbwzr23yxcx4irdrb2c&st=et28s5h0&dl=0\",\"fileName\":null},{\"id\":1776123188222,\"file\":null,\"type\":\"review-multiple-choice\",\"order\":16,\"title\":\"\",\"caption\":\"\",\"content\":\"\",\"fileName\":null,\"questions\":[{\"id\":1776123188221,\"type\":\"Easy\",\"skill\":\"Analytical Thinking\",\"options\":[\"It consumes a large amount of power\",\"It overheats easily\",\"Data stored in it is erased when the computer is turned off\",\"It refreshes data automatically\"],\"question\":\"Why is RAM referred to as volatile memory?\",\"questionType\":\"Easy\",\"correctAnswer\":2}]},{\"id\":1776123188223,\"file\":null,\"type\":\"topic\",\"order\":17,\"title\":\"Topic 5: Storage Devices\",\"caption\":\"\",\"content\":\"\",\"fileName\":null},{\"id\":1777220247006,\"file\":null,\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"order\":18,\"title\":\"\",\"caption\":\"\",\"content\":\"<p>Where does a computer save files? The answer is storage devices. These components store the operating system, applications, and user data, making them essential to computer operations. You will learn different types of storage devices, how they work, and their role in Computer Hardware Servicing.[11] You will also gain basic skills in identifying, installing, and maintaining storage devices–important tasks.</p>\\n<p>Computer storage devices, classified as primary (temporary) or secondary (persistent), are essential hardware components that retain data, instructions, and information. The primary, most common devices are Hard Disk Drives (HDDs) for large capacity and Solid-State Drives (SSDs) for high-speed, durable storage. Other forms include USB flash drives, memory cards, optical discs (CD/DVD), and cloud storage.[12][13]</p>\\n<p>While it may at first seem like the range of storage options available to you is vast, they largely fall under three main categories:</p>\\n<p>Internal physical storage on your computer—your computer’s built-in storage space, often referred to as its hard drive.</p>\\n<p>External physical storage devices—similar to the memory built into your computer, only you can remove it and connect it to another device.</p>\\n<p>Cloud storage—platforms like Google Drive allow you to store files over the internet, rather than on physical storage, meaning any compatible device with an internet connection can access the files.[13]</p>\\n<p>To help you to understand which type of storage is right for your needs, let’s dive into each in a little more detail and walk through some examples.</p>\\n<p>This ultimately refers to your device’s built-in memory. Most computers and handheld devices will come with some degree of internal storage. It’s also common to be able to choose how much internal storage you want when buying a laptop, for example.</p>\",\"fileName\":null,\"tableTitle\":\"\",\"contentLayout\":\"text\"},{\"id\":1776123188306,\"file\":null,\"type\":\"video\",\"order\":19,\"title\":\"\",\"caption\":\"Lesson 3 Storage Video\",\"content\":\"https://www.dropbox.com/scl/fi/4fcxtt2ddpw8oc5k5mgcb/Lesson-3-Topic-1-Storage.mp4?rlkey=hewjpgu1k8etnnfvfnrzx3plu&st=21rtv163&dl=0\",\"fileName\":null},{\"id\":1776123188233,\"file\":null,\"type\":\"review-multiple-choice\",\"order\":20,\"title\":\"\",\"caption\":\"\",\"content\":\"\",\"fileName\":null,\"questions\":[{\"id\":1776123188231,\"type\":\"Easy\",\"skill\":\"Memorization\",\"options\":[\"To process and render images, videos, and graphics efficiently\",\"To store files and data\",\"To manage network connections\",\"To control input from devices like keyboard and mouse\"],\"question\":\"What is the primary role of a GPU?\",\"questionType\":\"Easy\",\"correctAnswer\":0},{\"id\":1776123188232,\"type\":\"Easy\",\"skill\":\"Critical Thinking\",\"options\":[\"Stores files\",\"Processes CPU\",\"Supplies stable power\",\"Controls cooling\"],\"question\":\"Why is PSU called the “heart”?\",\"questionType\":\"Easy\",\"correctAnswer\":2}]},{\"id\":1776123188234,\"file\":null,\"type\":\"topic\",\"order\":21,\"title\":\"Topic 6: GPU\",\"caption\":\"\",\"content\":\"\",\"fileName\":null},{\"id\":1777220247007,\"file\":null,\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"order\":22,\"title\":\"\",\"caption\":\"\",\"content\":\"<p>A Graphics Processing Unit (GPU) is a specialized electronic circuit designed to rapidly process and render images, videos, and 3D animations by executing parallel mathematical calculations. Often referred to as a graphics card, video card, or visual processing unit, it offloads tasks from the CPU to accelerate gaming, video editing, and AI workloads. It is important because it enhances display performance, supports high-resolution monitors, and accelerates demanding applications such as simulations, multimedia editing, and even modern tasks like artificial intelligence and data processing.[16][17]</p>\\n<p>A GPU has its own random access memory (RAM), an electronic memory used to store code and data that the chip can access and alter as needed. Advanced GPUs typically have RAM that has been built to hold the large data volumes required for compute-intensive tasks such as graphics editing, gaming or AI/ML use cases.</p>\\n<p>Discrete GPUs - Discrete GPUs, or dGPUs, are graphics processors that are separate from a device\'s CPU, where information is taken in and processed, allowing a computer to function. Discrete GPUs are typically used in advanced applications with special requirements, such as editing, content creation or high-end gaming. They are distinct chips with connectors to separate circuit boards and attached to the CPU by using an express slot.</p>\\n<p>One of the most widely used discrete GPUs is the Intel Arc brand, built for the PC gaming industry.</p>\\n<p>Integrated GPUs - An integrated GPU, or iGPU, is built into a computer or device\'s infrastructure and typically slotted in next to the CPU. Designed in the 2010s by Intel, integrated GPUs became more popular as manufacturers such as MSI, ASUS and Nvidia noticed the power of combining GPUs with CPUs rather than requiring users to add GPUs by a PCI express slot themselves. They remain a popular choice for laptop users, gamers and others who are running compute-intensive programs on their PCs.</p>\\n<p>Virtual GPUs - Virtual GPUs, or vGPUs, have the same capabilities as discrete or integrated GPUs but without the hardware. They are software-based versions of GPUs built for cloud instances and can be used to run the same workloads. Also, because they have no hardware, they are simpler and cheaper to maintain than their physical counterparts.[17]</p>\\n<p>What problem in a computer usually causes poor graphics performance in games?</p>\\n<p>a. Storage issue</p>\",\"fileName\":null,\"tableTitle\":\"\",\"contentLayout\":\"text\"},{\"id\":1776123188310,\"file\":null,\"type\":\"video\",\"order\":23,\"title\":\"\",\"caption\":\"Lesson 3 GPU Video\",\"content\":\"https://www.dropbox.com/scl/fi/wey9a8q3bx12llq5gcvn4/Lesson-3-Topic-1-GPU.mp4?rlkey=o4tfq4j89bs4u42ol6y85vhg2&st=59hbppsb&dl=0\",\"fileName\":null},{\"id\":1776123188238,\"file\":null,\"type\":\"review-multiple-choice\",\"order\":24,\"title\":\"\",\"caption\":\"\",\"content\":\"\",\"fileName\":null,\"questions\":[{\"id\":1776123188236,\"type\":\"Easy\",\"skill\":\"Memorization\",\"options\":[\"Switching power supply\",\"Linear power supply\",\"Battery\",\"External\"],\"question\":\"Which type of power supply is MOST commonly used?\",\"questionType\":\"Easy\",\"correctAnswer\":0},{\"id\":1776123188237,\"type\":\"Easy\",\"skill\":\"Technical Comprehension\",\"options\":[\"Keyboard\",\"Monitor\",\"CPU, GPU, power supply, motherboard\",\"Flash drive\"],\"question\":\"Which components generate heat?\",\"questionType\":\"Easy\",\"correctAnswer\":2}]},{\"id\":1776123188239,\"file\":null,\"type\":\"topic\",\"order\":25,\"title\":\"Topic 7: Power Supply\",\"caption\":\"\",\"content\":\"\",\"fileName\":null},{\"id\":1777220247008,\"file\":null,\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"order\":26,\"title\":\"\",\"caption\":\"\",\"content\":\"<p>In the world of building and upgrading PCs, one component that often doesn\'t get the spotlight it deserves is the PSU. In fact, when people think of powerful PCs, they often focus on the GPU or CPU. However, without a reliable PSU, even the best PC components can fail. The PSU is like the heart of your computer, pumping power to every component. A bad PSU can lead to system instability, crashes, and even hardware damage.</p>\\n<p>A computer power supply unit (PSU) is an internal hardware component that converts high-voltage alternating current (AC) from a wall outlet into low-voltage direct current (DC) necessary for components like the motherboard, CPU, and graphics card. It acts as the heart of the computer, providing stable, regulated power to ensure safe and reliable operation.[18][19]</p>\\n<p>AC to DC Conversion: at first step PSU intake the alternating current (AC) from the standard electrical outlet which is different for different. The standard electrical voltage in the Philippines is 220 volts (V) with a frequency of 60 hertz (Hz), then further, this alternating current (AC) is passed through a transformer to step it up or down according to the requirement, transformer make the current ready for the upcoming step.</p>\\n<p>Rectification: The process of rectification is based on the concept that current flows only in positive direction in a diode, in the process power supply uses the rectifiers (diodes) to convert the alternating current into vibrating direct current. The whole process is called rectification.</p>\\n<p>Smoothing: The current prepared by rectification is a vibrating direct current , which is not suitable for directly powering the computer components. Capacitors are used for making the vibrating direct current smooth which make the direct current even more suitable for the powering of the computer components.</p>\\n<p>Voltage Regulation: Despite passing through the process of smoothing, there may still have some fluctuations. Voltage regulators are installed to ensure a steady and precise output voltage. The function of this circuit is to adjust the voltage in order to meet the specifications required by the electronic components. The voltage is basically around 3v -12v depending on specific requirements of electronic components.</p>\\n<p>Output: At last, the regulated direct current (DC) voltage is then supplied according to the requirement to all components of the electronic device like motherboard, hard drives, graphics cards and so on, the output voltage or power is provided to different parts of the device using different connectors and cables.[19]</p>\\n<p>Linear Power Supply - it regulates the output voltage by dissipating the excess electrical energy as heat using simple electronic components. Because it does not use complex switching, its design is straightforward, making it reliable and easy to maintain. However, this simplicity comes at the cost of efficiency–linear PSUs tend to waste more energy and generate more heat compared to other designs. They are typically found in low-powered or specialized systems where stable, low-noise power is more important than efficiency.[18]</p>\",\"fileName\":null,\"tableTitle\":\"\",\"contentLayout\":\"text\"},{\"id\":1776123188308,\"file\":null,\"type\":\"video\",\"order\":27,\"title\":\"\",\"caption\":\"Lesson 3 PSU Video\",\"content\":\"https://www.dropbox.com/scl/fi/79gttebuedkew38twuj72/Lesson-3-Topic-1-PSU.mp4?rlkey=66t6wqdjuhx8h5eq13s2bbj28&st=kkd5neqf&dl=0\",\"fileName\":null},{\"id\":1776123188243,\"file\":null,\"type\":\"review-multiple-choice\",\"order\":28,\"title\":\"\",\"caption\":\"\",\"content\":\"\",\"fileName\":null,\"questions\":[{\"id\":1776123188241,\"type\":\"Easy\",\"skill\":\"Memorization\",\"options\":[\"Display\",\"Store\",\"Send data to computer\",\"Supply power\"],\"question\":\"Function of input device?\",\"questionType\":\"Easy\",\"correctAnswer\":2},{\"id\":1776123188242,\"type\":\"Easy\",\"skill\":\"Memorization\",\"options\":[\"Convert processed data into human-readable form\",\"Enter data\",\"Store data\",\"Control system\"],\"question\":\"Function of output device?\",\"questionType\":\"Easy\",\"correctAnswer\":0}]},{\"id\":1776123188244,\"file\":null,\"type\":\"topic\",\"order\":29,\"title\":\"Topic 8: Cooling System\",\"caption\":\"\",\"content\":\"\",\"fileName\":null},{\"id\":1777220247009,\"file\":null,\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"order\":30,\"title\":\"\",\"caption\":\"\",\"content\":\"<p>A cooling system in a computer is a set of hardware components designed to control and reduce the heat generated by internal parts such as the CPU, GPU, power supply, and motherboard during operation. As these components work, they produce heat, and without proper cooling, excessive temperatures can cause performance throttling, system instability, or permanent hardware damage. The cooling system helps maintain safe operating temperatures so the computer can run efficiently and reliably.[20]</p>\\n<p>Fans - The most popular type of cooling for computers is spinning fans that blow hot air away from the PC’s components and draw in cool air. Fans are extremely popular for consumer-grade PCs, but they have several disadvantages. They can easily spread dust and microbes in their operating environment. This makes them unsuitable for any workspace that requires cleanliness, such as hospitals or clean rooms. Additionally, the constant spinning of their fans can cause reliability issues; a broken fan can easily lead to the overheating issues we’ve previously discussed. Lastly, the continuous noise of their spinning can be distracting or uncomfortable for people nearby, such as patients trying to sleep. For these reasons, cooling fans are not an ideal solution in the medical or industrial sector.[21]</p>\\n<p>Liquid cooling - It works on a similar principle to air cooling, but with liquid as the medium. A liquid cooling system mounts directly onto the heat source, such as the CPU, and uses a heatsink to transfer heat from the processor to the liquid. The liquid is then pumped away from the heatsink, cooled, and pumped back to the heatsink in a continuous cycle. While extremely effective, liquid cooling has several notable downsides. First, it is the most expensive of all cooling options. Second, it requires very specialized equipment that takes up lots of space inside the PC, which is a serious issue for roles that require a smaller form factor. Lastly, liquid cooling systems require periodic maintenance for their numerous moving parts and can be very delicate, which makes them a poor fit for any application requiring ruggedness. For these reasons, liquid cooling is typically only seen in dedicated computing roles, such as for dedicated servers or high-end gaming PCs.[20][21]</p>\\n<p>Fanless cooling - Also known as radiative cooling, fanless cooling relies on heatsinks and radiation fans to disperse heat from the processors and into the air. A heatsink is attached to the heat source, draws heat from it, and radiates it into the surrounding air. These heatsinks are designed with as much surface area as possible and can radiate large amounts of heat despite being comparatively small. The greatest advantage of fanless cooling over other options is that it requires no moving parts and doesn’t consume electricity to do its job. For these reasons, fanless cooling is extremely popular for industrial-grade computers that need to be as rugged and simple as possible to work on or near heavy machinery. Their lack of moving parts also makes computers with fanless cooling nearly silent during operations, meaning they’re more comfortable to be around for long periods of time. Fanless cooling systems also don’t need holes in the computer’s casing to vent air through, meaning that it’s easier to make the case watertight. These factors are invaluable for medical computers, which operate for hours on end next to patients and must be frequently cleaned and disinfected.[21]</p>\\n<p>Airflow within a computer case is essential for maintaining an optimal operating environment for the system’s components. Properly managed airflow not only helps in keeping components cool but also enhances the longevity and performance of the system.</p>\\n<p>Temperature Control: Modern computer components, especially CPUs and GPUs, generate significant amounts of heat. Without effective airflow, this heat can accumulate, causing components to throttle or even fail.</p>\\n<p>System Longevity: Excessive temperatures can shorten the lifespan of computer parts. Maintaining a cooler internal environment can prolong the operational life of these components.</p>\\n<p>Performance: Many computer components will throttle, or reduce their performance, when they get too hot. Efficient airflow ensures that components stay cool and can operate at their maximum capability.[32]</p>\",\"fileName\":null,\"tableTitle\":\"\",\"contentLayout\":\"text\"},{\"id\":1776123188312,\"file\":null,\"type\":\"video\",\"order\":31,\"title\":\"\",\"caption\":\"Lesson 3 Cooling Video\",\"content\":\"https://www.dropbox.com/scl/fi/imcz9hagea0aokee9nctx/Lesson-3-Topic-1-Cooling.mp4?rlkey=nddqtbc0e1d7rp2pydt00s9zs&st=vlyyhq0c&dl=0\",\"fileName\":null},{\"id\":1776123188248,\"file\":null,\"type\":\"review-multiple-choice\",\"order\":32,\"title\":\"\",\"caption\":\"\",\"content\":\"\",\"fileName\":null,\"questions\":[{\"id\":1776123188246,\"type\":\"Easy\",\"skill\":\"Technical Comprehension\",\"options\":[\"Arithmetic device\",\"Core component\",\"Connected device adding functionality\",\"Software\"],\"question\":\"What is a peripheral device?\",\"questionType\":\"Easy\",\"correctAnswer\":2},{\"id\":1776123188247,\"type\":\"Easy\",\"skill\":\"Analytical Thinking\",\"options\":[\"Keyboard\",\"Printer\",\"Monitor\",\"CPU\"],\"question\":\"Which of the following is NOT considered a peripheral device?\",\"questionType\":\"Easy\",\"correctAnswer\":3}]},{\"id\":1776123188249,\"file\":null,\"type\":\"topic\",\"order\":33,\"title\":\"Topic 9: Input Devices\",\"caption\":\"\",\"content\":\"\",\"fileName\":null},{\"id\":1777220247010,\"file\":null,\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"order\":34,\"title\":\"\",\"caption\":\"\",\"content\":\"<p>Input devices are hardware peripherals that send data, commands, and control signals to a computer, allowing users to interact with and operate it. They convert physical input (keystrokes, mouse clicks, voice) into machine-readable digital signals.[23]</p>\\n<p>The main purpose of an input device is to serve as a bridge between the user and the computer, which it achieves through several key functions:</p>\\n<p>Data Input: Input devices transform real-world input, like keystrokes or scanned images, into digital data that a computer can process.</p>\\n<p>Command Execution: They let users control the computer, such as opening applications, selecting options, or navigating menus.</p>\\n<p>User Interface Interaction: Input devices enable engagement with graphical interfaces, allowing users to point, click, type, or gesture to interact with software effectively.[22][23]</p>\\n<p>Keyboard - The most widely used input device, designed for entering text, numbers, and commands. It includes alphanumeric keys, function keys, control keys, and special keys.[image-46]</p>\\n<p>Mouse - A pointing device that allows users to move the cursor, select items, click buttons, and navigate graphical user interfaces (GUI) efficiently.[image-47]</p>\\n<p>Joystick - Used mainly for gaming and simulations, allowing directional control of objects or characters on the screen.[image-48]</p>\",\"fileName\":null,\"tableTitle\":\"\",\"contentLayout\":\"text\"},{\"id\":1777220247011,\"file\":null,\"type\":\"image\",\"order\":35,\"title\":\"Image 64\",\"images\":[{\"url\":\"/uploads/lessons/064_image_approx.webp\",\"file\":null,\"caption\":\"Image 64\",\"fileName\":null}],\"layout\":\"text-left\",\"caption\":\"\",\"content\":\"/uploads/lessons/064_image_approx.webp\",\"fileName\":null,\"sideTexts\":[\"<p><strong>Image 64</strong></p>\"],\"layerImages\":[[{\"url\":\"/uploads/lessons/064_image_approx.webp\",\"file\":null,\"caption\":\"Image 64\",\"fileName\":null}]]},{\"id\":1777220247012,\"file\":null,\"type\":\"image\",\"order\":36,\"title\":\"Keyboard\",\"images\":[{\"url\":\"/uploads/lessons/065_keyboard_the_most_widely_used_input_devi.webp\",\"file\":null,\"caption\":\"Keyboard\",\"fileName\":null}],\"layout\":\"text-left\",\"caption\":\"\",\"content\":\"/uploads/lessons/065_keyboard_the_most_widely_used_input_devi.webp\",\"fileName\":null,\"sideTexts\":[\"<p><strong>Keyboard</strong></p><p>Keyboard - The most widely used input device, designed for entering text,…</p>\"],\"layerImages\":[[{\"url\":\"/uploads/lessons/065_keyboard_the_most_widely_used_input_devi.webp\",\"file\":null,\"caption\":\"Keyboard\",\"fileName\":null}]]},{\"id\":1777220247013,\"file\":null,\"type\":\"image\",\"order\":37,\"title\":\"Mouse\",\"images\":[{\"url\":\"/uploads/lessons/066_mouse_a_pointing_device_that_allows_user_approx.webp\",\"file\":null,\"caption\":\"Mouse\",\"fileName\":null}],\"layout\":\"text-left\",\"caption\":\"\",\"content\":\"/uploads/lessons/066_mouse_a_pointing_device_that_allows_user_approx.webp\",\"fileName\":null,\"sideTexts\":[\"<p><strong>Mouse</strong></p><p>Mouse - A pointing device that allows users to move the cursor, select items,…</p>\"],\"layerImages\":[[{\"url\":\"/uploads/lessons/066_mouse_a_pointing_device_that_allows_user_approx.webp\",\"file\":null,\"caption\":\"Mouse\",\"fileName\":null}]]},{\"id\":1777220247014,\"file\":null,\"type\":\"image\",\"order\":38,\"title\":\"Joystick\",\"images\":[{\"url\":\"/uploads/lessons/067_joystick_used_mainly_for_gaming_and_simu_approx.webp\",\"file\":null,\"caption\":\"Joystick\",\"fileName\":null}],\"layout\":\"text-left\",\"caption\":\"\",\"content\":\"/uploads/lessons/067_joystick_used_mainly_for_gaming_and_simu_approx.webp\",\"fileName\":null,\"sideTexts\":[\"<p><strong>Joystick</strong></p><p>Joystick - Used mainly for gaming and simulations, allowing directional control…</p>\"],\"layerImages\":[[{\"url\":\"/uploads/lessons/067_joystick_used_mainly_for_gaming_and_simu_approx.webp\",\"file\":null,\"caption\":\"Joystick\",\"fileName\":null}]]},{\"id\":1777220247015,\"file\":null,\"type\":\"image\",\"order\":39,\"title\":\"Light Pen\",\"images\":[{\"url\":\"/uploads/lessons/068_light_pen_a_pen_shaped_input_device_that_approx.webp\",\"file\":null,\"caption\":\"Light Pen\",\"fileName\":null}],\"layout\":\"text-left\",\"caption\":\"\",\"content\":\"/uploads/lessons/068_light_pen_a_pen_shaped_input_device_that_approx.webp\",\"fileName\":null,\"sideTexts\":[\"<p><strong>Light Pen</strong></p><p>Light Pen - A pen-shaped input device that enables the user to select or draw…</p>\"],\"layerImages\":[[{\"url\":\"/uploads/lessons/068_light_pen_a_pen_shaped_input_device_that_approx.webp\",\"file\":null,\"caption\":\"Light Pen\",\"fileName\":null}]]},{\"id\":1777220247016,\"file\":null,\"type\":\"image\",\"order\":40,\"title\":\"Scanner\",\"images\":[{\"url\":\"/uploads/lessons/070_scanner_converts_printed_documents_image_approx.webp\",\"file\":null,\"caption\":\"Scanner\",\"fileName\":null}],\"layout\":\"text-left\",\"caption\":\"\",\"content\":\"/uploads/lessons/070_scanner_converts_printed_documents_image_approx.webp\",\"fileName\":null,\"sideTexts\":[\"<p><strong>Scanner</strong></p><p>Scanner - Converts printed documents, images, and photos into digital format,…</p>\"],\"layerImages\":[[{\"url\":\"/uploads/lessons/070_scanner_converts_printed_documents_image_approx.webp\",\"file\":null,\"caption\":\"Scanner\",\"fileName\":null}]]},{\"id\":1776123188265,\"file\":null,\"type\":\"review-multiple-choice\",\"order\":41,\"title\":\"\",\"caption\":\"\",\"content\":\"\",\"fileName\":null,\"questions\":[{\"id\":1776123188263,\"type\":\"Easy\",\"skill\":\"Memorization\",\"options\":[\"HDMI\",\"Ethernet\",\"USB\",\"VGA\"],\"question\":\"Which connection type is MOST commonly used for keyboards, mice, and printers?\",\"questionType\":\"Easy\",\"correctAnswer\":2},{\"id\":1776123188264,\"type\":\"Easy\",\"skill\":\"Technical Comprehension\",\"options\":[\"Store data permanently\",\"Process information\",\"Connect external devices and enable data transfer and communication\",\"Cool components\"],\"question\":\"What is the main function of computer ports?\",\"questionType\":\"Easy\",\"correctAnswer\":2}]},{\"id\":1776123188266,\"file\":null,\"type\":\"topic\",\"order\":42,\"title\":\"Topic 10: Output Devices\",\"caption\":\"\",\"content\":\"\",\"fileName\":null},{\"id\":1777220247017,\"file\":null,\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"order\":43,\"title\":\"\",\"caption\":\"\",\"content\":\"<p>An output device is any computer hardware component that receives processed data from a computer and translates it into a form that is perceivable by humans, such as visual (screens), auditory (speakers), or physical (printed). These devices represent the final step in the information processing cycle, converting digital information into user-readable output.</p>\\n<p>Output devices are essential components of a computer system that deliver processed data to the user in a human-readable form—be it visual, auditory, or physical. If input devices are how a computer receives information (like typing or clicking), output devices are how it responds or communicates back.[24]</p>\\n<p>An output device is hardware that takes processed digital data from a computer and converts it into a form humans can perceive or use.</p>\\n<p>Data Processing – The computer’s CPU processes information and prepares it for output.</p>\\n<p>Signal Transmission – The processed data is sent as digital signals to the output device through an interface.</p>\\n<p>Conversion – The output device converts these digital signals into a human-perceivable form.</p>\\n<p>Presentation – The information is presented so the user can interpret or use it.[25]</p>\\n<p>Input (data entry) → Processing (CPU) → Output (results via output devices)</p>\",\"fileName\":null,\"tableTitle\":\"\",\"contentLayout\":\"text\"},{\"id\":1777220247018,\"file\":null,\"type\":\"image\",\"order\":44,\"title\":\"Monitor\",\"images\":[{\"url\":\"/uploads/lessons/072_monitor_a_device_that_displays_visual_in.webp\",\"file\":null,\"caption\":\"Monitor\",\"fileName\":null}],\"layout\":\"text-left\",\"caption\":\"\",\"content\":\"/uploads/lessons/072_monitor_a_device_that_displays_visual_in.webp\",\"fileName\":null,\"sideTexts\":[\"<p><strong>Monitor</strong></p><p>Monitor - A device that displays visual information such as text and graphics…</p>\"],\"layerImages\":[[{\"url\":\"/uploads/lessons/072_monitor_a_device_that_displays_visual_in.webp\",\"file\":null,\"caption\":\"Monitor\",\"fileName\":null}]]},{\"id\":1777220247019,\"file\":null,\"type\":\"image\",\"order\":45,\"title\":\"Speaker\",\"images\":[{\"url\":\"/uploads/lessons/073_speaker_a_device_that_converts_digital_a_approx.webp\",\"file\":null,\"caption\":\"Speaker\",\"fileName\":null}],\"layout\":\"text-left\",\"caption\":\"\",\"content\":\"/uploads/lessons/073_speaker_a_device_that_converts_digital_a_approx.webp\",\"fileName\":null,\"sideTexts\":[\"<p><strong>Speaker</strong></p><p>Speaker - A device that converts digital audio signals from the computer into…</p>\"],\"layerImages\":[[{\"url\":\"/uploads/lessons/073_speaker_a_device_that_converts_digital_a_approx.webp\",\"file\":null,\"caption\":\"Speaker\",\"fileName\":null}]]},{\"id\":1777220247020,\"file\":null,\"type\":\"image\",\"order\":46,\"title\":\"Projector\",\"images\":[{\"url\":\"/uploads/lessons/074_projector_a_device_that_takes_visual_inf_approx.webp\",\"file\":null,\"caption\":\"Projector\",\"fileName\":null}],\"layout\":\"text-left\",\"caption\":\"\",\"content\":\"/uploads/lessons/074_projector_a_device_that_takes_visual_inf_approx.webp\",\"fileName\":null,\"sideTexts\":[\"<p><strong>Projector</strong></p><p>Projector - A device that takes visual information from a computer and displays…</p>\"],\"layerImages\":[[{\"url\":\"/uploads/lessons/074_projector_a_device_that_takes_visual_inf_approx.webp\",\"file\":null,\"caption\":\"Projector\",\"fileName\":null}]]},{\"id\":1776123188275,\"file\":null,\"type\":\"review-multiple-choice\",\"order\":47,\"title\":\"\",\"caption\":\"\",\"content\":\"\",\"fileName\":null,\"questions\":[{\"id\":1776123188273,\"type\":\"Easy\",\"skill\":\"Memorization\",\"options\":[\"Modem port\",\"Ethernet port\",\"FireWire port\",\"Infrared port\"],\"question\":\"Which port is primarily used to connect a computer to a local area network (LAN) or the internet?\",\"questionType\":\"Easy\",\"correctAnswer\":1},{\"id\":1776123188274,\"type\":\"Easy\",\"skill\":\"Technical Comprehension\",\"options\":[\"Serial (COM) port\",\"Parallel port\",\"USB port\",\"Ethernet port\"],\"question\":\"Which port transmits data one bit at a time and is mostly considered a legacy port today?\",\"questionType\":\"Easy\",\"correctAnswer\":0}]},{\"id\":1776123188276,\"file\":null,\"type\":\"topic\",\"order\":48,\"title\":\"Topic 11: Peripheral Devices\",\"caption\":\"\",\"content\":\"\",\"fileName\":null},{\"id\":1777220247021,\"file\":null,\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"order\":49,\"title\":\"\",\"caption\":\"\",\"content\":\"<p>A peripheral device is defined as a computer device, such as a keyboard or printer, that is not part of the essential computer (i.e., the memory and microprocessor). These auxiliary devices are intended to be connected to the computer and used. Any various devices (including sensors) used to enter information and instructions into a computer for storage or processing and to deliver the processed data to a human operator or, in some cases, a machine controlled by the computer. Such devices make up the peripheral equipment of modern digital computer systems.[27][28]</p>\\n<p>Peripheral devices are important for enhancing functionality of a computer. Here\'s why peripheral devices are so important:</p>\\n<p>Enhanced Functionality: Peripheral devices expand a computer\'s capabilities, enabling it to perform various tasks.</p>\\n<p>User Interaction: Input devices like keyboards and mice allow users to control and interact with the system.</p>\\n<p>Data Output: Output devices such as monitors and printers display or present processed data.</p>\\n<p>Data Storage: Storage devices ensure important data is saved and can be accessed or backed up when needed.</p>\\n<p>Communication: Communication devices enable network connectivity, allowing the computer to communicate with other systems or networks.</p>\\n<p>Increased Efficiency: Peripherals improve the overall efficiency and usability of the computer by adding specialized functions.[29]</p>\",\"fileName\":null,\"tableTitle\":\"\",\"contentLayout\":\"text\"},{\"id\":1777220247022,\"file\":null,\"type\":\"image\",\"order\":50,\"title\":\"Peripheral devices can connect to a computer through various\",\"images\":[{\"url\":\"/uploads/lessons/075_peripheral_devices_can_connect_to_a_comp_approx.webp\",\"file\":null,\"caption\":\"Peripheral devices can connect to a computer through various\",\"fileName\":null}],\"layout\":\"text-left\",\"caption\":\"\",\"content\":\"/uploads/lessons/075_peripheral_devices_can_connect_to_a_comp_approx.webp\",\"fileName\":null,\"sideTexts\":[\"<p><strong>Peripheral devices can connect to a computer through various</strong></p><p>Peripheral devices can connect to a computer through various methods. Each…</p>\"],\"layerImages\":[[{\"url\":\"/uploads/lessons/075_peripheral_devices_can_connect_to_a_comp_approx.webp\",\"file\":null,\"caption\":\"Peripheral devices can connect to a computer through various\",\"fileName\":null}]]},{\"id\":1777220247023,\"file\":null,\"type\":\"image\",\"order\":51,\"title\":\"Wi-Fi: Wi-Fi is used for wireless networked devices like pri\",\"images\":[{\"url\":\"/uploads/lessons/076_wi_fi_wi_fi_is_used_for_wireless_network_approx.webp\",\"file\":null,\"caption\":\"Wi-Fi: Wi-Fi is used for wireless networked devices like pri\",\"fileName\":null}],\"layout\":\"text-left\",\"caption\":\"\",\"content\":\"/uploads/lessons/076_wi_fi_wi_fi_is_used_for_wireless_network_approx.webp\",\"fileName\":null,\"sideTexts\":[\"<p><strong>Wi-Fi: Wi-Fi is used for wireless networked devices like pri</strong></p><p>Wi-Fi: Wi-Fi is used for wireless networked devices like printers and cameras.</p>\"],\"layerImages\":[[{\"url\":\"/uploads/lessons/076_wi_fi_wi_fi_is_used_for_wireless_network_approx.webp\",\"file\":null,\"caption\":\"Wi-Fi: Wi-Fi is used for wireless networked devices like pri\",\"fileName\":null}]]},{\"id\":1777220247024,\"file\":null,\"type\":\"image\",\"order\":52,\"title\":\"HDMI: HDMI connects monitors\",\"images\":[{\"url\":\"/uploads/lessons/077_hdmi_hdmi_connects_monitors_projectors_a_approx.webp\",\"file\":null,\"caption\":\"HDMI: HDMI connects monitors\",\"fileName\":null}],\"layout\":\"text-left\",\"caption\":\"\",\"content\":\"/uploads/lessons/077_hdmi_hdmi_connects_monitors_projectors_a_approx.webp\",\"fileName\":null,\"sideTexts\":[\"<p><strong>HDMI: HDMI connects monitors</strong></p><p>HDMI: HDMI connects monitors, projectors, and TVs for high-definition video and…</p>\"],\"layerImages\":[[{\"url\":\"/uploads/lessons/077_hdmi_hdmi_connects_monitors_projectors_a_approx.webp\",\"file\":null,\"caption\":\"HDMI: HDMI connects monitors\",\"fileName\":null}]]},{\"id\":1777220247025,\"file\":null,\"type\":\"image\",\"order\":53,\"title\":\"Ethernet: Wired connection for network communication\",\"images\":[{\"url\":\"/uploads/lessons/078_ethernet_wired_connection_for_network_co_approx.webp\",\"file\":null,\"caption\":\"Ethernet: Wired connection for network communication\",\"fileName\":null}],\"layout\":\"text-left\",\"caption\":\"\",\"content\":\"/uploads/lessons/078_ethernet_wired_connection_for_network_co_approx.webp\",\"fileName\":null,\"sideTexts\":[\"<p><strong>Ethernet: Wired connection for network communication</strong></p><p>Ethernet: Wired connection for network communication, often for internet or LAN…</p>\"],\"layerImages\":[[{\"url\":\"/uploads/lessons/078_ethernet_wired_connection_for_network_co_approx.webp\",\"file\":null,\"caption\":\"Ethernet: Wired connection for network communication\",\"fileName\":null}]]},{\"id\":1777220247026,\"file\":null,\"type\":\"image\",\"order\":54,\"title\":\"External port\",\"images\":[{\"url\":\"/uploads/lessons/080_parallel_port_crop.webp\",\"file\":null,\"caption\":\"External port\",\"fileName\":null}],\"layout\":\"text-left\",\"caption\":\"\",\"content\":\"/uploads/lessons/080_parallel_port_crop.webp\",\"fileName\":null,\"sideTexts\":[\"<p><strong>External port</strong></p><p>External port - External ports are used to connect external devices: modem,…</p>\"],\"layerImages\":[[{\"url\":\"/uploads/lessons/080_parallel_port_crop.webp\",\"file\":null,\"caption\":\"External port\",\"fileName\":null}]]},{\"id\":1777220247027,\"file\":null,\"type\":\"image\",\"order\":55,\"title\":\"Sockets\",\"images\":[{\"url\":\"/uploads/lessons/087_sockets_interface_points_used_to_connect_approx.webp\",\"file\":null,\"caption\":\"Sockets\",\"fileName\":null}],\"layout\":\"text-left\",\"caption\":\"\",\"content\":\"/uploads/lessons/087_sockets_interface_points_used_to_connect_approx.webp\",\"file