\"Monitor\",\"Printer\",\"Keyboard\",\"Speaker\"],\"question\":\"Which of the following devices is an input device?\",\"questionType\":\"Easy\",\"correctAnswer\":2}]}]', '[{\"id\":1776123188207,\"skill\":\"Memorization\",\"options\":[\"RAM\",\"CPU\",\"Motherboard\",\"Hard Drive\"],\"question\":\"Which part of the computer is known as the ‘brain’ of the system?\",\"questionType\":\"Easy\",\"correctAnswer\":1},{\"id\":1776123188208,\"skill\":\"Technical Comprehension\",\"options\":[\"Stores data permanently\",\"Stores temporary data while the computer is running\",\"Processes instructions\",\"Cools the CPU\"],\"question\":\"What is the main function of RAM?\",\"questionType\":\"Easy\",\"correctAnswer\":1},{\"id\":1776123188212,\"skill\":\"Technical Comprehension\",\"options\":[\"Control Unit\",\"Memory Unit\",\"Arithmetic/Logic Unit\",\"Register\"],\"question\":\"Which part of the CPU is responsible for arithmetic and logical operations?\",\"questionType\":\"Easy\",\"correctAnswer\":2},{\"id\":1776123188213,\"skill\":\"Technical Comprehension\",\"options\":[\"Cache\",\"Register\",\"Bus\",\"Clock\"],\"question\":\"What CPU component stores data that needs to be accessed immediately?\",\"questionType\":\"Easy\",\"correctAnswer\":1},{\"id\":1776123188217,\"skill\":\"Memorization\",\"options\":[\"RAM\",\"BIOS/UEFI\",\"PCIe slot\",\"Power supply\"],\"question\":\"Which motherboard component stores startup instructions that allow the computer to boot?\",\"questionType\":\"Easy\",\"correctAnswer\":1}]', '[{\"id\":1776123188387,\"type\":\"Easy\",\"skill\":\"Memorization\",\"options\":[\"RAM\",\"CPU\",\"Motherboard\",\"Hard Drive\"],\"question\":\"Which part of the computer is known as the ‘brain’ of the system?\",\"questionType\":\"Easy\",\"correctAnswer\":1},{\"id\":1776123188388,\"type\":\"Easy\",\"skill\":\"Technical Comprehension\",\"options\":[\"Stores data permanently\",\"Stores temporary data while the computer is running\",\"Processes instructions\",\"Cools the CPU\"],\"question\":\"What is the main function of RAM?\",\"questionType\":\"Easy\",\"correctAnswer\":1},{\"id\":1776123188389,\"type\":\"Easy\",\"skill\":\"Technical Comprehension\",\"options\":[\"Control Unit\",\"Memory Unit\",\"Arithmetic/Logic Unit\",\"Register\"],\"question\":\"Which part of the CPU is responsible for arithmetic and logical operations?\",\"questionType\":\"Easy\",\"correctAnswer\":2},{\"id\":1776123188390,\"type\":\"Easy\",\"skill\":\"Technical Comprehension\",\"options\":[\"Cache\",\"Register\",\"Bus\",\"Clock\"],\"question\":\"What CPU component stores data that needs to be accessed immediately?\",\"questionType\":\"Easy\",\"correctAnswer\":1},{\"id\":1776123188391,\"type\":\"Easy\",\"skill\":\"Memorization\",\"options\":[\"RAM\",\"BIOS/UEFI\",\"PCIe slot\",\"Power supply\"],\"question\":\"Which motherboard component stores startup instructions that allow the computer to boot?\",\"questionType\":\"Easy\",\"correctAnswer\":1},{\"id\":1776123188392,\"type\":\"Easy\",\"skill\":\"Analytical Thinking\",\"options\":[\"It consumes a large amount of power\",\"It overheats easily\",\"Data stored in it is erased when the computer is turned off\",\"It refreshes data automatically\"],\"question\":\"Why is RAM referred to as volatile memory?\",\"questionType\":\"Easy\",\"correctAnswer\":2},{\"id\":1776123188393,\"type\":\"Easy\",\"skill\":\"Memorization\",\"options\":[\"To process and render images, videos, and graphics efficiently\",\"To store files and data\",\"To manage network connections\",\"To control input from devices like keyboard and mouse\"],\"question\":\"What is the primary role of a GPU?\",\"questionType\":\"Easy\",\"correctAnswer\":0},{\"id\":1776123188394,\"type\":\"Easy\",\"skill\":\"Critical Thinking\",\"options\":[\"Stores files\",\"Processes CPU\",\"Supplies stable power\",\"Controls cooling\"],\"question\":\"Why is PSU called the “heart”?\",\"questionType\":\"Easy\",\"correctAnswer\":2},{\"id\":1776123188395,\"type\":\"Easy\",\"skill\":\"Memorization\",\"options\":[\"Switching power supply\",\"Linear power supply\",\"Battery\",\"External\"],\"question\":\"Which type of power supply is MOST commonly used?\",\"questionType\":\"Easy\",\"correctAnswer\":0},{\"id\":1776123188396,\"type\":\"Easy\",\"skill\":\"Technical Comprehension\",\"options\":[\"Keyboard\",\"Monitor\",\"CPU, GPU, power supply, motherboard\",\"Flash drive\"],\"question\":\"Which components generate heat?\",\"questionType\":\"Easy\",\"correctAnswer\":2},{\"id\":1776123188397,\"type\":\"Easy\",\"skill\":\"Memorization\",\"options\":[\"Display\",\"Store\",\"Send data to computer\",\"Supply power\"],\"question\":\"Function of input device?\",\"questionType\":\"Easy\",\"correctAnswer\":2},{\"id\":1776123188398,\"type\":\"Easy\",\"skill\":\"Memorization\",\"options\":[\"Convert processed data into human-readable form\",\"Enter data\",\"Store data\",\"Control system\"],\"question\":\"Function of output device?\",\"questionType\":\"Easy\",\"correctAnswer\":0},{\"id\":1776123188399,\"type\":\"Easy\",\"skill\":\"Technical Comprehension\",\"options\":[\"Arithmetic device\",\"Core component\",\"Connected device adding functionality\",\"Software\"],\"question\":\"What is a peripheral device?\",\"questionType\":\"Easy\",\"correctAnswer\":2},{\"id\":1776123188400,\"type\":\"Easy\",\"skill\":\"Analytical Thinking\",\"options\":[\"Keyboard\",\"Printer\",\"Monitor\",\"CPU\"],\"question\":\"Which of the following is NOT considered a peripheral device?\",\"questionType\":\"Easy\",\"correctAnswer\":3},{\"id\":1776123188401,\"type\":\"Easy\",\"skill\":\"Memorization\",\"options\":[\"HDMI\",\"Ethernet\",\"USB\",\"VGA\"],\"question\":\"Which connection type is MOST commonly used for keyboards, mice, and printers?\",\"questionType\":\"Easy\",\"correctAnswer\":2},{\"id\":1776123188402,\"type\":\"Easy\",\"skill\":\"Technical Comprehension\",\"options\":[\"Store data permanently\",\"Process information\",\"Connect external devices and enable data transfer and communication\",\"Cool components\"],\"question\":\"What is the main function of computer ports?\",\"questionType\":\"Easy\",\"correctAnswer\":2},{\"id\":1776123188403,\"type\":\"Easy\",\"skill\":\"Memorization\",\"options\":[\"Modem port\",\"Ethernet port\",\"FireWire port\",\"Infrared port\"],\"question\":\"Which port is primarily used to connect a computer to a local area network (LAN) or the internet?\",\"questionType\":\"Easy\",\"correctAnswer\":1},{\"id\":1776123188404,\"type\":\"Easy\",\"skill\":\"Technical Comprehension\",\"options\":[\"Serial (COM) port\",\"Parallel port\",\"USB port\",\"Ethernet port\"],\"question\":\"Which port transmits data one bit at a time and is mostly considered a legacy port today?\",\"questionType\":\"Easy\",\"correctAnswer\":0},{\"id\":1776123188405,\"type\":\"Easy\",\"skill\":\"Memorization\",\"options\":[\"Monitor\",\"Printer\",\"Keyboard\",\"Speaker\"],\"question\":\"Which of the following devices is an input device?\",\"questionType\":\"Easy\",\"correctAnswer\":2},{\"id\":1776123188406,\"type\":\"Easy\",\"skill\":\"Technical Comprehension\",\"options\":[\"HDDs use flash memory\",\"SSDs are slower\",\"SSDs have no moving parts and are faster than HDDs\",\"HDDs are more durable\"],\"question\":\"What is the key difference between HDD and SSD?\",\"questionType\":\"Easy\",\"correctAnswer\":2}]', '[{\"id\":1776123188407,\"type\":\"Situational\",\"skill\":\"Memorization\",\"options\":[\"Power System Unit\",\"Primary Supply Utility\",\"Power Supply Unit\",\"Processing Support Unit\"],\"question\":\"Question: A technician installs a component that distributes electrical power to all internal parts of a computer. What is this component called?\",\"questionType\":\"Situational\",\"correctAnswer\":2},{\"id\":1776123188408,\"type\":\"Situational\",\"skill\":\"Memorization\",\"options\":[\"SSD\",\"HDD\",\"Flash Drive\",\"Cloud Storage\"],\"question\":\"Question: A technician explains that a storage device reads and writes data using rotating disks and magnetic heads. Which device is being described?\",\"questionType\":\"Situational\",\"correctAnswer\":1},{\"id\":1776123188409,\"type\":\"Situational\",\"skill\":\"Memorization\",\"options\":[\"VGA\",\"USB\",\"Serial\",\"HDMI\"],\"question\":\"Question: A user connects input devices using a universal plug-and-play interface found on most modern computers. Which port is this?\",\"questionType\":\"Situational\",\"correctAnswer\":1},{\"id\":1776123188410,\"type\":\"Situational\",\"skill\":\"Technical Comprehension\",\"options\":[\"It stores memory\",\"It connects and allows communication between components\",\"It cools the CPU\",\"It powers peripherals\"],\"question\":\"Question: A technician explains that one component links all parts together and allows communication between them. Which function is being described?\",\"questionType\":\"Situational\",\"correctAnswer\":1},{\"id\":1776123188411,\"type\":\"Situational\",\"skill\":\"Technical Comprehension\",\"options\":[\"Increase storage\",\"Reduce heat and prevent damage\",\"Improve internet speed\",\"Store BIOS\"],\"question\":\"Question: A computer shuts down due to overheating, so a technician installs a system to regulate temperature and protect components. What is its purpose?\",\"questionType\":\"Situational\",\"correctAnswer\":1},{\"id\":1776123188412,\"type\":\"Situational\",\"skill\":\"Analytical Thinking\",\"options\":[\"Cheaper only\",\"More efficient and produces less heat\",\"Larger in size\",\"Uses more electricity\"],\"question\":\"Question: A technician chooses a power supply that wastes less energy and produces minimal heat during operation. Why is this type preferred?\",\"questionType\":\"Situational\",\"correctAnswer\":1},{\"id\":1776123188413,\"type\":\"Situational\",\"skill\":\"Memorization\",\"options\":[\"HDD\",\"SSD\",\"DVD\",\"Floppy Disk\"],\"question\":\"Question: A user upgrades storage to improve speed and reliability by choosing a device with no moving parts. Which is the best option?\",\"questionType\":\"Situational\",\"correctAnswer\":1},{\"id\":1776123188414,\"type\":\"Situational\",\"skill\":\"Technical Comprehension\",\"options\":[\"Execute–Decode–Fetch\",\"Fetch–Decode–Execute\",\"Store–Execute–Fetch\",\"Decode–Execute–Store\"],\"question\":\"Question: A student studies how the CPU handles instructions in sequence—first retrieving, then interpreting, and finally performing them. What is the correct order?\",\"questionType\":\"Situational\",\"correctAnswer\":1},{\"id\":1776123188415,\"type\":\"Situational\",\"skill\":\"Problem Solving\",\"options\":[\"GPU\",\"Keyboard\",\"Mouse\",\"Speaker\"],\"question\":\"Question: A computer powers on, but nothing appears on the screen. The technician suspects a component responsible for visual output. Which should be checked?\",\"questionType\":\"Situational\",\"correctAnswer\":0},{\"id\":1776123188416,\"type\":\"Situational\",\"skill\":\"Memorization\",\"options\":[\"Fan-based\",\"Liquid cooling\",\"Fanless cooling\",\"Hybrid cooling\"],\"question\":\"Question: A technician installs a silent cooling solution that does not rely on fans or pumps. Which type is this?\",\"questionType\":\"Situational\",\"correctAnswer\":2},{\"id\":1776123188417,\"type\":\"Situational\",\"skill\":\"Problem Solving\",\"options\":[\"Add fan\",\"Replace SSD with HDD\",\"Upgrade to SSD\",\"Change keyboard\"],\"question\":\"Question: A technician suggests replacing a slow storage device with one that significantly improves startup speed and system responsiveness. What is the best upgrade?\",\"questionType\":\"Situational\",\"correctAnswer\":2},{\"id\":1776123188418,\"type\":\"Situational\",\"skill\":\"Problem Solving\",\"options\":[\"RAM\",\"PSU\",\"Monitor\",\"GPU\"],\"question\":\"Question: A system shows no signs of power when the button is pressed. A technician begins troubleshooting the component responsible for supplying electricity. What should be checked first?\",\"questionType\":\"Situational\",\"correctAnswer\":1},{\"id\":1776123188419,\"type\":\"Situational\",\"skill\":\"Analytical Thinking\",\"options\":[\"SSD\",\"HDD\",\"RAM\",\"Cache\"],\"question\":\"Question: A user needs to store large amounts of data cheaply and does not require high speed. Which storage option is most suitable?\",\"questionType\":\"Situational\",\"correctAnswer\":1},{\"id\":1776123188420,\"type\":\"Situational\",\"skill\":\"Technical Comprehension\",\"options\":[\"Stores data temporarily\",\"Requires no internet\",\"Provides remote access and backup\",\"Replaces RAM\"],\"question\":\"Question: A user accesses files from different devices and locations while keeping backups online. What advantage of storage is being used?\",\"questionType\":\"Situational\",\"correctAnswer\":2},{\"id\":1776123188421,\"type\":\"Situational\",\"skill\":\"Critical Thinking\",\"options\":[\"Fanless\",\"Liquid cooling\",\"No cooling\",\"VGA cooling\"],\"question\":\"Question: A gamer runs high-end applications that generate significant heat and needs an efficient cooling solution for stable performance. Which is the best choice? EXCESS ITEMS (CAN BE USED IF NEEDED)\",\"questionType\":\"Situational\",\"correctAnswer\":1},{\"id\":1776123188441,\"type\":\"Situational\",\"skill\":\"Memorization\",\"options\":[\"RAM\",\"CPU\",\"Motherboard\",\"Hard Drive\"],\"question\":\"Question: A technician explains that the component responsible for executing instructions and controlling all computer operations is often called the “brain.” Which component is this?\",\"questionType\":\"Situational\",\"correctAnswer\":1},{\"id\":1776123188442,\"type\":\"Situational\",\"skill\":\"Technical Comprehension\",\"options\":[\"Stores data permanently\",\"Stores temporary data while the computer is running\",\"Processes instructions\",\"Cools the CPU\"],\"question\":\"Question: While using multiple applications, a computer temporarily holds active data so programs can run efficiently. Which function is being described?\",\"questionType\":\"Situational\",\"correctAnswer\":1},{\"id\":1776123188443,\"type\":\"Situational\",\"skill\":\"Technical Comprehension\",\"options\":[\"Control Unit\",\"Memory Unit\",\"Arithmetic/Logic Unit\",\"Register\"],\"question\":\"Question: During processing, a component performs calculations like addition and comparison. Which unit is responsible?\",\"questionType\":\"Situational\",\"correctAnswer\":2},{\"id\":1776123188444,\"type\":\"Situational\",\"skill\":\"Technical Comprehension\",\"options\":[\"Cache\",\"Register\",\"Bus\",\"Clock\"],\"question\":\"The processor needs ultra-fast access to small amounts of critical data during execution. Which component handles this?\",\"questionType\":\"Situational\",\"correctAnswer\":1},{\"id\":1776123188445,\"type\":\"Situational\",\"skill\":\"Memorization\",\"options\":[\"RAM\",\"BIOS/UEFI\",\"PCIe slot\",\"Power supply\"],\"question\":\"Question: When a computer is powered on, firmware initializes hardware and starts the system. Which component contains this firmware?\",\"questionType\":\"Situational\",\"correctAnswer\":1},{\"id\":1776123188446,\"type\":\"Situational\",\"skill\":\"Analytical Thinking\",\"options\":[\"It consumes a large amount of power\",\"It overheats easily\",\"Data stored in it is erased when the computer is turned off\",\"It refreshes data automatically\"],\"question\":\"Question: A user loses unsaved work after a sudden shutdown. What characteristic of RAM explains this?\",\"questionType\":\"Situational\",\"correctAnswer\":2},{\"id\":1776123188447,\"type\":\"Situational\",\"skill\":\"Memorization\",\"options\":[\"To process and render images, videos, and graphics efficiently\",\"To store files and data\",\"To manage network connections\",\"To control input from devices like keyboard and mouse\"],\"question\":\"Question: A gamer wants smooth graphics rendering while playing high-resolution games. In order to achieve it, the user needs to have the GPU in his computer setup. What is the function of the component?\",\"questionType\":\"Situational\",\"correctAnswer\":0},{\"id\":1776123188448,\"type\":\"Situational\",\"skill\":\"Critical Thinking\",\"options\":[\"Stores files\",\"Processes CPU\",\"Supplies stable power\",\"Controls cooling\"],\"question\":\"Question: A new computer user sets up his computer setup for the first time. However, when he tries to turn on the computer, it won’t turn on. Turns out, he lacks the PSU component. What does the PSU’s function based on the situation?\",\"questionType\":\"Situational\",\"correctAnswer\":2},{\"id\":1776123188449,\"type\":\"Situational\",\"skill\":\"Memorization\",\"options\":[\"Switching power supply\",\"Linear power supply\",\"Battery\",\"External\"],\"question\":\"Question: A technician selects a power supply known for high efficiency and reduced heat output. Which type is this?\",\"questionType\":\"Situational\",\"correctAnswer\":0},{\"id\":1776123188450,\"type\":\"Situational\",\"skill\":\"Technical Comprehension\",\"options\":[\"Keyboard\",\"Monitor\",\"CPU, GPU, power supply, motherboard\",\"Flash drive\"],\"question\":\"Question: A technician installs cooling systems for parts that produce heat during operation. Which are these?\",\"questionType\":\"Situational\",\"correctAnswer\":2},{\"id\":1776123188451,\"type\":\"Situational\",\"skill\":\"Memorization\",\"options\":[\"Display\",\"Store\",\"Send data to computer\",\"Supply power\"],\"question\":\"Question: A user sends commands into a system using hardware. What is this function?\",\"questionType\":\"Situational\",\"correctAnswer\":2},{\"id\":1776123188452,\"type\":\"Situational\",\"skill\":\"Memorization\",\"options\":[\"Convert processed data into human-readable form\",\"Enter data\",\"Store data\",\"Control system\"],\"question\":\"Question: A monitor shows processed results to the user. What function is this?\",\"questionType\":\"Situational\",\"correctAnswer\":0},{\"id\":1776123188453,\"type\":\"Situational\",\"skill\":\"Technical Comprehension\",\"options\":[\"Arithmetic device\",\"Core component\",\"Connected device adding functionality\",\"Software\"],\"question\":\"Question: A device is connected externally to add functionality. What is it classified as?\",\"questionType\":\"Situational\",\"correctAnswer\":2},{\"id\":1776123188454,\"type\":\"Situational\",\"skill\":\"Analytical Thinking\",\"options\":[\"Keyboard\",\"Printer\",\"Monitor\",\"CPU\"],\"question\":\"Question: A technician is identifying which component is part of the core internal system rather than an external or add-on device. Which one is NOT a peripheral?\",\"questionType\":\"Situational\",\"correctAnswer\":3},{\"id\":1776123188455,\"type\":\"Situational\",\"skill\":\"Memorization\",\"options\":[\"HDMI\",\"Ethernet\",\"USB\",\"VGA\"],\"question\":\"Question: A user connects a keyboard and mouse to a computer using a widely supported plug-and-play interface. Which connection type is being used?\",\"questionType\":\"Situational\",\"correctAnswer\":2},{\"id\":1776123188424,\"type\":\"Easy\",\"skill\":\"Memorization\",\"options\":[\"Power System Unit\",\"Primary Supply Utility\",\"Power Supply Unit\",\"Processing Support Unit\"],\"question\":\"What does PSU stand for?\",\"questionType\":\"Easy\",\"correctAnswer\":2},{\"id\":1776123188425,\"type\":\"Easy\",\"skill\":\"Memorization\",\"options\":[\"SSD\",\"HDD\",\"Flash Drive\",\"Cloud Storage\"],\"question\":\"Which storage device uses spinning magnetic platters?\",\"questionType\":\"Easy\",\"correctAnswer\":1},{\"id\":1776123188426,\"type\":\"Easy\",\"skill\":\"Memorization\",\"options\":[\"VGA\",\"USB\",\"Serial\",\"HDMI\"],\"question\":\"Which port is most commonly used today for keyboards and mice?\",\"questionType\":\"Easy\",\"correctAnswer\":1},{\"id\":1776123188427,\"type\":\"Easy\",\"skill\":\"Technical Comprehension\",\"options\":[\"It stores memory\",\"It connects and allows communication between components\",\"It cools the CPU\",\"It powers peripherals\"],\"question\":\"Why is the motherboard compared to the nervous system?\",\"questionType\":\"Easy\",\"correctAnswer\":1},{\"id\":1776123188428,\"type\":\"Easy\",\"skill\":\"Technical Comprehension\",\"options\":[\"Increase storage\",\"Reduce heat and prevent damage\",\"Improve internet speed\",\"Store BIOS\"],\"question\":\"What is the main purpose of the cooling system?\",\"questionType\":\"Easy\",\"correctAnswer\":1},{\"id\":1776123188429,\"type\":\"Easy\",\"skill\":\"Analytical Thinking\",\"options\":[\"Cheaper only\",\"More efficient and produces less heat\",\"Larger in size\",\"Uses more electricity\"],\"question\":\"Why is switching PSU commonly used?\",\"questionType\":\"Easy\",\"correctAnswer\":1},{\"id\":1776123188430,\"type\":\"Easy\",\"skill\":\"Memorization\",\"options\":[\"HDD\",\"SSD\",\"DVD\",\"Floppy Disk\"],\"question\":\"Which is more durable and faster?\",\"questionType\":\"Easy\",\"correctAnswer\":1},{\"id\":1776123188431,\"type\":\"Easy\",\"skill\":\"Technical Comprehension\",\"options\":[\"Execute–Decode–Fetch\",\"Fetch–Decode–Execute\",\"Store–Execute–Fetch\",\"Decode–Execute–Store\"],\"question\":\"Which correctly describes the CPU processing cycle?\",\"questionType\":\"Easy\",\"correctAnswer\":1},{\"id\":1776123188432,\"type\":\"Easy\",\"skill\":\"Problem Solving\",\"options\":[\"GPU\",\"Keyboard\",\"Mouse\",\"Speaker\"],\"question\":\"If the monitor shows no display but the CPU fan runs, which component should be checked?\",\"questionType\":\"Easy\",\"correctAnswer\":0},{\"id\":1776123188433,\"type\":\"Easy\",\"skill\":\"Memorization\",\"options\":[\"Fan-based\",\"Liquid cooling\",\"Fanless cooling\",\"Hybrid cooling\"],\"question\":\"Which cooling system has no moving parts?\",\"questionType\":\"Easy\",\"correctAnswer\":2},{\"id\":1776123188434,\"type\":\"Easy\",\"skill\":\"Problem Solving\",\"options\":[\"Add fan\",\"Replace SSD with HDD\",\"Upgrade to SSD\",\"Change keyboard\"],\"question\":\"A user wants faster boot time. What upgrade should be recommended?\",\"questionType\":\"Easy\",\"correctAnswer\":2},{\"id\":1776123188435,\"type\":\"Easy\",\"skill\":\"Problem Solving\",\"options\":[\"RAM\",\"PSU\",\"Monitor\",\"GPU\"],\"question\":\"The computer does not power on. What should be checked first?\",\"questionType\":\"Easy\",\"correctAnswer\":1},{\"id\":1776123188436,\"type\":\"Easy\",\"skill\":\"Analytical Thinking\",\"options\":[\"SSD\",\"HDD\",\"RAM\",\"Cache\"],\"question\":\"Which storage device is best for large, low-cost storage?\",\"questionType\":\"Easy\",\"correctAnswer\":1},{\"id\":1776123188437,\"type\":\"Easy\",\"skill\":\"Technical Comprehension\",\"options\":[\"Stores data temporarily\",\"Requires no internet\",\"Provides remote access and backup\",\"Replaces RAM\"],\"question\":\"Cloud storage is beneficial because it:\",\"questionType\":\"Easy\",\"correctAnswer\":2},{\"id\":1776123188438,\"type\":\"Easy\",\"skill\":\"Critical Thinking\",\"options\":[\"Fanless\",\"Liquid cooling\",\"No cooling\",\"VGA cooling\"],\"question\":\"For a high-performance gaming PC, which cooling system is most suitable?\",\"questionType\":\"Easy\",\"correctAnswer\":1}]', '{\"hours\":1,\"minutes\":30}', 'Easy', NULL, '[{\"id\":\"introduction\",\"type\":\"introduction\",\"label\":\"Introduction\",\"order\":1},{\"id\":\"diagnostic\",\"type\":\"diagnostic\",\"label\":\"Diagnostic\",\"order\":2},{\"id\":\"lesson\",\"type\":\"lesson\",\"label\":\"Lesson\",\"order\":3},{\"id\":\"final\",\"type\":\"final\",\"label\":\"Final Assessment\",\"order\":4}]');
INSERT INTO `module` (`ModuleID`, `ModuleTitle`, `Description`, `LessonOrder`, `Tesda_Reference`, `Is_Unlocked`, `Is_Completed`, `LessonLanguage`, `Is_Deleted`, `created_at`, `updated_at`, `sections`, `diagnosticQuestions`, `reviewQuestions`, `finalQuestions`, `LessonTime`, `Difficulty`, `finalInstruction`, `roadmapStages`) VALUES
(9, 'Computer Assembly and Software Configuration', '<div>This lesson guides learners through the step-by-step process of assembling a computer, understanding each component’s role, and applying safe and proper installation techniques. Additionally, it introduces learners to software, its types, and proper installation and configuration. By learning how parts fit and work together, students develop foundational CHS skills necessary for building, upgrading, and maintaining computer systems.</div><p><br></p><p><strong>Learning Objectives:</strong></p><p>This lesson aims to:</p><p>1. identify the required tools, components, and safety precautions for computer assembly;</p><p>2. demonstrate proper installation of internal computer hardware components; and</p><p>3. understand software and its proper installation and configuration.</p>', 4, '', 0, 0, 'English', 0, '2026-03-15 23:45:22', '2026-04-27 00:17:37', '[{\"id\":1776121460373,\"file\":null,\"type\":\"topic\",\"order\":1,\"title\":\"Topic 1: Pre-Assembly Procedures and Safety Preparation\",\"caption\":\"\",\"content\":\"\",\"fileName\":null},{\"id\":1777220247030,\"file\":null,\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"order\":2,\"title\":\"\",\"caption\":\"\",\"content\":\"<p>Before assembling a computer system, technicians must ensure that the work environment, tools, and components are properly prepared. Pre-assembly preparation minimizes hardware damage, ensures safety, and improves assembly efficiency. Proper preparation includes gathering the correct tools, observing safety precautions (especially electrostatic discharge protection), and verifying that all necessary components are available before installation.</p>\\n<p>Computer assembly requires specialized tools designed to handle delicate electronic components safely and accurately. The most commonly used tool is the Phillips screwdriver, which is needed for installing motherboard screws, power supply units, storage drives, and expansion cards. Additional tools include anti-static wrist straps, tweezers for handling small connectors, thermal paste for proper heat transfer between the CPU and heatsink, cable ties for cable management, and cleaning tools such as compressed air or soft brushes.</p>\\n<p>Using the correct tools prevents accidental damage to components and improves the accuracy and speed of installation. Proper cable organization using cable ties also enhances airflow inside the computer case, which contributes to better cooling and longer component lifespan. In addition, insulated tools and proper handling practices reduce the risk of electrical hazards during installation.[1][2]</p>\\n<p>Electrostatic discharge (ESD) is one of the most common causes of hidden hardware damage during computer assembly. Static electricity stored in the human body can transfer to sensitive components such as RAM, CPUs, and motherboards, potentially causing immediate or long-term failure. Therefore, technicians must follow grounding procedures before touching any electronic parts.</p>\\n<p>Common ESD protection methods include wearing an anti-static wrist strap connected to a grounded surface, touching an unpainted metal surface to discharge static electricity, working on non-carpeted or anti-static surfaces, and handling components only by their edges without touching circuitry or connector pins. Components should remain inside anti-static packaging until installation to prevent static exposure.[3]</p>\\n<p>Grounding devices such as wrist straps maintain the technician at the same electrical potential as the equipment, preventing sudden discharge between the body and components. This practice significantly reduces the risk of damaging sensitive electronics during installation or servicing.[4]</p>\\n<p>Before starting assembly, technicians must check whether all required components are available and compatible with each other. Essential components include the motherboard, central processing unit (CPU), random access memory (RAM), storage devices (SSD or HDD), power supply unit (PSU), cooling system, computer casing, and expansion cards such as graphics cards or network adapters.</p>\\n<p>Part verification ensures compatibility between the motherboard and processor socket, RAM type and speed, and power requirements of installed devices. Confirming the availability of all parts before assembly prevents delays, reduces the need for reassembly, and ensures a smooth workflow. Careful inspection also helps detect damaged connectors, missing accessories, or incorrect components before installation begins.[5]</p>\",\"fileName\":null,\"contentLayout\":\"text\"},{\"id\":1776121460378,\"file\":null,\"type\":\"review-multiple-choice\",\"order\":3,\"title\":\"\",\"caption\":\"\",\"content\":\"\",\"fileName\":null,\"questions\":[{\"id\":1776121460375,\"skill\":\"Memorization\",\"options\":[\"Anti-static wrist strap\",\"Screwdriver\",\"Cleaning cloth\",\"Cable ties\"],\"question\":\"Which tool prevents electrostatic discharge while assembling a computer?\",\"questionType\":\"Easy\",\"correctAnswer\":0},{\"id\":1776121460376,\"skill\":\"Memorization\",\"options\":[\"By the circuitry\",\"By the sides or edges\",\"By the ports\",\"Anywhere as long as it is clean\"],\"question\":\"When handling computer components, where should you hold them to avoid damage?\",\"questionType\":\"Easy\",\"correctAnswer\":1},{\"id\":1776121460377,\"skill\":\"Memorization\",\"options\":[\"Install software first\",\"Check all components and tools needed\",\"Power on the computer immediately\",\"Connect to the internet\"],\"question\":\"What must be done before starting the assembly process?\",\"questionType\":\"Easy\",\"correctAnswer\":1}]},{\"id\":1776121460379,\"file\":null,\"type\":\"topic\",\"order\":4,\"title\":\"Topic 2: Step-by-Step Installation of Components\",\"caption\":\"\",\"content\":\"\",\"fileName\":null},{\"id\":1777220247031,\"file\":null,\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"order\":5,\"title\":\"\",\"caption\":\"\",\"content\":\"<p>Computer assembly requires installing hardware components in the proper order to ensure compatibility, safety, and system functionality. Following a structured installation sequence helps technicians avoid damage, simplifies cable routing, and ensures that each component is properly recognized by the system during startup.</p>\\n<p>Installing a motherboard can seem like a daunting task, but it\'s easier than you might think if you follow steps. Installing a motherboard is one of the most critical steps in building a computer. The motherboard is the backbone of your system, connecting to and powering all the other components. Some of the best motherboards may offer advanced features, but a well-installed motherboard should lead to stability, proper functionality, and efficient cooling.[6][7]</p>\\n<p>Preparation: Setting the stage</p>\\n<p>Clear a clean, flat workspace and gather tools like a Philips-head screwdriver and manuals.</p>\\n<p>Wear an anti-static wrist strap or use an anti-static mat to protect components.</p>\\n<p>(Optional) Install key parts on the motherboard before putting it in the case:</p>\\n<p>CPU cooler</p>\\n<p>M.2 storage (if applicable)</p>\",\"fileName\":null,\"contentLayout\":\"text\"},{\"id\":1777220247032,\"file\":null,\"type\":\"image\",\"order\":6,\"title\":\"Step-by-Step Installation of Components\",\"images\":[{\"url\":\"/uploads/lessons/093_preparation_setting_the_stage.webp\",\"file\":null,\"caption\":\"Preparation: Setting the stage\",\"fileName\":\"093_preparation_setting_the_stage.webp\"},{\"url\":\"/uploads/lessons/094_remove_case_panels.webp\",\"file\":null,\"caption\":\"Remove Case Panels\",\"fileName\":\"094_remove_case_panels.webp\"},{\"url\":\"/uploads/lessons/095_install_the_i_o_shield.webp\",\"file\":null,\"caption\":\"Install the I/O Shield\",\"fileName\":\"095_install_the_i_o_shield.webp\"},{\"url\":\"/uploads/lessons/096_make_sure_the_ports_line_up_with_the_shi.webp\",\"file\":null,\"caption\":\"Make sure the ports line up with the shield cutouts\",\"fileName\":\"096_make_sure_the_ports_line_up_with_the_shi.webp\"},{\"url\":\"/uploads/lessons/097_add_or_adjust_standoffs_if_needed_remove.webp\",\"file\":null,\"caption\":\"Add or adjust standoffs if needed\",\"fileName\":\"097_add_or_adjust_standoffs_if_needed_remove.webp\"},{\"url\":\"/uploads/lessons/098_make_sure_it_sits_flat_and_straight.webp\",\"file\":null,\"caption\":\"Make sure it sits flat and straight\",\"fileName\":\"098_make_sure_it_sits_flat_and_straight.webp\"},{\"url\":\"/uploads/lessons/099_tighten_just_enough_so_the_board_doesn_t.webp\",\"file\":null,\"caption\":\"Tighten just enough so the board doesn’t shift\",\"fileName\":\"099_tighten_just_enough_so_the_board_doesn_t.webp\"},{\"url\":\"/uploads/lessons/100_locate_the_alignment_keys_on_the_motherb.webp\",\"file\":null,\"caption\":\"Locate the alignment keys on the motherboard CPU socket and\",\"fileName\":\"100_locate_the_alignment_keys_on_the_motherb.webp\"},{\"url\":\"/uploads/lessons/101_do_not_touch_socket_contacts_to_protect_.webp\",\"file\":null,\"caption\":\"DO NOT touch socket contacts\",\"fileName\":\"101_do_not_touch_socket_contacts_to_protect_.webp\"},{\"url\":\"/uploads/lessons/102_lift_the_cpu_socket_lever_and_the_metal_.webp\",\"file\":null,\"caption\":\"Lift the CPU socket lever and the metal load plate will be l\",\"fileName\":\"102_lift_the_cpu_socket_lever_and_the_metal_.webp\"},{\"url\":\"/uploads/lessons/104_before_installing_the_cpu_cooler_please_.webp\",\"file\":null,\"caption\":\"Before installing the CPU cooler\",\"fileName\":\"104_before_installing_the_cpu_cooler_please_.webp\"},{\"url\":\"/uploads/lessons/106_finally_tidy_up_your_cables_one_last_tim.webp\",\"file\":null,\"caption\":\"Finally\",\"fileName\":\"106_finally_tidy_up_your_cables_one_last_tim.webp\"},{\"url\":\"/uploads/lessons/107_ideally_as_you_press_the_power_button_th.webp\",\"file\":null,\"caption\":\"Ideally as you press the power button\",\"fileName\":\"107_ideally_as_you_press_the_power_button_th.webp\"}],\"layout\":\"grid-3\",\"caption\":\"\",\"content\":\"/uploads/lessons/093_preparation_setting_the_stage.webp\",\"fileName\":\"093_preparation_setting_the_stage.webp\"},{\"id\":1776121460402,\"file\":null,\"type\":\"review-multiple-choice\",\"order\":7,\"title\":\"\",\"caption\":\"\",\"content\":\"\",\"fileName\":null,\"questions\":[{\"id\":1776121460399,\"skill\":\"Memorization\",\"options\":[\"Cable ties\",\"Thermal paste\",\"Alignment markers on the socket\",\"The motherboard manual\"],\"question\":\"What ensures that the CPU is installed in the correct orientation?\",\"questionType\":\"Easy\",\"correctAnswer\":2},{\"id\":1776121460400,\"skill\":\"Memorization\",\"options\":[\"Increase CPU speed\",\"Enhance heat transfer between CPU and cooler\",\"Protect the CPU from electrical damage\",\"Prevent dust build-up\"],\"question\":\"What is the purpose of applying thermal paste?\",\"questionType\":\"Easy\",\"correctAnswer\":1},{\"id\":1776121460401,\"skill\":\"Memorization\",\"options\":[\"Motherboard\",\"RAM\",\"Power Supply Unit (PSU)\",\"SSD\"],\"question\":\"Which component supplies electrical power to the whole system?\",\"questionType\":\"Easy\",\"correctAnswer\":2}]},{\"id\":1776121460403,\"file\":null,\"type\":\"topic\",\"order\":8,\"title\":\"Topic 3: The Software Components of a Computer\",\"caption\":\"\",\"content\":\"\",\"fileName\":null},{\"id\":1777220247033,\"file\":null,\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"order\":9,\"title\":\"\",\"caption\":\"\",\"content\":\"<p>While hardware represents the physical parts of a computer, software components provide the instructions that allow hardware to function. Software controls system operations, enables user interaction, and allows computers to perform specific tasks. In Computer Hardware Servicing, understanding software is essential because hardware cannot operate effectively without proper software support.[12][13]</p>\\n<p>Software components are commonly classified into operating system, application software, programming software, and firmware. These components work together to manage hardware resources, execute user commands, and support computing tasks. A technician must recognize how these software layers interact to properly diagnose, install, and maintain computer systems.[14]</p>\\n<p>An operating system (OS) is a collection of software that manages a computer’s hardware and applications by allocating resources, including memory, CPU, input/output devices and file storage.[15]</p>\\n<p>A user interacts with an operating system through a user interface (UI), which issues commands in a language the OS can understand. The UI can be either a graphical user interface (GUI) or a command-line interface (CLI). Billions of people rely on operating systems as the underlying management system for tasks like sending emails, browsing the internet, playing video games and more.[15]</p>\\n<p>Hardware Management - Controls peripheral devices like printers, monitors, and disk drivers.</p>\\n<p>Resource Allocation - Manages CPU usage, memory, and storage to ensure multiple programs can run efficiently without interfering with each other.</p>\\n<p>User Interface (UI) - Provides a way for users to interact with the computer, such as a Graphical User Interface (GUI) or Command-Line Interface (CLI).</p>\\n<p>File System Management - Organizes data on storage devices.</p>\",\"fileName\":null,\"contentLayout\":\"text\"},{\"id\":1777220247034,\"file\":null,\"type\":\"image\",\"order\":10,\"title\":\"The Software Components of a Computer\",\"images\":[{\"url\":\"/uploads/lessons/108_a_user_interacts_with_an_operating_syste.webp\",\"file\":null,\"caption\":\"A user interacts with an operating system through a user int\",\"fileName\":\"108_a_user_interacts_with_an_operating_syste.webp\"},{\"url\":\"/uploads/lessons/109_microsoft_windows.webp\",\"file\":null,\"caption\":\"Microsoft Windows\",\"fileName\":\"109_microsoft_windows.webp\"},{\"url\":\"/uploads/lessons/110_apple_ios.webp\",\"file\":null,\"caption\":\"Apple iOS\",\"fileName\":\"110_apple_ios.webp\"},{\"url\":\"/uploads/lessons/111_google_android.webp\",\"file\":null,\"caption\":\"Google Android\",\"fileName\":\"111_google_android.webp\"},{\"url\":\"/uploads/lessons/112_apple_macos.webp\",\"file\":null,\"caption\":\"Apple macOS\",\"fileName\":\"112_apple_macos.webp\"},{\"url\":\"/uploads/lessons/113_linux.webp\",\"file\":null,\"caption\":\"Linux\",\"fileName\":\"113_linux.webp\"}],\"layout\":\"grid-3\",\"caption\":\"\",\"content\":\"/uploads/lessons/108_a_user_interacts_with_an_operating_syste.webp\",\"fileName\":\"108_a_user_interacts_with_an_operating_syste.webp\"},{\"id\":1776121460475,\"file\":null,\"type\":\"video\",\"order\":11,\"title\":\"\",\"caption\":\"Lesson 4 Topic 3 Video\",\"content\":\"https://www.dropbox.com/scl/fi/q4svlqak2yu7zbzesfkry/Lesson-4-Topic-3.mp4?rlkey=u93nfxhvf0zjq38j0qfpkp16i&st=xtmw84m1&dl=0\",\"fileName\":null},{\"id\":1776121460411,\"file\":null,\"type\":\"review-multiple-choice\",\"order\":12,\"title\":\"\",\"caption\":\"\",\"content\":\"\",\"fileName\":null,\"questions\":[{\"id\":1776121460408,\"skill\":\"Memorization\",\"options\":[\"To replace hardware\",\"To store electricity\",\"To provide instructions for hardware operation\",\"To physically connect components\"],\"question\":\"What is the primary role of software in a computer system?\",\"questionType\":\"Easy\",\"correctAnswer\":2},{\"id\":1776121460409,\"skill\":\"Memorization\",\"options\":[\"RAM\",\"CPU\",\"Operating System\",\"Power Supply\"],\"question\":\"Which of the following is considered a software component?\",\"questionType\":\"Easy\",\"correctAnswer\":2},{\"id\":1776121460410,\"skill\":\"Memorization\",\"options\":[\"Software is optional\",\"Hardware works without software\",\"Software controls and manages hardware functionality\",\"Software only affects internet speed\"],\"question\":\"Why is understanding software important in Computer Hardware Servicing?\",\"questionType\":\"Easy\",\"correctAnswer\":2}]},{\"id\":1776121460412,\"file\":null,\"type\":\"topic\",\"order\":13,\"title\":\"Topic 4: Device Drivers\",\"caption\":\"\",\"content\":\"\",\"fileName\":null},{\"id\":1777220247035,\"file\":null,\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"order\":14,\"title\":\"\",\"caption\":\"\",\"content\":\"<p>Device drivers are specialized software programs that allow the operating system to communicate with hardware devices. Without proper drivers, hardware components such as printers, graphics cards, network adapters, and sound cards may not function correctly or at all.</p>\\n<p>In Computer Hardware Servicing, technicians are responsible for installing, updating, and troubleshooting device drivers. Drivers act as translators between the operating system and the hardware, ensuring compatibility, performance optimization, and system stability. Incorrect or outdated drivers may cause system errors, hardware malfunctions, or performance issues.[32]</p>\\n<p>Generic device drivers – As mentioned before, these are pre-installed drivers for general purposes and many devices.</p>\\n<p>Specific device drivers – Installed by the user, they are prepared for a particular device (or a particular class of devices: see point 8 on this list)</p>\\n<p>Kernel device drivers – These are the most generic drivers possible loaded along with the OS. They access RAM to function, hence the minimal requirements for every operating system.</p>\\n<p>User-mode device drivers – These drivers are loaded in user mode and may be saved on the computer. This means that they are not as heavy for the system. They include the drivers for your typical external devices.</p>\\n<p>Character device drivers – These deal with data in a stream of characters, where each character is treated independently. Examples of character devices include keyboards, mice, serial ports, and terminals – devices that typically handle input or output one character at a time.</p>\\n<p>Block device drivers – This type handles file system requests, employing the strategy(9E) routine to execute disk I/O operations. They can also offer a character driver interface, enabling direct device access (raw interface).</p>\",\"fileName\":null,\"contentLayout\":\"text\"},{\"id\":1777220247036,\"file\":null,\"type\":\"image\",\"order\":15,\"title\":\"Device Drivers\",\"images\":[{\"url\":\"/uploads/lessons/114_i_o_devices_keyboards_mice_cd_dvd_drives.webp\",\"file\":null,\"caption\":\"I/O devices (keyboards\",\"fileName\":\"114_i_o_devices_keyboards_mice_cd_dvd_drives.webp\"},{\"url\":\"/uploads/lessons/118_communication_interfaces_in_embedded_sys.webp\",\"file\":null,\"caption\":\"Communication interfaces in embedded systems (UART\",\"fileName\":\"118_communication_interfaces_in_embedded_sys.webp\"},{\"url\":\"/uploads/lessons/119_display_devices_lcds_or_leds_39.webp\",\"file\":null,\"caption\":\"Display devices (LCDs or LEDs)\",\"fileName\":\"119_display_devices_lcds_or_leds_39.webp\"},{\"url\":\"/uploads/lessons/120_wireless_modules_40.webp\",\"file\":null,\"caption\":\"Wireless modules\",\"fileName\":\"120_wireless_modules_40.webp\"},{\"url\":\"/uploads/lessons/121_usb_controllers_41.webp\",\"file\":null,\"caption\":\"USB controllers\",\"fileName\":\"121_usb_controllers_41.webp\"}],\"layout\":\"grid-3\",\"caption\":\"\",\"content\":\"/uploads/lessons/114_i_o_devices_keyboards_mice_cd_dvd_drives.webp\",\"fileName\":\"114_i_o_devices_keyboards_mice_cd_dvd_drives.webp\"},{\"id\":1776121460418,\"file\":null,\"type\":\"review-multiple-choice\",\"order\":16,\"title\":\"\",\"caption\":\"\",\"content\":\"\",\"fileName\":null,\"questions\":[{\"id\":1776121460415,\"skill\":\"Memorization\",\"options\":[\"To power hardware\",\"To connect hardware physically\",\"To enable communication between OS and hardware\",\"To store user files\"],\"question\":\"What is the main function of a device driver?\",\"questionType\":\"Easy\",\"correctAnswer\":2},{\"id\":1776121460416,\"skill\":\"Memorization\",\"options\":[\"The computer runs faster\",\"Hardware may not function properly\",\"Software installs automatically\",\"The system shuts down permanently\"],\"question\":\"What may happen if a device driver is missing or outdated?\",\"questionType\":\"Easy\",\"correctAnswer\":3},{\"id\":1776121460417,\"skill\":\"Memorization\",\"options\":[\"Monitor\",\"Printer\",\"Graphics card\",\"All of the above\"],\"question\":\"Which hardware requires a device driver?\",\"questionType\":\"Easy\",\"correctAnswer\":3}]},{\"id\":1776121460419,\"file\":null,\"type\":\"topic\",\"order\":17,\"title\":\"Topic 5: Firmware\",\"caption\":\"\",\"content\":\"\",\"fileName\":null},{\"id\":1777220247037,\"file\":null,\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"order\":18,\"title\":\"\",\"caption\":\"\",\"content\":\"<p>Firmware is a type of software embedded directly into hardware components. It provides low-level control and instructions that allow hardware to initialize and operate correctly. Unlike application software, firmware is stored in non-volatile memory, meaning it remains even when the computer is powered off.[42]</p>\\n<p>Many devices rely on firmware to function, including TVs, cameras, mobile phones, printers, drives and more. Firmware is located in a device’s nonvolatile memory, where content can be stored when a device is off. Firmware can be written to different memory types including, random access memory (RAM), read-only memory (ROM), erasable programmable read-only memory (EPROM) and flash memory.[42]</p>\\n<p>Firmware helps devices perform their intended functions in several important ways, including delivering the instructions for how the device should start up, how it should interact with other devices—such as Internet routers or remote controls—and how it should perform critical input/output(I/O) tasks.[42]</p>\\n<p>In addition to changes in the way firmware uses and stores memory, there have been advancements in the types of firmware available to users as well. Today, firmware can be categorized into three basic groups defined by its architecture:</p>\\n<p>Low-level firmware - intrinsic to a device’s hardware and stored on nonvolatile, read-only chips, like ROM, which can’t be updated. Devices that rely on low-level firmware use memory that can only be written once and never reprogrammed.</p>\\n<p>High-level firmware - firmware that can’t be updated because of the complexity of its hardware. In a computer, high-level firmware is contained in flash memory chips and is responsible for more advanced tasks than low-level firmware. High-level firmware contains important instructions for how a device functions and various components interact.</p>\\n<p>Subsystem firmware - is contained in what’s known as an ‘‘embedded system,’’ a specific combination of hardware and software designed for a purpose or task. Subsystem firmware is similar to high-level firmware in its complexity and adaptability. Like high-level firmware, subsystem firmware can be easily updated.[42]</p>\\n<p>An essential firmware stored on a motherboard chip that initializes hardware, performs a Power-On Self-Test (POST), and loads the operating system when a computer powers on. It acts as the initial, low-level interface between the hardware and the OS.[43]</p>\",\"fileName\":null,\"contentLayout\":\"text\"},{\"id\":1777220247038,\"file\":null,\"type\":\"image\",\"order\":19,\"title\":\"Firmware\",\"images\":[{\"url\":\"/uploads/lessons/122_an_essential_firmware_stored_on_a_mother.webp\",\"file\":null,\"caption\":\"An essential firmware stored on a motherboard chip that init\",\"fileName\":\"122_an_essential_firmware_stored_on_a_mother.webp\"},{\"url\":\"/uploads/lessons/123_uefi_is_a_modern_replacement_for_the_tra.webp\",\"file\":null,\"caption\":\"UEFI is a modern replacement for the traditional basic input\",\"fileName\":\"123_uefi_is_a_modern_replacement_for_the_tra.webp\"}],\"layout\":\"side-by-side\",\"caption\":\"\",\"content\":\"/uploads/lessons/122_an_essential_firmware_stored_on_a_mother.webp\",\"fileName\":\"122_an_essential_firmware_stored_on_a_mother.webp\"},{\"id\":1776121460432,\"file\":null,\"type\":\"review-multiple-choice\",\"order\":20,\"title\":\"\",\"caption\":\"\",\"content\":\"\",\"fileName\":null,\"questions\":[{\"id\":1776121460429,\"skill\":\"Memorization\",\"options\":[\"Hard drive\",\"RAM\",\"Non-volatile memory on the hardware\",\"Cloud storage\"],\"question\":\"Where is firmware typically stored?\",\"questionType\":\"Easy\",\"correctAnswer\":2},{\"id\":1776121460430,\"skill\":\"Memorization\",\"options\":[\"Microsoft Word\",\"Device driver\",\"BIOS/UEFI\",\"Web browser\"],\"question\":\"Which of the following is an example of firmware?\",\"questionType\":\"Easy\",\"correctAnswer\":0},{\"id\":1776121460431,\"skill\":\"Memorization\",\"options\":[\"Load games\",\"Initialize hardware components\",\"Open applications\",\"Connect to the internet\"],\"question\":\"What is the main role of firmware during startup?\",\"questionType\":\"Easy\",\"correctAnswer\":1}]},{\"id\":1776121460433,\"file\":null,\"type\":\"topic\",\"order\":21,\"title\":\"Topic 6: Application Software\",\"caption\":\"\",\"content\":\"\",\"fileName\":null},{\"id\":1777220247039,\"file\":null,\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"order\":22,\"title\":\"\",\"caption\":\"\",\"content\":\"<p>Application software consists of programs designed to help users perform specific tasks such as word processing, graphic design, data analysis, communication, and entertainment. These applications rely on system software and hardware resources to function effectively.[49]</p>\\n<p>From a Computer Hardware Servicing perspective, technicians may be required to install, configure, troubleshoot, and update application software based on user requirements. Understanding compatibility, system requirements, and licensing is important to ensure optimal system performance and user satisfaction.[49]</p>\\n<p>Creating documents and spreadsheets</p>\\n<p>Word processing and spreadsheet programs are application software. These programs allow you to create, edit and store documents. Word processing systems are useful for creating and printing documents like handouts or manuscripts, while spreadsheet programs allow you to track data and create spreadsheet systems. You can use spreadsheet programs to track productivity or create budgets.[49]</p>\\n<p>Sending and receiving communication</p>\\n<p>Communication applications can include those for direct messaging, message boards and collaborative spaces. This can include written communication, like emailing or instant messaging, but can also include voice and video calls. Many communication applications are vital for remote jobs with digital workspaces, as they allow team members in different locations or time zones to communicate regarding projects.[49]</p>\\n<p>Storing, processing and analyzing data</p>\\n<p>Databases can be useful for companies because they allow them to track and analyze information about customer relationships, inventory, payroll and performance. Customer relationship management applications allow businesses to record and act upon potential and current customers. They also allow businesses to record client information. Payroll and scheduling applications support staff scheduling and business tax information tracking.[49]</p>\",\"fileName\":null,\"contentLayout\":\"text\"},{\"id\":1777220247040,\"file\":null,\"type\":\"image\",\"order\":23,\"title\":\"Application Software\",\"images\":[{\"url\":\"/uploads/lessons/124_popular_office_suites_include_microsoft_.webp\",\"file\":null,\"caption\":\"Popular office suites include Microsoft Office (Word\",\"fileName\":\"124_popular_office_suites_include_microsoft_.webp\"},{\"url\":\"/uploads/lessons/125_google_chrome.webp\",\"file\":null,\"caption\":\"Google Chrome\",\"fileName\":\"125_google_chrome.webp\"},{\"url\":\"/uploads/lessons/126_safari.webp\",\"file\":null,\"caption\":\"Safari\",\"fileName\":\"126_safari.webp\"},{\"url\":\"/uploads/lessons/127_microsoft_edge.webp\",\"file\":null,\"caption\":\"Microsoft Edge\",\"fileName\":\"127_microsoft_edge.webp\"},{\"url\":\"/uploads/lessons/128_mozilla_firefox_crop_2.webp\",\"file\":null,\"caption\":\"Mozilla Firefox\",\"fileName\":\"128_mozilla_firefox_crop_2.webp\"}],\"layout\":\"grid-3\",\"caption\":\"\",\"content\":\"/uploads/lessons/124_popular_office_suites_include_microsoft_.webp\",\"fileName\":\"124_popular_office_suites_include_microsoft_.webp\"},{\"id\":1776121460444,\"file\":null,\"type\":\"review-multiple-choice\",\"order\":24,\"title\":\"\",\"caption\":\"\",\"content\":\"\",\"fileName\":null,\"questions\":[{\"id\":1776121460441,\"skill\":\"Memorization\",\"options\":[\"BIOS\",\"Device driver\",\"Microsoft Excel\",\"Operating system\"],\"question\":\"Which of the following is an example of application software?\",\"questionType\":\"Easy\",\"correctAnswer\":1},{\"id\":1776121460442,\"skill\":\"Memorization\",\"options\":[\"Control hardware directly\",\"Perform user-oriented tasks\",\"Manage memory allocation\",\"Boot the computer\"],\"question\":\"What is the primary purpose of application software?\",\"questionType\":\"Easy\",\"correctAnswer\":1},{\"id\":1776121460443,\"skill\":\"Memorization\",\"options\":[\"Firmware only\",\"Hardware only\",\"System software\",\"Programming software\"],\"question\":\"Application software depends on which software to run properly?\",\"questionType\":\"Easy\",\"correctAnswer\":0}]},{\"id\":1776121460445,\"file\":null,\"type\":\"topic\",\"order\":25,\"title\":\"Topic 7: Software Installation and Configuration\",\"caption\":\"\",\"content\":\"\",\"fileName\":null},{\"id\":1777220247041,\"file\":null,\"type\":\"paragraph\",\"order\":26,\"title\":\"\",\"caption\":\"\",\"content\":\"<p>Software installation and configuration is an important skill to have in terms of CHS. Applications must be installed correctly, licensed properly, and configured to meet business and security requirements. Incorrect installations or misconfigurations can lead to application failures, security gaps, and inconsistent user experiences. Software installation and configuration involves setting up system software, drivers, and applications to ensure correct functionality and performance. This process includes verifying system requirements, configuring settings, applying updates, and testing software after installation.[70]</p>\\n<p>Challenges commonly occur when dealing with multiple software versions, compatibility with different operating systems, licensing and activation issues, dependency conflicts, and user-specific configuration requirements. Inconsistent manual installations often result in configuration drift across devices.</p>\\n<p>Without standardization, software environments become difficult to support and secure.</p>\\n<p>System requirements are the minimum hardware and software conditions that must be met before installing or running a software application. This includes CPU speed, RAM, disk space, operating system version, and sometimes specific privileges like administrator access.[71]</p>\\n<p>Examples of common requirements:</p>\\n<p>Minimum processor speed</p>\\n<p>Minimum RAM (e.g., 1–2 GB or more)</p>\\n<p>Available disk space</p>\",\"fileName\":null,\"contentLayout\":\"text\"},{\"id\":1777220247042,\"file\":null,\"type\":\"image\",\"order\":27,\"title\":\"Software Installation and Configuration\",\"images\":[{\"url\":\"/uploads/lessons/129_a_standard_installation_sometimes_called.webp\",\"file\":null,\"caption\":\"A Standard installation (sometimes called Typical\",\"fileName\":\"129_a_standard_installation_sometimes_called.webp\"},{\"url\":\"/uploads/lessons/130_a_custom_installation_lets_you_choose_wh.webp\",\"file\":null,\"caption\":\"A Custom installation lets you choose which parts of the sof\",\"fileName\":\"130_a_custom_installation_lets_you_choose_wh.webp\"},{\"url\":\"/uploads/lessons/131_during_the_first_stage_of_configuration__crop_approx.webp\",\"file\":null,\"caption\":\"During the first stage of configuration\",\"fileName\":\"131_during_the_first_stage_of_configuration__crop_approx.webp\"},{\"url\":\"/uploads/lessons/134_creating_a_user_account_is_a_crucial_ste.webp\",\"file\":null,\"caption\":\"Creating a user account is a crucial step to protect the sys\",\"fileName\":\"134_creating_a_user_account_is_a_crucial_ste.webp\"},{\"url\":\"/uploads/lessons/135_network_configuration_allows_the_compute.webp\",\"file\":null,\"caption\":\"Network configuration allows the computer to connect to the\",\"fileName\":\"135_network_configuration_allows_the_compute.webp\"},{\"url\":\"/uploads/lessons/136_security_settings_are_configured_to_prot.webp\",\"file\":null,\"caption\":\"Security settings are configured to protect the computer fro\",\"fileName\":\"136_security_settings_are_configured_to_prot.webp\"},{\"url\":\"/uploads/lessons/137_device_drivers_act_as_a_bridge_between_t.webp\",\"file\":null,\"caption\":\"Device drivers act as a bridge between the operating system\",\"fileName\":\"137_device_drivers_act_as_a_bridge_between_t.webp\"},{\"url\":\"/uploads/lessons/138_after_technical_and_security_settings_ar.webp\",\"file\":null,\"caption\":\"After technical and security settings are configured\",\"fileName\":\"138_after_technical_and_security_settings_ar.webp\"}],\"layout\":\"grid-3\",\"caption\":\"\",\"content\":\"/uploads/lessons/129_a_standard_installation_sometimes_called.webp\",\"fileName\":\"129_a_standard_installation_sometimes_called.webp\"},{\"id\":1776121460474,\"file\":null,\"type\":\"review-multiple-choice\",\"order\":28,\"title\":\"\",\"caption\":\"\",\"content\":\"\",\"fileName\":null,\"questions\":[{\"id\":1776121460472,\"skill\":\"Memorization\",\"options\":[\"Internet speed only\",\"System requirements and compatibility\",\"Keyboard layout\",\"Desktop wallpaper\"],\"question\":\"What should be checked before installing software?\",\"questionType\":\"Easy\",\"correctAnswer\":1},{\"id\":1776121460473,\"skill\":\"Memorization\",\"options\":[\"To remove hardware\",\"To personalize appearance only\",\"To optimize performance and functionality\",\"To uninstall drivers\"],\"question\":\"What is the purpose of configuring software after installation?\",\"questionType\":\"Easy\",\"correctAnswer\":2}]}]', '[{\"id\":1776121460620,\"skill\":\"Memorization\",\"options\":[\"Anti-static wrist strap\",\"Screwdriver\",\"Cleaning cloth\",\"Cable ties\"],\"question\":\"Which tool prevents electrostatic discharge while assembling a computer?\",\"questionType\":\"Easy\",\"correctAnswer\":0},{\"id\":1776121460621,\"skill\":\"Memorization\",\"options\":[\"By the circuitry\",\"By the sides or edges\",\"By the ports\",\"Anywhere as long as it is clean\"],\"question\":\"When handling computer components, where should you hold them to avoid damage?\",\"questionType\":\"Easy\",\"correctAnswer\":1},{\"id\":1776121460622,\"skill\":\"Memorization\",\"options\":[\"Install software first\",\"Check all components and tools needed\",\"Power on the computer immediately\",\"Connect to the internet\"],\"question\":\"What must be done before starting the assembly process?\",\"questionType\":\"Easy\",\"correctAnswer\":1},{\"id\":1776121460623,\"skill\":\"Memorization\",\"options\":[\"Cable ties\",\"Thermal paste\",\"Alignment markers on the socket\",\"The motherboard manual\"],\"question\":\"What ensures that the CPU is installed in the correct orientation?\",\"questionType\":\"Easy\",\"correctAnswer\":2},{\"id\":1776121460624,\"skill\":\"Memorization\",\"options\":[\"Increase CPU speed\",\"Enhance heat transfer between CPU and cooler\",\"Protect the CPU from electrical damage\",\"Prevent dust build-up\"],\"question\":\"What is the purpose of applying thermal paste?\",\"questionType\":\"Easy\",\"correctAnswer\":1},{\"id\":1776121460625,\"skill\":\"Memorization\",\"options\":[\"Motherboard\",\"RAM\",\"Power Supply Unit (PSU)\",\"SSD\"],\"question\":\"Which component supplies electrical power to the whole system?\",\"questionType\":\"Easy\",