to sensitive circuitry\",\"To prevent the component from overheating during installation\",\"To make installation faster and easier for technicians\",\"To reduce power consumption of the component\"],\"question\":\"Question: A student touches the circuitry of RAM and damages it. Their instructor reminded them that components must be handled by their edges only. Why is it so?\",\"questionType\":\"Situational\",\"correctAnswer\":0},{\"id\":1776121460583,\"skill\":\"Analytical Thinking\",\"options\":[\"To ensure cables reach the correct connectors inside the case\",\"To confirm that hardware parts are compatible with each other\",\"To verify that the operating system is already installed\",\"To check that the monitor supports the correct resolution\"],\"question\":\"Question: RAM does not fit the motherboard during installation. What first should have been verified?\",\"questionType\":\"Situational\",\"correctAnswer\":1},{\"id\":1776121460584,\"skill\":\"Critical Thinking\",\"options\":[\"It may create an electrical short circuit between motherboard components\",\"It prevents airflow from entering the computer case properly\",\"It blocks RAM slots and prevents modules from locking in place\",\"It interferes with the operating system loading process\"],\"question\":\"Question: A screw is left inside the case after assembly. What risk does this create?\",\"questionType\":\"Situational\",\"correctAnswer\":1},{\"id\":1776121460585,\"skill\":\"Critical Thinking\",\"options\":[\"To install application software immediately after hardware setup\",\"To verify that installed hardware powers on and is detected correctly\",\"To update firmware before the operating system loads\",\"To measure the processing speed of the CPU\"],\"question\":\"Question: After installing components, a technician powers on the system to verify detection. Why is this necessary?\",\"questionType\":\"Situational\",\"correctAnswer\":1},{\"id\":1776121460586,\"skill\":\"Critical Thinking\",\"options\":[\"Blocked airflow prevents heat from being removed from components\",\"Increased airflow causes components to receive too much voltage\",\"Reduced airflow prevents the operating system from loading properly\",\"Improper airflow disables communication between hardware devices\"],\"question\":\"Question: Cables block internal fans causing high temperatures. What is the main issue?\",\"questionType\":\"Situational\",\"correctAnswer\":2},{\"id\":1776121460587,\"skill\":\"Problem Solving\",\"options\":[\"PSU switch and cables\",\"RAM speed\",\"SSD capacity\",\"Mouse connection\"],\"question\":\"Question: A computer shows no signs of power. What should be checked first?\",\"questionType\":\"Situational\",\"correctAnswer\":0},{\"id\":1776121460588,\"skill\":\"Problem Solving\",\"options\":[\"Reseat RAM\",\"Replace CPU\",\"Install OS\",\"Remove PSU\"],\"question\":\"Question: The system boots but shows no display after RAM installation. What should be done?\",\"questionType\":\"Situational\",\"correctAnswer\":0},{\"id\":1776121460589,\"skill\":\"Problem Solving\",\"options\":[\"Check whether the CPU cooler is properly mounted and thermal paste applied\",\"Verify that the storage drive is detected in BIOS\",\"Reinstall the operating system to fix startup issues\",\"Replace the RAM modules with higher capacity ones\"],\"question\":\"Question: The computer shuts down after startup due to overheating. What should be checked?\",\"questionType\":\"Situational\",\"correctAnswer\":0},{\"id\":1776121460605,\"skill\":\"Memorization\",\"options\":[\"Anti-static wrist strap\",\"Screwdriver\",\"Cleaning cloth\",\"Cable ties\"],\"question\":\"Question: While preparing to install RAM and other internal components, a student wants to avoid electrostatic discharge that might damage sensitive parts. Which tool should the student use first? Anti-static wrist strap Screwdriver Cleaning cloth Cable ties\",\"questionType\":\"Situational\",\"correctAnswer\":0},{\"id\":1776121460606,\"skill\":\"Memori