What is the primary purpose of application software?\",\"questionType\":\"Easy\",\"correctAnswer\":1},{\"id\":1776121460647,\"skill\":\"Memorization\",\"options\":[\"Firmware only\",\"Hardware only\",\"System software\",\"Programming software\"],\"question\":\"Application software depends on which software to run properly?\",\"questionType\":\"Easy\",\"correctAnswer\":0},{\"id\":1776121460648,\"skill\":\"Memorization\",\"options\":[\"Internet speed only\",\"System requirements and compatibility\",\"Keyboard layout\",\"Desktop wallpaper\"],\"question\":\"What should be checked before installing software?\",\"questionType\":\"Easy\",\"correctAnswer\":1},{\"id\":1776121460649,\"skill\":\"Memorization\",\"options\":[\"To remove hardware\",\"To personalize appearance only\",\"To optimize performance and functionality\",\"To uninstall drivers\"],\"question\":\"What is the purpose of configuring software after installation?\",\"questionType\":\"Easy\",\"correctAnswer\":2}]', '[{\"id\":1776121460650,\"skill\":\"Memorization\",\"options\":[\"Phillips screwdriver\",\"Tweezers\",\"Anti-static wrist strap\",\"Cleaning brush\"],\"question\":\"Question: A technician prepares to secure the motherboard inside the case. Which tool should be used?\",\"questionType\":\"Situational\",\"correctAnswer\":0},{\"id\":1776121460651,\"skill\":\"Memorization\",\"options\":[\"Storing files\",\"Processing instructions\",\"Supplying power\",\"Cooling system\"],\"question\":\"A computer cannot process instructions because the processor is missing. What is the CPU responsible for?\",\"questionType\":\"Situational\",\"correctAnswer\":1},{\"id\":1776121460652,\"skill\":\"Memorization\",\"options\":[\"Power-On Self-Test\",\"Program Operating Setup Test\",\"Power Operating System Tool\",\"Primary Output System Test\"],\"question\":\"Question: During startup, the computer performs a diagnostic test before loading the OS. What is this called?\",\"questionType\":\"Situational\",\"correctAnswer\":0},{\"id\":1776121460653,\"skill\":\"Technical Comprehension\",\"options\":[\"To increase RAM speed\",\"To improve airflow\",\"To add storage\",\"To reduce voltage\"],\"question\":\"Question: A technician organizes cables neatly to improve cooling inside the case. Why is this done?\",\"questionType\":\"Situational\",\"correctAnswer\":1},{\"id\":1776121460654,\"skill\":\"Technical Comprehension\",\"options\":[\"To fill microscopic gaps and improve heat transfer between CPU and cooler\",\"To electrically connect the CPU to the motherboard\",\"To secure the CPU physically inside the socket\",\"To increase the processor clock speed\"],\"question\":\"Question: A CPU overheats after installing a cooler without paste. What is the work of the thermal paste?\",\"questionType\":\"Situational\",\"correctAnswer\":0},{\"id\":1776121460655,\"skill\":\"Technical Comprehension\",\"options\":[\"Stores operating system and application files for later use\",\"Converts AC power from the outlet into usable DC power for components\",\"Controls communication between software and hardware devices\",\"Provides temporary working memory for running programs\"],\"question\":\"Question: A computer receives no power to internal component. It means that a power supply unit is missing. What does the power supply units role?\",\"questionType\":\"Situational\",\"correctAnswer\":2},{\"id\":1776121460656,\"skill\":\"Analytical Thinking\",\"options\":[\"Prevents the motherboard from directly touching the case and causing short circuits\",\"Improves CPU cooling by raising the motherboard closer to fans\",\"Secures expansion cards more firmly inside the motherboard slots\",\"Allows additional RAM modules to be installed properly\"],\"question\":\"Question: A motherboard is installed directly on case metal. What is indicated here?\",\"questionType\":\"Situational\",\"correctAnswer\":0},{\"id\":1776121460657,\"skill\":\"Analytical Thinking\",\"options\":[\"To avoid transferring static electricity and oils to sensitive circuitry\",\"To prevent the component from overheating during installation\",\"To make installation faster and easier for technicians\",\"To reduce power consumption of the component\"],\"question\":\"Question: A student touches the circuitry of RAM and damages it. Their instructor reminded them that components must be handled by their edges only. Why is it so?\",\"questionType\":\"Situational\",\"correctAnswer\":0},{\"id\":1776121460658,\"skill\":\"Analytical Thinking\",\"options\":[\"To ensure cables reach the correct connectors inside the case\",\"To confirm that hardware parts are compatible with each other\",\"To verify that the operating system is already installed\",\"To check that the monitor supports the correct resolution\"],\"question\":\"Question: RAM does not fit the motherboard during installation. What first should have been verified?\",\"questionType\":\"Situational\",\"correctAnswer\":1},{\"id\":1776121460659,\"skill\":\"Critical Thinking\",\"options\":[\"It may create an electrical short circuit between motherboard components\",\"It prevents airflow from entering the computer case properly\",\"It blocks RAM slots and prevents modules from locking in place\",\"It interferes with the operating system loading process\"],\"question\":\"Question: A screw is left inside the case after assembly. What risk does this create?\",\"questionType\":\"Situational\",\"correctAnswer\":1},{\"id\":1776121460660,\"skill\":\"Critical Thinking\",\"options\":[\"To install application software immediately after hardware setup\",\"To verify that installed hardware powers on and is detected correctly\",\"To update firmware before the operating system loads\",\"To measure the processing speed of the CPU\"],\"question\":\"Question: After installing components, a technician powers on the system to verify detection. Why is this necessary?\",\"questionType\":\"Situational\",\"correctAnswer\":1},{\"id\":1776121460661,\"skill\":\"Critical Thinking\",\"options\":[\"Blocked airflow prevents heat from being removed from components\",\"Increased airflow causes components to receive too much voltage\",\"Reduced airflow prevents the operating system from loading properly\",\"Improper airflow disables communication between hardware devices\"],\"question\":\"Question: Cables block internal fans causing high temperatures. What is the main issue?\",\"questionType\":\"Situational\",\"correctAnswer\":2},{\"id\":1776121460662,\"skill\":\"Problem Solving\",\"options\":[\"PSU switch and cables\",\"RAM speed\",\"SSD capacity\",\"Mouse connection\"],\"question\":\"Question: A computer shows no signs of power. What should be checked first?\",\"questionType\":\"Situational\",\"correctAnswer\":0},{\"id\":1776121460663,\"skill\":\"Problem Solving\",\"options\":[\"Reseat RAM\",\"Replace CPU\",\"Install OS\",\"Remove PSU\"],\"question\":\"Question: The system boots but shows no display after RAM installation. What should be done?\",\"questionType\":\"Situational\",\"correctAnswer\":0},{\"id\":1776121460664,\"skill\":\"Problem Solving\",\"options\":[\"Check whether the CPU cooler is properly mounted and thermal paste applied\",\"Verify that the storage drive is detected in BIOS\",\"Reinstall the operating system to fix startup issues\",\"Replace the RAM modules with higher capacity ones\"],\"question\":\"Question: The computer shuts down after startup due to overheating. What should be checked?\",\"questionType\":\"Situational\",\"correctAnswer\":0},{\"id\":1776121460680,\"skill\":\"Memorization\",\"options\":[\"Anti-static wrist strap\",\"Screwdriver\",\"Cleaning cloth\",\"Cable ties\"],\"question\":\"Question: While preparing to install RAM and other internal components, a student wants to avoid electrostatic discharge that might damage sensitive parts. Which tool should the student use first? Anti-static wrist strap Screwdriver Cleaning cloth Cable ties\",\"questionType\":\"Situational\",\"correctAnswer\":0},{\"id\":1776121460681,\"skill\":\"Memorization\",\"options\":[\"By the circuitry\",\"By the sides or edges\",\"By the ports\",\"Anywhere as long as it is clean\"],\"question\":\"Question: A learner is about to install an expansion card into the motherboard. To avoid damaging the component, how should it be held while being installed? By the circuitry By the sides or edges By the ports Anywhere as long as it is clean\",\"questionType\":\"Situational\",\"correctAnswer\":1},{\"id\":1776121460682,\"skill\":\"Memorization\",\"options\":[\"Install software first\",\"Check all components and tools needed\",\"Power on the computer immediately\",\"Connect to the internet\"],\"question\":\"Question: Before beginning the assembly of a desktop computer, a technician wants to avoid delays and missing parts during the procedure. What should be done first? Install software first Check all components and tools needed Power on the computer immediately Connect to the internet\",\"questionType\":\"Situational\",\"correctAnswer\":1},{\"id\":1776121460683,\"skill\":\"Memorization\",\"options\":[\"Cable ties\",\"Thermal paste\",\"Alignment markers on the socket\",\"The motherboard manual\"],\"question\":\"Question: A student is preparing to place the processor into the motherboard socket but wants to avoid bending the pins or placing it incorrectly. What should be checked to ensure proper orientation? Cable ties Thermal paste Alignment markers on the socket The motherboard manual\",\"questionType\":\"Situational\",\"correctAnswer\":2},{\"id\":1776121460684,\"skill\":\"Memorization\",\"options\":[\"Increase CPU speed\",\"Enhance heat transfer between CPU and cooler\",\"Protect the CPU from electrical damage\",\"Prevent dust build-up\"],\"question\":\"Question: After assembling a new desktop PC, a technician notices that the CPU temperature is unusually high during normal operation. Upon inspection, it is found that the CPU cooler was installed without applying thermal paste between the CPU and the cooler base. What does the thermal paste mainly do? Increase CPU speed Enhance heat transfer between CPU and cooler Protect the CPU from electrical damage Prevent dust build-up\",\"questionType\":\"Situational\",\"correctAnswer\":1},{\"id\":1776121460685,\"skill\":\"Memorization\",\"options\":[\"Motherboard\",\"RAM\",\"Power Supply Unit (PSU)\",\"SSD\"],\"question\":\"Question: While using a desktop PC, it suddenly shuts down and fails to boot. Upon inspection, the technician notices that there are no lights or any signs of life from the system even though it is plugged into the outlet. Which of the following components is most likely causing the problem? Motherboard RAM Power Supply Unit (PSU) SSD\",\"questionType\":\"Situational\",\"correctAnswer\":2},{\"id\":1776121460686,\"skill\":\"Memorization\",\"options\":[\"To replace hardware\",\"To store electricity\",\"To provide instructions for hardware operation\",\"To physically connect components\"],\"question\":\"Question: A student asks why a computer cannot perform useful tasks with hardware alone. What explains the importance of software in the system? To replace hardware To store electricity To provide instructions for hardware operation To physically connect components\",\"questionType\":\"Situational\",\"correctAnswer\":2},{\"id\":1776121460687,\"skill\":\"Memorization\",\"options\":[\"RAM\",\"CPU\",\"Operating System\",\"Power Supply\"],\"question\":\"Question: A learner is sorting examples of hardware and software in computer servicing. Which of the following should be classified as software? RAM CPU Operating System Power Supply\",\"questionType\":\"Situational\",\"correctAnswer\":2},{\"id\":1776121460688,\"skill\":\"Memorization\",\"options\":[\"Software is optional\",\"Hardware works without software\",\"Software controls and manages hardware functionality\",\"Software only affects internet speed\"],\"question\":\"Question: A technician can identify internal parts correctly but struggles to understand why some devices still fail to work after installation. Why is knowledge of software also important in Computer Hardware Servicing? Software is optional Software controls and manages hardware functionality Software only affects internet speed\",\"questionType\":\"Situational\",\"correctAnswer\":2},{\"id\":1776121460689,\"skill\":\"Memorization\",\"options\":[\"To power hardware\",\"To connect hardware physically\",\"To enable communication between OS and hardware\",\"To store user files\"],\"question\":\"Question: After installing a printer, a student notices that the operating system cannot properly use the device until the correct supporting software is installed. What is the main function of that software? To power hardware To connect hardware physically To enable communication between OS and hardware To store user files\",\"questionType\":\"Situational\",\"correctAnswer\":2},{\"id\":1776121460690,\"skill\":\"Memorization\",\"options\":[\"The computer runs faster\",\"Hardware may not function properly\",\"Software installs automatically\",\"The system shuts down permanently\"],\"question\":\"Question: A graphics card is physically installed correctly, but the display settings are limited and the device is not performing as expected. What is the most likely effect of a missing or outdated driver? The computer runs faster Software installs automatically The system shuts down permanently\",\"questionType\":\"Situational\",\"correctAnswer\":3},{\"id\":1776121460691,\"skill\":\"Memorization\",\"options\":[\"Monitor\",\"Printer\",\"Graphics card\",\"All of the above\"],\"question\":\"Question: A learner is identifying which devices need driver software so they can communicate properly with the operating system. Which hardware requires a device driver? Monitor Printer Graphics card All of the above\",\"questionType\":\"Situational\",\"correctAnswer\":3},{\"id\":1776121460692,\"skill\":\"Memorization\",\"options\":[\"Hard drive\",\"RAM\",\"Non-volatile memory on the hardware\",\"Cloud storage\"],\"question\":\"Question: A technician explains that firmware remains available even when the computer is turned off, unlike temporary memory. Where is firmware typically stored? RAM Non-volatile memory on the hardware Cloud storage\",\"questionType\":\"Situational\",\"correctAnswer\":2},{\"id\":1776121460693,\"skill\":\"Memorization\",\"options\":[\"Microsoft Word\",\"Device driver\",\"BIOS/UEFI\",\"Web browser\"],\"question\":\"Question: A student is asked to identify software that is built into the hardware and helps initialize the system during startup. Which of the following is an example of firmware? Microsoft Word Device driver BIOS/UEFI Web browser\",\"questionType\":\"Situational\",\"correctAnswer\":0},{\"id\":1776121460694,\"skill\":\"Memorization\",\"options\":[\"Load games\",\"Initialize hardware components\",\"Open applications\",\"Connect to the internet\"],\"question\":\"Question: When a computer is powered on, a built-in program runs before the operating system loads. What is the main role of this firmware during startup? Load games Initialize hardware components Open applications Connect to the internet\",\"questionType\":\"Situational\",\"correctAnswer\":1},{\"id\":1776121460665,\"skill\":\"Memorization\",\"options\":[\"Phillips screwdriver\",\"Tweezers\",\"Anti-static wrist strap\",\"Cleaning brush\"],\"question\":\"Which tool is commonly used to install motherboard screws?\",\"questionType\":\"Easy\",\"correctAnswer\":0},{\"id\":1776121460666,\"skill\":\"Memorization\",\"options\":[\"Storing files\",\"Processing instructions\",\"Supplying power\",\"Cooling system\"],\"question\":\"What is the main function of the CPU?\",\"questionType\":\"Easy\",\"correctAnswer\":1},{\"id\":1776121460667,\"skill\":\"Memorization\",\"options\":[\"Power-On Self-Test\",\"Program Operating Setup Test\",\"Power Operating System Tool\",\"Primary Output System Test\"],\"question\":\"What does POST stand for?\",\"questionType\":\"Easy\",\"correctAnswer\":0},{\"id\":1776121460668,\"skill\":\"Technical Comprehension\",\"options\":[\"To increase RAM speed\",\"To improve airflow\",\"To add storage\",\"To reduce voltage\"],\"question\":\"Why are cable ties used inside a computer case?\",\"questionType\":\"Easy\",\"correctAnswer\":1},{\"id\":1776121460669,\"skill\":\"Technical Comprehension\",\"options\":[\"To fill microscopic gaps and improve heat transfer between CPU and cooler\",\"To electrically connect the CPU to the motherboard\",\"To secure the CPU physically inside the socket\",\"To increase the processor clock speed\"],\"question\":\"Why is thermal paste applied before installing the CPU cooler?\",\"questionType\":\"Easy\",\"correctAnswer\":0},{\"id\":1776121460670,\"skill\":\"Technical Comprehension\",\"options\":[\"Stores operating system and application files for later use\",\"Converts AC power from the outlet into usable DC power for components\",\"Controls communication between software and hardware devices\",\"Provides temporary working memory for running programs\"],\"question\":\"What is the role of the power supply unit?\",\"questionType\":\"Easy\",\"correctAnswer\":2},{\"id\":1776121460671,\"skill\":\"Analytical Thinking\",\"options\":[\"Prevents the motherboard from directly touching the case and causing short circuits\",\"Improves CPU cooling by raising the motherboard closer to fans\",\"Secures expansion cards more firmly inside the motherboard slots\",\"Allows additional RAM modules to be installed properly\"],\"question\":\"Why are motherboard standoffs installed before mounting the board?\",\"questionType\":\"Easy\",\"correctAnswer\":0},{\"id\":1776121460672,\"skill\":\"Analytical Thinking\",\"options\":[\"To avoid transferring static electricity and oils to sensitive circuitry\",\"To prevent the component from overheating during installation\",\"To make installation faster and easier for technicians\",\"To reduce power consumption of the component\"],\"question\":\"Why should components be handled by their edges?\",\"questionType\":\"Easy\",\"correctAnswer\":0},{\"id\":1776121460673,\"skill\":\"Analytical Thinking\",\"options\":[\"To ensure cables reach the correct connectors inside the case\",\"To confirm that hardware parts are compatible with each other\",\"To verify that the operating system is already installed\",\"To check that the monitor supports the correct resolution\"],\"question\":\"Why must compatibility be checked before assembly?\",\"questionType\":\"Easy\",\"correctAnswer\":1},{\"id\":1776121460674,\"skill\":\"Critical Thinking\",\"options\":[\"It may create an electrical short circuit between motherboard components\",\"It prevents airflow from entering the computer case properly\",\"It blocks RAM slots and prevents modules from locking in place\",\"It interferes with the operating system loading process\"],\"question\":\"Why should loose screws be removed before powering on?\",\"questionType\":\"Easy\",\"correctAnswer\":1},{\"id\":1776121460675,\"skill\":\"Critical Thinking\",\"options\":[\"To install application software immediately after hardware setup\",\"To verify that installed hardware powers on and is detected correctly\",\"To update firmware before the operating system loads\",\"To measure the processing speed of the CPU\"],\"question\":\"Why is boot testing performed after assembly?\",\"questionType\":\"Easy\",\"correctAnswer\":1},{\"id\":1776121460676,\"skill\":\"Critical Thinking\",\"options\":[\"Blocked airflow prevents heat from being removed from components\",\"Increased airflow causes components to receive too much voltage\",\"Reduced airflow prevents the operating system from loading properly\",\"Improper airflow disables communication between hardware devices\"],\"question\":\"Why should airflow be maintained inside the case?\",\"questionType\":\"Easy\",\"correctAnswer\":2},{\"id\":1776121460677,\"skill\":\"Problem Solving\",\"options\":[\"PSU switch and cables\",\"RAM speed\",\"SSD capacity\",\"Mouse connection\"],\"question\":\"What should be checked if the PC does not power on?\",\"questionType\":\"Easy\",\"correctAnswer\":0},{\"id\":1776121460678,\"skill\":\"Problem Solving\",\"options\":[\"Reseat RAM\",\"Replace CPU\",\"Install OS\",\"Remove PSU\"],\"question\":\"What is best to do if RAM is not detected?\",\"questionType\":\"Easy\",\"correctAnswer\":0},{\"id\":1776121460679,\"skill\":\"Problem Solving\",\"options\":[\"Check whether the CPU cooler is properly mounted and thermal paste applied\",\"Verify that the storage drive is detected in BIOS\",\"Reinstall the operating system to fix startup issues\",\"Replace the RAM modules with higher capacity ones\"],\"question\":\"What should be done if the CPU overheats immediately?\",\"questionType\":\"Easy\",\"correctAnswer\":0}]', '{\"hours\":0,\"minutes\":30}', 'Easy', NULL, '[]');
